--[[
	Anomaly Coop - shared tasks in Lua (gamedata\scripts\coop_tasks.script), work package W3c.
	SPEC R-7.2, R-7.5, R-7.6, R-7.8. Engine side: src\xrGame\coop\coop_story.cpp (WP4 + W3c).

	One task manager for the whole group: the HOST's Anomaly task_manager. The engine layer (coop_story)
	already mirrors the engine task list (texts, targets, states, PDA spots) to every client. This script
	does the same for the Lua side and routes every task decision to the host:

	Client (connected, in the host's world):
	  - task_manager:give_task / set_task_completed / set_task_failed / set_task_cancelled are sent to the
	    host (event coop_tq) and are NOT run locally, so on-give effects, on_complete, rewards and news run
	    exactly once, on the host (R-7.8, item 4 of W3c). The task vars a dialog prepared in this player's
	    pstor (fetch item, stash target, keys starting with the task id) travel with the give request.
	  - The client never evaluates tasks (no status functors, no completion checks): its task_manager holds
	    stubs mirrored from the host (stage, status, giver, task vars), so dialogs that read
	    task_info[id].stage / .status / .task_giver_id offer the same turn-in and cancel options as on the
	    host, for every task, including tasks the host gave after this client joined (R-7.2).
	    A dialog script that writes stub.stage or stub.forced_status sends that to the host as well.
	Host:
	  - Runs the requests with Anomaly's own task_manager and remembers who took and who turned in a task.
	    In the task callback the rewards go to the player who turned it in (R-7.6): money through the host
	    ledger (coop.money_grant onto the player's character, F2 T6; the client only gets the news line in
	    event coop_trw), items spawned by the host into that player's character, goodwill/faction effects
	    keyed to that character. Console coop_share_rewards: 1 splits money equally among the online players,
	    2 and 3 reward everyone who played, split or in full (coop_reward_group.script);
	    items still go to the finisher.
	  - Quest items count from any group member's inventory (R-7.5): fetch / stash status functors also count
	    the other players' characters, and removing the items takes them from whoever holds them (the player
	    who turned the task in first).
	  - Broadcasts the Lua task state (coop_tl, on change, scanned every 0.5 s), a digest list every 10 s
	    (coop_tl_list, in parts of 200 tasks) and the full state on request (coop_tl_req).
	  - Group task bookkeeping in the actor's pstor (keys "drx_sl_*": givers with outstanding tasks, the
	    current storyline task, ...) is the host's: mirrored to clients (coop_tv: the keys that changed, the whole set in
	    parts for a sync, never an empty set for a set that got long); a client's save_var of such a key goes to the host
	    (coop_tvd, giver counters as deltas, the rest as values), so a giver's "has a task for you" state is the same for
	    everybody.
	  - What a task's end does to the character of the player who turned it in (statistics, rank, reputation, faction)
	    runs on that player's machine (coop_trw k = stat, fx), whatever coop_share_rewards says. His machine answers
	    (coop_trw_ok); unanswered effects go out again on his next coop_tl_req.
	  - While the host's actor is dead the stock binder stops before task_manager:update and the actor_on_update callback:
	    a frame call (level.add_call) goes on with both, so the group's tasks do not stand still.
	  - Messages (docs\MESSAGES.md): the host's news_manager.send_task ("new" / "updated" / "complete" / "fail" / "reversed")
	    goes to every client as event coop_tn with the player who caused it. A client shows the stock line for its own
	    action and for an event nobody caused, "<nick> took / completed / failed / cancelled a task" (coop_quests_news)
	    for another player's; the host does the same for a client's action. The client's own send_task for a group
	    task is swallowed: the engine fires the actor's task callback for the copy it applies ("new"), a second line.
	API for scripts (any machine):
	  coop_tasks.party_has(section, count, min_condition) -> bool   (also coop.party_has when not set)
	  coop_tasks.party_count(section, min_condition)      -> number (multi-use items count their uses)
	    Host: the host's actor + the characters of all connected players. Client: own actor + the other
	    players' characters as mirrored here.
	  coop_tasks.party_object(section) -> item of that section held by another player's character, or nil
	  coop_tasks.party_holds_id(item_id, section) -> true if a player character holds that item
	  coop_tasks.recipient(task_id) -> peer that would get the reward now (host only)
	  coop_tasks.taker(task_id) -> peer that took the task (host only; 0 = the host)
	  coop_tasks.reward_peer() -> client peer that gets the effects being run now, or nil (host only)
	  coop_tasks.active_of(peer) -> the task that player has as his active one (host only, nil: none reported)
	  coop_tasks.run_as(peer, fn, ...) -> runs fn as a request of that player (host: gives / turn-ins
	    inside belong to that player)
	  coop_tasks.with_task_owner(task_id, fn, ...) -> runs fn with the companions it adds and the effects keyed to the actor going
	    to the player who took the task (host: items a status functor hands out, news)
	  coop_tasks.with_recipient(peer, fn, ...) -> the same for a given player (host)
	  coop_tasks.in_reward_scope() -> true while such effects belong to one player (host)
	  coop_tasks.party_take(section, amount) -> removes that many items from the group (host), count
	  coop_tasks.party_inventory_walker(real) -> an iterate_inventory over every player's character (host, for one call)
	  coop_tasks.taker_money(task_id) -> the ledger balance of the client who took the task (host; nil: the host took it)
	  coop_tasks.giving_npc() -> the giver of the client's give request being run (host; nil outside one)
	  coop_tasks.give_to_peer(peer, money, sections[, effect]) -> money / items for one player (host)
	  coop_tasks.news_actor(kind, task_id) -> peer, cancelled: the player whose action caused a task event ("new" |
	    "complete" | "fail"; 0 = the host, nil = nobody: a script, a timer). The one rule the task lines and any
	    other report of "who did it" (docs\MESSAGES.md, docs\ABSENT_REWARDS.md) share. Host only.
	  coop_tasks.money_line(peer, n) -> the "money received" line on that player's machine for money the host
	    changed outside a task reward (the achievement money of coop_quests_pda). Host only.
	  coop_tasks.set_local_task(task_id) -> a personal task (xrRazom xrr_local_tasks): given, checked
	    and finished on the machine that has it, never sent to the host or mirrored
	Called by the engine: coop_tasks.host_note(task_id, "taker"|"finisher", peer)  (coop_story.cpp requests)
--]]

local api = rawget(_G, "coop") -- engine namespace (nil on an exe without co-op)

local tostring, tonumber, type, pairs, ipairs, pcall, next = tostring, tonumber, type, pairs, ipairs, pcall, next
local string_format, string_char, table_concat, table_sort = string.format, string.char, table.concat, table.sort
local math_floor, math_max = math.floor, math.max

local EV_REQ = "coop_tq" -- client -> host: task operation
local EV_STATE = "coop_tl" -- host -> client(s): Lua state of one task
local EV_LIST = "coop_tl_list" -- host -> client(s): ids + digests of all tasks
local EV_SYNC = "coop_tl_req" -- client -> host: send me everything
local EV_REWARD = "coop_trw" -- host -> one client: money / news / personal effect for this player
local EV_NEWS = "coop_tn" -- host -> clients: a task line (new / updated / complete / fail / reversed) and who caused it
local EV_VARS = "coop_tv" -- host -> client(s): the group's shared task bookkeeping vars (whole set)
local EV_VAR = "coop_tvd" -- client -> host: this client's dialog changed one of them
local EV_ACK = "coop_trw_ok" -- client -> host: the effect of a coop_trw event ran here

-- Actor pstor keys that are task bookkeeping of the whole group (DRX storyline: givers with outstanding
-- tasks, current storyline task, ...). Written by the giving dialog on whichever machine, read by dialog
-- preconditions everywhere, cleared by on_complete on the host. Host-owned, mirrored, client writes routed.
-- Later ones: the escort tasks' target anomaly, its level and analyzed flag | Warfare escort's target smart (read by the
-- companion tasks' "arrived" test) | the counters of the Zaton b33 and Jupiter b200 dialog quests (several players count them)
local SHARED_PREFIXES = { "drx_sl_", "task_target_anomaly", "warfare_escort_", "zat_b33_", "jup_b200_" }
local COUNTER_PREFIX = "drx_sl_task_giver_" -- the only numbers that several players count at once: these travel as deltas

local SCAN_MS = 500
local LIST_MS = 10000
local SYNC_RETRY_MS = 10000
local PENDING_MS = 15000 -- provisional give / optimistic turn-in without an answer from the host
local MAX_STATE = 12000 -- characters of one state message (event payload limit is 16 KiB)
local LIST_IDS = 200 -- tasks in one part of the digest list
local DEAD_UPDATE_MS = 500 -- task_manager:update while the actor is dead (the stock binder: every frame)

local CONTAINERS = { "lead_box", "af_aam", "af_aac", "af_iam" } -- artefact containers (stock suffixes)
local FETCH_MIN_COND = { -- stock actor_has_fetch_item asks for a minimal condition on these two
	esc_2_12_stalker_nimble_task_1 = 0.9,
	jup_b220_trapper_task_3 = 0.9,
}
-- Effects that change the turning-in player's own character: run on that player's machine (R-3.4).
local FORWARD_EFFECTS = { drx_sl_change_factions = true }
-- game_statistics counters of a task's end. With rank and reputation they are the character's of the player who turned
-- the task in, for every coop_share_rewards.
local TASK_STATS = { tasks_completed = true, tasks_failed = true, tasks_cancelled = true }
local MONEY_FUNCTOR = "drx_sl_money_task_status" -- DRX money tasks (faction change): the finisher pays from his own money
local WAIT_FUNCTOR = "check_if_enough_time_passed" -- tm_yantar: Sakharov's helmet upgrade, a wait counted from the give

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Logging, roles
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function log(fmt, ...)
	local ok, line = pcall(string_format, fmt, ...)
	printf("[coop-tasks] %s", ok and line or tostring(fmt))
end

local stats = {
	req_out = 0, req_in = 0, refused = 0, state_out = 0, state_in = 0, lists = 0, syncs = 0,
	rewards_routed = 0, rewards_in = 0, party_moves = 0, party_releases = 0, stage_by_party = 0, errors = 0,
	news_out = 0, news_in = 0, news_swallowed = 0, news_limited = 0,
	-- host (TZ 6.4 #1 round 3, R2-B2): ends of tasks a player did not take that his own stock logic sent (check task_auto_end),
	-- counted without a line each; how many of them it refused
	auto_end = 0, auto_end_refused = 0,
}

local function report(what, err)
	stats.errors = stats.errors + 1
	if stats.errors <= 10 or stats.errors % 100 == 0 then
		log("! %s: %s", tostring(what), tostring(err))
	end
end

local function active()
	if not api then return false end
	local ok, v = pcall(api.is_active)
	return ok and v == true
end
local function world_active() return active() and coop_mode.decides_world() end
-- A map server mirrors the world's task state even while it leads its own level.
local function mirrors_tasks() return active() and not coop_mode.decides_world() end
-- A task of the stock manager is a luabind object, type() says "userdata"; a client's mirror stub is a Lua table.
function is_task(t)
	local kind = type(t)
	return kind == "userdata" or kind == "table"
end
local function client_live() return mirrors_tasks() and api.is_live() == true end

local function self_peer()
	local ok, v = pcall(api.self_id)
	return ok and tonumber(v) or 0
end

local function players()
	if not api then return {} end
	local ok, list = pcall(api.players)
	return ok and type(list) == "table" and list or {}
end

local function to_host_id(id)
	if not (api and api.to_host_id and type(id) == "number") then return id end
	return api.to_host_id(id) or id
end
local function to_local_id(id)
	if not (api and api.to_local_id and type(id) == "number") then return id end
	return api.to_local_id(id) or id
end

local function tmgr()
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	if not (mod and mod.get_task_manager) then return nil end
	local ok, tm = pcall(mod.get_task_manager)
	return ok and tm or nil
end

local function now() return time_global() end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Payloads: "k=v;k=v" of scalars, values may be one level of flat table ("t" + "k:v,k:v").
-- No code is ever loaded from the network.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function esc(s)
	return (tostring(s):gsub("[%%;=,:]", function(c) return string_format("%%%02X", c:byte()) end))
end
local function unesc(s)
	return (s:gsub("%%(%x%x)", function(h) return string_char(tonumber(h, 16)) end))
end

local function enc_scalar(v)
	local tv = type(v)
	if tv == "number" then
		if v ~= v or v == math.huge or v == -math.huge then return nil end
		return "n" .. string_format("%.17g", v)
	elseif tv == "boolean" then
		return v and "b1" or "b0"
	elseif tv == "string" then
		return "s" .. v
	end
	return nil
end

local function dec_scalar(v)
	local tag, body = v:sub(1, 1), v:sub(2)
	if tag == "n" then return tonumber(body) end
	if tag == "b" then return body == "1" end
	if tag == "s" then return body end
	return nil
end

-- flat table of scalars -> "k:v,..." (keys typed: "$" string, "#" number); nil if it holds anything else
local function enc_flat(t)
	local out = {}
	for k, v in pairs(t) do
		local ek
		if type(k) == "string" then
			ek = "$" .. k
		elseif type(k) == "number" then
			ek = "#" .. string_format("%.17g", k)
		end
		local ev = enc_scalar(v)
		if not (ek and ev) then return nil end
		out[#out + 1] = esc(ek) .. ":" .. esc(ev)
	end
	table_sort(out)
	return table_concat(out, ",")
end

local function dec_flat(s)
	local t = {}
	for pair in s:gmatch("[^,]+") do
		local k, v = pair:match("^([^:]*):(.*)$")
		if k then
			k = unesc(k)
			local tag, body = k:sub(1, 1), k:sub(2)
			local key = (tag == "#" and tonumber(body)) or (tag == "$" and body) or nil
			local val = dec_scalar(unesc(v))
			if key ~= nil and val ~= nil then t[key] = val end
		end
	end
	return t
end

local function pack(t, allow_tables)
	local out = {}
	for k, v in pairs(t) do
		if type(k) == "string" then
			local ev
			if type(v) == "table" then
				if allow_tables then
					local f = enc_flat(v)
					ev = f and ("t" .. f) or nil
				end
			else
				ev = enc_scalar(v)
			end
			if ev then out[#out + 1] = esc(k) .. "=" .. esc(ev) end
		end
	end
	table_sort(out)
	return table_concat(out, ";")
end

local function unpack_payload(s)
	local t = {}
	if type(s) ~= "string" then return t end
	for pair in s:gmatch("[^;]+") do
		local k, v = pair:match("^([^=]*)=(.*)$")
		if k then
			k, v = unesc(k), unesc(v)
			if v:sub(1, 1) == "t" then
				t[k] = dec_flat(v:sub(2))
			else
				local val = dec_scalar(v)
				if val ~= nil then t[k] = val end
			end
		end
	end
	return t
end

local function digest(s)
	local h = 5381
	for i = 1, #s do h = (h * 33 + s:byte(i)) % 4294967296 end
	return string_format("%08x", h)
end

-- Task vars a dialog or a task script keeps in the actor's pstor: keys that start with the task id
-- (fetch item "<id>_fetch", counts, stash/delivery tables saved under "<id>").
local function var_value_ok(v)
	local tv = type(v)
	if tv == "number" or tv == "string" or tv == "boolean" then return true end
	return tv == "table" and enc_flat(v) ~= nil
end

local function actor_pstor(create)
	local actor = db and db.actor
	local st = actor and db.storage and db.storage[actor:id()]
	if not st then return nil end
	if not st.pstor and create then st.pstor = {} end
	return st.pstor
end

-- The task's own vars: the key is the task id or starts with "<id>_" (not "<id>0", another task's).
local function is_task_key(k, id)
	if type(k) ~= "string" then return false end
	local n = #id
	if k:sub(1, n) ~= id then return false end
	return #k == n or k:sub(n + 1, n + 1) == "_"
end

local function task_vars(id)
	local out = {}
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	if not ps then return out end
	for k, v in pairs(ps) do
		if is_task_key(k, id) and var_value_ok(v) then out[k] = v end
	end
	return out
end

-- Personal tasks (xrRazom xrr_local_tasks): never routed to the host, never mirrored.
local local_tasks = {}
local function is_local(id) return type(id) == "string" and local_tasks[id] == true end

-- Needs the engine side too: coop_story must give/finish the engine task of such an id locally as well.
-- Without coop.story_local_task the request is refused (the engine would still send the task to the host).
function set_local_task(id)
	if type(id) ~= "string" or id == "" then return false end
	if not (api and api.story_local_task) then
		log("! personal task '%s' not set: the engine has no coop.story_local_task", id)
		return false
	end
	-- true = the engine keeps it local; false = refused (id over 256 chars, more than 1024 tasks)
	local ok, res = pcall(api.story_local_task, id)
	if ok and res then
		local_tasks[id] = true
		return true
	end
	log("! personal task '%s' refused by the engine (%s)", id, ok and "limit" or tostring(res))
	return false
end

function is_local_task(id) return is_local(id) end

-- Bounty targets are chosen while the dialog builds its text (setup_bounty_task) and kept in
-- axr_task_manager.bounties_by_id, not in the pstor: they travel with the task too.
local function bounties()
	local atm = rawget(_G, "axr_task_manager") or axr_task_manager
	local t = atm and atm.bounties_by_id
	return type(t) == "table" and t or nil
end

local function is_shared_key(k)
	if type(k) ~= "string" then return false end
	for _, p in ipairs(SHARED_PREFIXES) do
		if k:sub(1, #p) == p then return true end
	end
	return false
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Group inventories (R-7.5)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- A player on another level, as coop_quests_core answers for him. Not local: the chunk is at Lua's limit (test_engine_header).
function far_of(peer, id)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core") or coop_quests_core
	return qc and qc.far_body and qc.far_body(peer, id) or nil
end

-- Characters of the group on this machine: own actor first, then the other connected players, those on another level as far_body.
local function party()
	local out = {}
	-- the actor of a dedicated host or of a map server is nobody's character (owner 2026-11-13)
	if db and db.actor and coop_mode.actor_is_player() then out[1] = { obj = db.actor, peer = self_peer(), self = true } end
	if not active() then return out end
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if not p.is_self and p.avatar_id then
			local o = level.object_by_id(p.avatar_id) or far_of(p.id, p.avatar_id)
			if o then out[#out + 1] = { obj = o, peer = p.id } end
		end
	end
	return out
end

local function uses_of(sec)
	return IsItem and IsItem("multiuse", sec) or nil
end

-- Units of `sec` in one inventory (multi-use items count their uses, like utils_item.get_amount mode 1).
local function count_in(obj, sec, min_cond)
	local n = 0
	local multi = uses_of(sec)
	local ok, err = pcall(function()
		obj:iterate_inventory(function(_, item)
			if item:section() == sec and (not min_cond or (item:condition() or 1) >= min_cond) then
				n = n + (multi and item:get_remaining_uses() or 1)
			end
		end, nil)
	end)
	if not ok then report("count " .. tostring(sec), err) end
	return n
end

function party_count(section, min_cond)
	if type(section) ~= "string" or section == "" then return 0 end
	local n = 0
	for _, h in ipairs(party()) do n = n + count_in(h.obj, section, min_cond) end
	return n
end

function party_has(section, count, min_cond)
	return party_count(section, min_cond) >= (tonumber(count) or 1)
end

-- An item of `section` in another player's character on this machine (not the own actor), or nil.
function party_object(section)
	if type(section) ~= "string" or not active() then return nil end
	for _, h in ipairs(party()) do
		if not h.self then
			local ok, o = pcall(h.obj.object, h.obj, section)
			if ok and o then return o end
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- True if the item `item_id` (of `section`, if given) is held by a player character on this machine.
function party_holds_id(item_id, section)
	if type(item_id) ~= "number" then return false end
	local o = level.object_by_id(item_id)
	local pid
	if o then
		if section and o:section() ~= section then return false end
		local ok, p = pcall(o.parent, o)
		if not (ok and p) then return false end
		pid = p:id()
	else -- on another level: the record says who has it
		local se = alife_object(item_id)
		if not se or (section and se:section_name() ~= section) then return false end
		pid = se.parent_id
	end
	for _, h in ipairs(party()) do
		if h.obj:id() == pid then return true end
	end
	return false
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host state
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local host = {
	sent = {}, -- id -> last broadcast state string
	taker = {}, -- id -> peer that took the task (0 = host)
	finisher = {}, -- id -> peer that turned it in / cancelled it, until the task callback uses it
	taker_note = {}, -- id -> peer told by the engine (coop_story) right before the give
	given_by = {}, -- id -> peer whose action gave the task (0 = the host's dialog); nil: a script gave it (news only)
	news_seen = {}, -- "<kind> <id>" -> time of the last tn event sent (dedupe)
	news_count = 0,
	exec_peer = nil, -- peer whose request is being executed
	giver = nil, -- giver (npc id) of the client's give request being run
	take_asked = nil, -- id whose give ops.give runs now, coop_conditions_stock.may_take asked already
	next_scan = 0,
	next_list = 0,
	shared = {}, -- key -> encoded "k=v" pair of a shared var as the clients have it
	shared_long = {}, -- key -> true: its value does not fit a message, the clients keep what they have
	shared_gen = 0, -- number of the last full set
	list_gen = 0, -- number of the last digest list
	active = {}, -- peer -> the task that client has as his active one
	fx_seq = 0,
	fx_wait = {}, -- effect_key(peer) -> { { q, s }, ... } effects his machine has not answered yet
	char_of = {}, -- peer -> his character (it outlives the peer: a player who left, a reconnect)
	taker_char = {}, -- task -> persistent character; a reconnect can reuse the peer slot
	participants = {}, -- task -> character ids captured when the task is accepted
	rep_party = {}, -- task -> character ids in game at the accept, always (the session rule rep_share)
	failure_participants = {}, -- a missed deadline is a group consequence even with individual item rewards
	map_seen = {},
	fines = {}, -- character -> pending guide fine; never a reusable peer slot
	give_near = nil, -- object of the condlist effect that is giving a task
	next_dead_update = 0,
	talks = {}, -- round 4: peer -> the talks the host saw of a player who stepped a stage (host.talk_look)
	stage_used = {}, -- round 4: peer -> task -> talk key -> number of the talk a stage step used (host.stage_note)
	talk_starts = {}, -- round 5: peer -> how many talk locks the host granted him (host.watch_talks)
	held_at = {}, -- round 6: "<task>|<section>" -> when the group last held an item a dialog turn-in hands over (host.watch_held)
	far_talk = {}, -- round 6: peer -> { now = in a dialog now (his map server's word), at = when it last said so } (Server)
	gives_own = 0, -- round 6: gives with no offer of their giver whose vars the stock generator could have made (no line)
	given_at = {}, -- round 7: task -> { peer, at }: the last give of the task a client's request ran (host.dialog_turn_in, fresh)
	esc_own = {}, -- round 7: escort key -> { v }: the value the host's own logic (or a map server's) wrote last (host.esc_value)
	esc_ready = false, -- round 7: the escort keys a load brought are taken as the host's (host.esc_init)
}
local ctx = nil -- host: { task, rcpt (peer), share, owner } while a task callback hands out rewards
local raw_create = nil -- alife_create_item without the reward redirect

function reward_group()
	return _G.coop_reward_group
end

function news_mod() return _G.coop_quests_news end

-- Host: the setting coop_share_rewards. 0 the finisher, 1 money split online, 2 and 3 see coop_reward_group.script.
local EVERYONE_SHARED, EVERYONE_FULL = 2, 3

local function reward_mode()
	local ok, v = pcall(function() return get_console():get_integer("coop_share_rewards") end)
	return ok and tonumber(v) or 0
end

-- Host: the session rule rep_share (docs\GAME_SETTINGS.md). "everyone" (default): the personal effects of a completed
-- task (statistics, reputation, faction goodwill) go in full to every character in game at the accept or at the end;
-- "taker": only to the player who took / turned it in. Money and items stay with coop_share_rewards.
function rep_share_rule() -- not local: the chunk is at Lua's limit of 200 locals
	local ok, v = pcall(function()
		local core = _G.coop_economy_core
		return core and core.rule and core.rule("rep_share")
	end)
	return ok and v == "taker" and "taker" or "everyone"
end

-- Host: character of a peer (0 = the host's actor), the far_body of one on another level; nil: he left the game.
local function avatar_obj(peer)
	if peer == nil then return nil end
	if peer == 0 or peer == self_peer() then return db.actor end
	local ok, id = pcall(api.avatar_of, peer)
	return ok and id and (level.object_by_id(id) or far_of(peer, id)) or nil
end

function character_of(peer)
	if ctx and ctx.rcpt == peer and ctx.character ~= nil then return ctx.character end
	if peer == 0 then return 0 end
	local rg = reward_group()
	local id = rg and rg.id_of(peer)
	if id == nil and api.avatar_of then id = api.avatar_of(peer) end
	if id ~= nil then host.char_of[peer] = id end
	return id or host.char_of[peer]
end

function peer_for_character(id)
	if id == 0 then return 0 end
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do if p.avatar_id == id then return p.id end end
	local rg = reward_group()
	for _, m in ipairs(rg and rg.list() or {}) do if m.id == id then return m.peer end end
end

function recipient_body(peer)
	local id = character_of(peer)
	if id == 0 then
		local p = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_players")
		return p and p.own_actor and p.own_actor() or db.actor
	end
	if id == nil then return nil end
	local o = level.object_by_id(id)
	if o then return o end
	local qc = _G.coop_quests_core
	return qc and qc.body_for_character and qc.body_for_character(id)
end

function participant_ids()
	local ids, seen = {}, {}
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		local id = p.is_self and self_peer() == 0 and 0 or p.avatar_id
		if id ~= nil and not seen[id] then ids[#ids + 1], seen[id] = id, true end
	end
	return ids
end

function peer_in_session(peer) -- not local: the chunk is at Lua's limit of 200 with the engine's two (test_engine_header)
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if p.id == peer then return true end
	end
	return false
end

local function has_clients()
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if not p.is_self then return true end
	end
	return false
end

local function send(name, payload, target)
	local ok, sent = pcall(api.send_event, name, payload, target)
	return ok and sent == true
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host: a task's audience in a split-levels world (coop_srv_task_audience.script, docs\plans\2026-11-16-task-audience.md C). A task
-- without a record - every task outside a split-levels world or on an exe without the engine's filter - goes to everybody as
-- before. The helpers live in `host` and as module functions: the chunk is at Lua's limit of 200 locals (test_engine_header).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
function task_audience()
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	local m = qc and qc.part and qc.part("audience") -- a server's part (from coop_mode.when_srv), nil in the co-op
	return type(m) == "table" and m or nil
end

-- The record of task `id` ({ k, t = taker character, inn = { [character] = true }, ... }), or nil: everybody sees it.
function host.aud_rec(id)
	-- a reward handed out later (a delayed payout) keeps the record of its task's end: the task may be gone from the table
	if ctx and ctx.task == id and ctx.aud then return ctx.aud end
	local m = task_audience()
	return m and type(m.record) == "function" and m.record(id) or nil
end

-- May `peer` see task `id`? A map server's bridge (peer >= 0x100) always; peer 0 of a dedicated world server is nobody.
function host.aud_sees(id, peer)
	local rec = host.aud_rec(id)
	if not rec then return true end
	if type(peer) ~= "number" then return false end
	if peer >= 0x100 then return true end
	if peer == 0 and coop_mode.decides_world() and not coop_mode.seat_plays(0) then return false end
	local c = character_of(peer)
	return c ~= nil and rec.inn[c] == true
end

-- Optional delivery functions supplied by the server's task script.
function host.task_delivery()
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	return qc and qc.part and qc.part("task_delivery") or nil
end

function host.bridges()
	local delivery = host.task_delivery()
	return delivery and delivery.bridges() or {}
end

-- Every peer a message of this world goes to one by one: the other players and the bridges.
function host.aud_peers()
	local out = {}
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if not p.is_self and type(p.id) == "number" then out[#out + 1] = p.id end
	end
	for _, b in ipairs(host.bridges()) do out[#out + 1] = b end
	return out
end

-- A message about task `id`: to everybody (-1) without a record, else to each player who may see it and to every bridge.
function host.send_task(name, payload, id)
	if not host.aud_rec(id) then return send(name, payload, -1) end
	for _, p in ipairs(host.aud_peers()) do
		if host.aud_sees(id, p) then send(name, payload, p) end
	end
	return true
end

-- Characters `ids` of task `id` cut to its audience; none left: its taker. No record: `ids` as it is.
function host.aud_cut(id, ids)
	local rec = host.aud_rec(id)
	if not rec or ids == nil then return ids end
	local out = {}
	for _, c in ipairs(ids) do
		if rec.inn[c] then out[#out + 1] = c end
	end
	if #out == 0 and rec.t ~= nil then out[1] = rec.t end
	return out
end

-- The reward group (coop_reward_group.list) cut to the audience of task `id`; none left: the taker's member.
function host.aud_group(id, group)
	local rec = host.aud_rec(id)
	if not rec or group == nil then return group end
	local out = {}
	for _, m in ipairs(group) do
		if rec.inn[m.id] then out[#out + 1] = m end
	end
	if #out == 0 and rec.t ~= nil then
		local peer = peer_for_character(rec.t)
		out[1] = { id = rec.t, peer = peer, in_world = peer ~= nil }
	end
	return #out > 0 and out or group
end

-- The peer of the taker of task `id` (a recipient who is out is replaced by him).
function host.aud_taker_peer(id)
	local rec = host.aud_rec(id)
	local peer = rec and rec.t ~= nil and peer_for_character(rec.t) or nil
	return peer or host.taker[id] or 0
end

-- One walk of the pstor for a whole scan: the vars of every task of `info` (task id -> table of vars, see is_task_key; an id
-- may hold "_" itself, so every cut at a "_" is looked up) and the group's shared vars. With thousands of keys and dozens of
-- tasks a walk per task every 0.5 s is hundreds of thousands of string operations a second on the host.
local function scan_vars(info)
	local by_task, shared = {}, {}
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	if not ps then return by_task, shared end
	local function add(id, k, v)
		local t = by_task[id]
		if not t then
			t = {}
			by_task[id] = t
		end
		t[k] = v
	end
	for k, v in pairs(ps) do
		if type(k) == "string" and var_value_ok(v) then
			if is_shared_key(k) then shared[k] = v end
			if info[k] ~= nil then add(k, k, v) end
			local at = k:find("_", 2, true)
			while at do
				local id = k:sub(1, at - 1)
				if info[id] ~= nil then add(id, k, v) end
				at = k:find("_", at + 1, true)
			end
		end
	end
	return by_task, shared
end

local function task_record(id, tsk, vars)
	local rec = { i = id }
	local ok, err = pcall(function()
		if type(tsk.stage) == "number" then rec.st = tsk.stage end
		if type(tsk.status) == "string" then rec.s = tsk.status end
		if type(tsk.task_giver_id) == "number" then rec.g = tsk.task_giver_id end
	end)
	if not ok then report("task state " .. id, err) end
	local b = bounties()
	if b and type(b[id]) == "number" then rec.bt = b[id] end
	local v = pack(vars or task_vars(id), true)
	if v ~= "" then rec.v = v end
	local s = pack(rec)
	if #s > MAX_STATE then
		rec.v, rec.nv = nil, true -- too many vars: the state still goes out, the client keeps the vars it has
		s = pack(rec)
	end
	return s
end

-- Groups of entries { s = encoded pair } whose pairs fit one message each.
local function pair_groups(entries)
	table_sort(entries, function(a, b) return a.s < b.s end)
	local groups, cur, size = {}, {}, 0
	for _, e in ipairs(entries) do
		if size + #e.s + 1 > MAX_STATE and #cur > 0 then
			groups[#groups + 1] = cur
			cur, size = {}, 0
		end
		cur[#cur + 1] = e
		size = size + #e.s + 1
	end
	if #cur > 0 then groups[#groups + 1] = cur end
	return groups
end

local function group_text(group)
	local out = {}
	for i, e in ipairs(group) do out[i] = e.s end
	return table_concat(out, ";")
end

-- One value of a shared var, as a pair; nil and a log line if it does not fit a message (the clients keep what they have).
local function shared_pair(k, v)
	local s = pack({ [k] = v }, true)
	if #s <= MAX_STATE then
		host.shared_long[k] = nil
		return s
	end
	if not host.shared_long[k] then log("! shared task var '%s' too long (%d characters), not mirrored", k, #s) end
	host.shared_long[k] = true
	return nil
end

-- The keys that changed since the last scan go to every client ("-key" = removed). An unsent group is sent again by the
-- next scan: host.shared moves only with what went out.
local function host_shared_delta(vars)
	local entries = {}
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		local s = shared_pair(k, v)
		if s and host.shared[k] ~= s then entries[#entries + 1] = { k = k, s = s, v = s } end
	end
	for k in pairs(host.shared) do
		if vars[k] == nil then entries[#entries + 1] = { k = k, s = pack({ ["-" .. k] = true }) } end
	end
	for k in pairs(host.shared_long) do
		if vars[k] == nil then host.shared_long[k] = nil end
	end
	if #entries == 0 then return end
	for _, group in ipairs(pair_groups(entries)) do
		if send(EV_VARS, group_text(group), -1) then
			for _, e in ipairs(group) do host.shared[e.k] = e.v end
		end
	end
end

-- The whole set to one player, in parts. His keys that are not in it go with the last part, if every part came.
local function host_shared_full(peer)
	local entries = {}
	local _, vars = scan_vars({})
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		entries[#entries + 1] = { s = shared_pair(k, v) or pack({ ["+" .. k] = true }) } -- "+key": it stays as it is there
	end
	local groups = pair_groups(entries)
	if #groups == 0 then groups[1] = {} end
	host.shared_gen = host.shared_gen + 1
	for i, group in ipairs(groups) do
		local head = pack({ _f = host.shared_gen, _p = i, _n = #groups })
		send(EV_VARS, #group > 0 and (head .. ";" .. group_text(group)) or head, peer)
	end
end

local function host_scan(force)
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm or type(tm.task_info) ~= "table" then return end
	local by_task, shared = scan_vars(tm.task_info)
	local seen = {}
	for id, tsk in pairs(tm.task_info) do
		if type(id) == "string" and not is_local(id) then
			seen[id] = true
			local s = task_record(id, tsk, by_task[id] or {})
			if force or host.sent[id] ~= s then
				host.sent[id] = s
				host.send_task(EV_STATE, s, id) -- a task with an audience: only to it and the bridges
				stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
			end
		end
	end
	local m = task_audience()
	for id in pairs(host.sent) do
		if not seen[id] then
			host.sent[id] = nil
			host.send_task(EV_STATE, pack({ i = id, d = true }), id)
			stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
			if m and m.drop then m.drop(id) end -- the record goes with its task
		end
	end
	if m and m.prune then m.prune(tm.task_info) end
	host_shared_delta(shared)
end

-- The digest list in parts: "<list>/<part>/<parts>|id:digest,id:digest...". A client acts on a list that came whole.
local function host_list(target)
	local m = task_audience()
	if target == -1 and m and m.any and m.any() then
		-- tasks with an audience: a list per player without what he may not see, the bridges get them all
		for _, p in ipairs(host.aud_peers()) do host_list(p) end
		return
	end
	local list = {}
	for id, s in pairs(host.sent) do
		if target == -1 or host.aud_sees(id, target) then list[#list + 1] = esc(id) .. ":" .. digest(s) end
	end
	table_sort(list)
	local parts = math_max(1, math.ceil(#list / LIST_IDS))
	host.list_gen = host.list_gen + 1
	for i = 1, parts do
		local items = {}
		for j = (i - 1) * LIST_IDS + 1, math.min(i * LIST_IDS, #list) do items[#items + 1] = list[j] end
		send(EV_LIST, string_format("%d/%d/%d|%s", host.list_gen, i, parts, table_concat(items, ",")), target)
	end
	stats.lists = stats.lists + 1
end

-- The current state of one task (or its removal) to one player.
local function host_send_state(id, peer)
	local tm = tmgr()
	local tsk = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
	-- a player out of the task's audience learns nothing of it: for him it is not there
	local s = tsk ~= nil and host.aud_sees(id, peer) and task_record(id, tsk) or pack({ i = id, d = true })
	send(EV_STATE, s, peer)
	stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
end

local function host_full_sync(peer)
	host_scan(false) -- everybody gets pending changes first, so host.sent is current
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm then return end
	for id in pairs(host.sent) do
		if host.aud_sees(id, peer) then
			send(EV_STATE, host.sent[id], peer)
			stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
		end
	end
	host_shared_full(peer)
	host_list(peer) -- his list drops on his machine what he may no longer see
	stats.syncs = stats.syncs + 1
end

-- Host: the audience of some task changed for player `peer` (coop_srv_task_audience: a faction change): his Lua tasks and the
-- engine's task list again, as he may see them now.
function audience_resync(peer)
	if not world_active() or type(peer) ~= "number" or peer <= 0 or peer >= 0x100 then return false end
	host_full_sync(peer)
	local resend = api.story_resend_tasks
	if type(resend) == "function" then pcall(resend, peer) end
	return true
end

-- A client's dialog changed a shared bookkeeping var: counters as a delta (several players may count
-- at once), anything else as the new value.
local function host_on_var(payload, from)
	if not world_active() or type(from) ~= "number" or from == 0 then return end
	local t = unpack_payload(payload)
	local k = t.k
	local ps = actor_pstor(true)
	if not (is_shared_key(k) and ps) then return end
	-- split levels: a faction's chain is moved by the world alone (coop_srv_storyline), never by a client's write of its keys;
	-- coop_conditions_stock answers the stock's rule, a server's storyline puts its own over it
	local sl = rawget(_G, "coop_conditions_stock")
	if type(sl) == "table" and type(sl.client_may_write) == "function" and not sl.client_may_write(k) then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		return
	end
	-- round 4 (blocker 3 of the round 3 review): a fetch / target key of a running task he did not take (task_var_write)
	if not host.var_write_ok(k, from) then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		return
	end
	host.esc_init() -- round 7 (P-ESC): the escort keys are the host's before a client's write lands
	local esc = host.ESC_KEYS[k] and from >= 0x100 -- a map server's logic (the companion's): its write is the host's record
	-- round 7 (the round 6 review): a counter's delta is a whole number of a few steps (a giver's task count moves by one)
	if t.op == "add" and type(t.d) == "number" and t.d == math_floor(t.d) and t.d >= -1000 and t.d <= 1000 then
		ps[k] = (tonumber(ps[k]) or 0) + t.d
	elseif t.op == "set" and t.v ~= nil and var_value_ok(t.v) then
		ps[k] = t.v
	elseif t.op == "del" then
		ps[k] = nil
	else
		return
	end
	if esc then host.esc_own[k] = { v = ps[k] } end
	host_scan(false)
end

-- Who gets the reward of `id` now: the player who turned it in, else who took it, else the host.
function recipient(id)
	local r = host.finisher[id]
	if r == nil then r = host.taker[id] end
	return r or 0
end

function taker(id)
	return host.taker[id] or 0
end

-- Round 5: the character of the player who took task `id` (the host's save keeps it), nil: not known (coop_quests_trust counts the
-- items a task asked of the group per task and taker).
function taker_character(id)
	return host.taker_char[id]
end

-- The player who took task `id` is in the session and not in the world (on his loading screen): true. One who left is not waited for.
function taker_away(id)
	local t = host.taker[id]
	if not t or t == 0 then return false end
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if p.id == t then return p.avatar_id == nil end
	end
	return false
end

-- Host: the giver of the task a client's request is giving right now (the speaker an on_init effect asks the
-- host's dialog for; the host is not talking then), or nil.
function giving_npc()
	local id = host.giver
	return type(id) == "number" and level.object_by_id(id) or nil
end

-- Host: runs fn as if `peer` had asked for it through a task request (give_task inside = its task).
function run_as(peer, fn, ...)
	local prev = host.exec_peer
	host.exec_peer = tonumber(peer) ~= 0 and tonumber(peer) or nil
	local res = { pcall(fn, ...) }
	host.exec_peer = prev
	if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
	return unpack(res, 2)
end

-- coop_story.cpp: a client asked through the engine requests (TaskReqGive / TaskReqState).
function host_note(id, kind, peer)
	peer = tonumber(peer)
	if type(id) ~= "string" or not peer then return end
	if kind == "taker" then
		host.taker_note[id] = peer
	elseif kind == "finisher" and host.finisher[id] == nil then
		host.finisher[id] = peer
	end
end

local function task_known(id)
	local ini = task_manager and task_manager.task_ini
	local ok, yes = pcall(function() return ini and ini:section_exist(id) end)
	return ok and yes == true
end

local function host_talking()
	local ok, yes = pcall(function() return db.actor:is_talking() end)
	return ok and yes == true
end

local function engine_task_running(id)
	local ok, t = pcall(function() return db.actor:get_task(id, true) end)
	return ok and t ~= nil
end

-- Host: a player's balance on the host ledger (coop.money_of), nil when the ledger does not answer.
local function ledger_money(peer)
	local fn = api and api.money_of
	if type(fn) ~= "function" then return nil end
	local ok, n = pcall(fn, peer)
	return ok and type(n) == "number" and n or nil
end

-- Host: the ledger balance of the client who took a task (nil: the host took it, or the ledger does not answer). The
-- host's own status functors read db.actor:money(), the host's: a money task a client took needs HIS money.
function taker_money(id)
	local peer = host.taker[id]
	if not world_active() or not peer or peer == 0 then return nil end
	return ledger_money(peer)
end

-- True if `peer` cannot pay the DRX money task `id` (its price is the task var "<id>_fetch": round 6, the host's own record of
-- it, host.fact_of; a price that is only a client's word is not paid with nothing).
local function money_short(tm, id, peer)
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	if not (is_task(tsk) and tsk.status_functor == MONEY_FUNCTOR) then return false end
	local have = ledger_money(peer)
	local price, foreign = host.fact_of(id .. "_fetch", 0)
	if foreign then return have ~= nil end
	return have ~= nil and have < (tonumber(price) or 0)
end

-- Units of a fetch task's item the group holds (R-7.5: every player's character; an artefact asked for without a minimal
-- condition also counts in its containers), and how many the task asks for. nil when the task has no fetch item. Round 6: the
-- host's own record of the item and its count (host.fact_of), whatever a client's coop_tvd write left in the pstor; an item that is
-- only a client's word: 0 of 1 ("foreign" third value).
function host.fetch_units(task_id)
	local sec, foreign = host.fact_of(task_id .. "_fetch")
	if foreign then return 0, 1, true end
	if type(sec) ~= "string" then return nil end
	local need = tonumber((host.fact_of(task_id .. "_fetch_count"))) or 1
	local min_cond = FETCH_MIN_COND[task_id]
	local n = party_count(sec, min_cond)
	if not min_cond and sec:find("af_", 1, true) then
		for _, cont in ipairs(CONTAINERS) do n = n + party_count(sec .. "_" .. cont) end
	end
	return n, need
end

-- Why a client's turn-in of a task he hands something over for cannot go through, or nil. Whatever his dialog said, the host looks at
-- its own view of the group's characters (owner 2026-11-16: the parcel was with a player, the rest of the group went by word):
--   delivery_task (stock tasks_delivery): THIS task's parcel (var.item_1_id, of var.item_1_sec) is in a player's character;
--   actor_has_fetch_item (stock tasks_fetch): the group holds as many as the task asks for.
-- Money tasks: money_short. The take itself is the on_complete's (coop_quests_party: the parcel by its id).
function host.item_short(tm, id)
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	if not is_task(tsk) then return nil end
	local sf = tsk.status_functor
	if sf == "delivery_task" then
		-- the stock delivery functor saves the table again with item_1_id: the host's own write (host.fact_of)
		local var = host.fact_of(id)
		if type(var) ~= "table" or type(var.item_1_id) ~= "number" then return "the task has no parcel" end
		if not party_holds_id(var.item_1_id, var.item_1_sec) then return "nobody of the group holds its parcel" end
	elseif sf == "actor_has_fetch_item" then
		local n, need, foreign = host.fetch_units(id)
		if foreign then return "its fetch item is a client's word, not the host's" end
		if n and n < need then return string_format("the group holds %d of %d", n, need) end
	end
	return nil
end

-- The wait of a "check_if_enough_time_passed" task is counted from the give. Its giving dialog saves the time right after
-- give_task, in the pstor of the machine that talks: a client's, where the host never sees it (a CTime cannot travel) and
-- the wait would end at once. The host stamps the give itself (over a time an earlier give of the client left in the vars).
-- (G.A.M.M.A. sets the wait of the helmet upgrade to 0; the stock task waits two days.)
local function stamp_wait(id, tsk)
	if not is_task(tsk) or tsk.status_functor ~= WAIT_FUNCTOR then return end
	local save_time = rawget(_G, "save_ctime")
	if type(save_time) == "function" then save_time(db.actor, id, game.get_game_time()) end
end

-- Client request handlers (host). Return true when accepted; the state is then broadcast by the scan.
local ops = {}

-- The player a request of a map server's logic belongs to: who took the task, else a player of its level. It is no player itself.
function player_of_request(from, id)
	local delivery = host.task_delivery()
	return delivery and delivery.player_of_request(from, host.taker[id]) or from
end

-- Host: did player `from` talk to NPC `nid` a moment ago? The talk lock of a player on a map server's level is on that map server,
-- which reports it with his place (as coop_quests_missions talked_recently). An engine without the talk locks: yes.
function host.talk_facts(from)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if type(qc) == "table" and type(qc.is_far_peer) == "function" and qc.is_far_peer(from) == true then
		local facts = coop_mode.facts_of(from)
		-- The facade drops invalid ids. Only engines without a partner binding use the vague dialogue check.
		if facts and facts.partner == nil then
			local delivery = host.task_delivery()
			if delivery then
				local ok, available = pcall(delivery.has_talk_partner)
				if ok and available then facts.partner = false end
			end
		end
		return facts, true
	end
	return nil, false
end

function _spoke_to(from, nid)
	local facts, far = host.talk_facts(from)
	if far then
		if facts and facts.partner ~= nil then return host.far_with(from, facts.partner, nid) end
		-- Older engines report only that he holds a dialog lock. Keep the same 15 s window.
		return host.far_said(from, facts == nil or facts.talking ~= false)
	end
	local recent = api.talk_recent
	if type(recent) ~= "function" then return true end
	return recent(from, nid, 15000) == true
end

-- Round 6: player `from`'s map server says he is in a dialog now (`live`): noted; -> he was within the last 15 s.
function host.far_said(from, live)
	local ft = host.far_talk[from]
	if not ft then
		ft = { now = false, at = nil }
		host.far_talk[from] = ft
	end
	ft.now = live == true
	if ft.now then ft.at = now() end
	return ft.now or (ft.at ~= nil and now() - ft.at <= 15000)
end

-- S5: player `from` talks to NPC `with` now (false: to nobody), as his map server names him: noted with the time. -> he talked to
-- NPC `nid` now or in the last 15 s (the co-op's talk_recent window); nid 0 / nil: only noted, false. host.far_talk[from].with:
-- NPC -> when last named; older than 15 s is forgotten.
function host.far_with(from, with, nid)
	local ft = host.far_talk[from]
	if not ft then
		ft = { now = false, at = nil }
		host.far_talk[from] = ft
	end
	local t = now()
	ft.with = ft.with or {}
	for npc, at in pairs(ft.with) do
		if t - at > 15000 then ft.with[npc] = nil end
	end
	ft.now = with ~= false
	if with then ft.at, ft.with[with] = t, t end
	nid = tonumber(nid)
	if not nid or nid <= 0 then return false end
	return ft.with[nid] ~= nil
end

-- Round 6: the scan's look at the dialogs of the players on a map server's level (host.far_said keeps when each was last in one);
-- a player who left is forgotten.
function host.far_watch()
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if not (type(qc) == "table" and type(qc.is_far_peer) == "function") then return end
	local here = {}
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		here[p.id] = true
		local okf, far = pcall(qc.is_far_peer, p.id)
		if not p.is_self and okf and far == true then _spoke_to(p.id, 0) end
	end
	for peer in pairs(host.far_talk) do
		if not here[peer] then host.far_talk[peer] = nil end
	end
end

-- Host (round 3, R2-S3): true when _spoke_to's answer for player `from` names no partner. The talk of a player on a map server's
-- level is that server's word "he is in some dialog" (LevelBodyFacts.talking, one byte in coop_levels_wire.h). S5 (A-S5T): protocol
-- 33 also reports the NPC (LevelBodyFacts.partner), which can explicitly say he is talking to nobody.
function _talk_vague(from)
	local facts, far = host.talk_facts(from)
	return far and (facts == nil or facts.partner == nil)
end

function ops.give(tm, id, t, from)
	if tm.task_info[id] ~= nil and engine_task_running(id) then return false end
	-- split levels: a main story belongs to the faction that started it, and a player holds one change-faction task at a time
	-- (coop_conditions_stock.may_take, a server's storyline over it, is the world's side of the dialog gates of modxml_coop_storyline)
	local sl = rawget(_G, "coop_conditions_stock")
	if type(sl) == "table" and type(sl.may_take) == "function" and sl.may_take(id, from) == false then
		log("#%s may not take '%s': another faction's main story or a second change-faction task", tostring(from), id)
		return false
	end
	local got_vars = {}
	local vars = {}
	if type(t.v) == "string" then
		for k, v in pairs(unpack_payload(t.v)) do
			if is_task_key(k, id) and var_value_ok(v) then vars[k] = v end
		end
	end
	host.his_vars(id, vars)
	-- the bounty target his dialog chose: an object id (round 6: a number of no id is no target)
	local bt = tonumber(t.bt)
	if bt and not (bt > 0 and bt < 65535 and bt == math_floor(bt)) then bt = nil end
	-- round 4: the vars of the give the host runs are its facts (coop_quests_trust.note_own); round 5 (blocker 1 of the round 4
	-- review): as far as they are what the host offered him (host.give_offer, check task_give_offer); round 6: the bounty target
	-- too, only the offers of his giver, and with no offer, a pick the task's own generator can make (host.give_own)
	local own, put, gbt, drop = host.give_offer(id, from, vars, t, bt)
	for k, v in pairs(put) do
		host.give_vars, host.var_foreign = own[k] == true, own[k] ~= true
		save_var(db.actor, k, v)
		got_vars[k] = true
	end
	for k in pairs(drop) do
		host.give_vars, host.var_foreign = false, true
		save_var(db.actor, k, nil) -- no value of his there: none of this task's facts
	end
	host.give_vars, host.var_foreign = nil, nil
	local b = bounties()
	if b and gbt ~= nil then b[id] = gbt or nil end
	local giver = tonumber(t.g) -- host numbering == local numbering on the host
	host.taker[id] = from
	host.given_by[id] = from
	host.given_at[id] = { peer = from, at = now() }
	host.finisher[id] = nil
	host.giver = giver
	-- The NPC the player talks to is the speaker while the task starts: an on_init asks get_speaker() for him (setup_fetch_task of
	-- lttz_ll_medical_supplies died on nil: the quest audit, 2026-11-13). His word counts only if the host saw the talk.
	local sp = tonumber(t.sp)
	local npc = sp and sp ~= 0 and (db.storage[sp] and db.storage[sp].object or level.object_by_id(sp)) or nil
	if npc and not _spoke_to(from, sp) then npc = nil end
	local stock_speaker = rawget(_G, "get_speaker")
	if npc then _G.get_speaker = function() return npc end end
	host.take_asked = id -- may_take was asked above: the patched give_task does not ask again for this id
	local gave, gerr = pcall(tm.give_task, tm, id, giver)
	host.take_asked = nil
	if npc then _G.get_speaker = stock_speaker end
	host.giver = nil
	if not gave then
		-- The stock puts the task object into task_info BEFORE its give_task runs on_init and gives the task to the actor
		-- (CRandomTask:give_task). An on_init that died leaves the object behind: a task of the journal that is no task of the
		-- engine. It was sent to every player as given and never judged ("the KMB does not update", owner 2026-11-13; seen on
		-- the stand 2026-11-14 with the guards of coop_srv_quests_far taken out).
		if tm.task_info[id] ~= nil and not engine_task_running(id) then tm.task_info[id] = nil end
		error(gerr, 0)
	end
	local given = tm.task_info[id] ~= nil
	if given then
		local qo = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_offer")
		stamp_wait(id, tm.task_info[id])
		-- host-side parts of the offer the client's dialog prepared (pinned target squads, ...)
		if type(qo) == "table" and type(qo.host_after_give) == "function" then
			local ok, err = pcall(qo.host_after_give, id, from, giver, got_vars)
			if not ok then report("after give " .. id, err) end
		end
		-- his offers of this task are spent by the give, after host_after_give read the one he took (A-REV-E-2 F4)
		if type(qo) == "table" and type(qo.offer_given) == "function" then pcall(qo.offer_given, from, id) end
	end
	return given
end

local function finish(method)
	return function(tm, id, t, from)
		if tm.task_info[id] == nil or not engine_task_running(id) then return false end
		-- round 7: the facts the money and item checks read below: the live pstor in "log" (as build 56), the host's record in
		-- "refuse" (check task_var_write); a difference is its line (host.fact_line)
		if method == "set_task_completed" then host.fact_line(tm, id, from) end
		if method == "set_task_completed" and money_short(tm, id, from) then
			log("#%s cannot turn in '%s': not enough money", tostring(from), id)
			return false
		end
		local short = method == "set_task_completed" and host.item_short(tm, id) or nil
		if short then
			log("#%s cannot turn in '%s': %s", tostring(from), id, short)
			return false
		end
		-- round 5 (blocker 2 of the round 4 review): the host's own state of a task that is not about items (task_complete_state)
		if method == "set_task_completed" and not host.complete_state(tm, id, from, t) then return false end
		-- round 4 (S1 of the round 3 review): and the talk it is turned in (check task_complete_talk)
		if method == "set_task_completed" and not host.complete_talk(tm, id, t, from) then return false end
		if host.finisher[id] == nil then host.finisher[id] = from end
		tm[method](tm, id)
		return "pending" -- the task callback follows when the host checks its tasks
	end
end
ops.complete = finish("set_task_completed")
ops.fail = finish("set_task_failed")
ops.cancel = finish("set_task_cancelled")

function ops.stage(tm, id, t, from)
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	local st = tonumber(t.st)
	-- a stage is a byte of the task object; 255 is the repeat timeout the host itself sets
	if tsk == nil or not st or st < 0 or st >= 255 or st ~= math_floor(st) then return false end
	-- TZ 6.4 #1 round 2 (F2): a dialog moves a stage on, one step at a time (aysd: stage + 1); the host's status functors
	-- move it any way they like on the host itself, which is no request. A map server's (its level's logic, the facts are
	-- there): not judged here.
	-- Round 3 (R2-S2), round 4 (blocker 1 of the round 3 review): a step also needs a talk a moment ago, which the host saw, with
	-- the NPC the task points to now, and at most one step per talk (host.stage_talk). The same stage again changes nothing and
	-- needs none.
	local cur = tonumber(tsk.stage) or 0
	local bridge = (tonumber(host.req_from) or 0) >= 0x100
	local ok, why, talk = st == cur, "a stage goes only up, one step at a time", nil
	if st == cur + 1 and not bridge then ok, why, talk = host.stage_talk(id, tsk, from, t.sp) end
	-- round 6 (blocker 1 of the round 5 review): a step that reaches the task's stage_complete turns it in; the host takes it
	-- only where its own state says the objective is reached (host.done_here)
	if ok and st == cur + 1 and not bridge and st == host.stage_complete(id) then ok, why = host.done_here(tm, id, tsk) end
	if not bridge and not host.trust("task_stage", ok, "player %s (#%s), task %s: stage %d asked, the host's is %d: %s",
		host.nick(from), tostring(from), id, st, cur, tostring(why)) then
		return false
	end
	tsk.stage = st
	if talk then host.stage_note(id, from, talk) end
	return true
end

-- Round 3 (R2-S2), round 4 (blocker 1 of the round 3 review): may player `from` move task `id` (object tsk) one stage on in his
-- talk with NPC `sp` (host numbering)? -> ok, why not, and the talk the step uses ({ key, n }, for host.stage_note).
-- The honest steps are a dialog's: aysd (Ashot and Yar, the only stage write of a client in the scripts) moves +1 in a talk with
-- Ashot while the task points to Ashot's squad, and with Yar, its giver, while it points to Yar's. So:
--   - the NPC is the one the task points to now (the NPC, or a member of the squad); the giver counts only for a task without a
--     target (a task that points to its giver has him as the target); a task with neither takes only an NPC its own target
--     condlist names (host.condlist_names), else nobody. Where the task points now is its target functor's word (the host's own
--     look runs every 0.5-1 s: right after a step it still points to the last NPC); without one, the host's last look;
--   - the host saw the talk a moment ago (_spoke_to: its talk locks, 15 s);
--   - one step per talk: a talk a step used moves nothing more; a new step needs a new talk (host.talk_of).
-- Server: S5 (A-S5T), protocol 33: his map server names the NPC of his talk (LevelBodyFacts.partner, the part "talk"): judged as
-- above. An engine that does not name him says only "in some dialog" (_talk_vague): a step is then judged ok only for a task with
-- neither a giver nor a target, at an NPC its condlist names, one step per dialog.
function host.stage_talk(id, tsk, from, sp)
	sp = tonumber(sp)
	if not sp or sp <= 0 or sp >= 65535 or sp ~= math_floor(sp) then return false, "a step, and no talk named" end
	local okg, giver = pcall(function() return tonumber(tsk.task_giver_id) end)
	if not (okg and giver and giver > 0 and giver < 65535) then giver = nil end
	local target = host.target_now(id, tsk)
	if (giver ~= nil or target ~= nil) and _talk_vague(from) then
		return false, string_format("Server: his map server says only that he is in some dialog, not with whom (giver %s, target "
			.. "%s): a step of a task with a giver or a target is not judged ok there", tostring(giver), tostring(target))
	end
	if _spoke_to(from, sp) ~= true then return false, string_format("a step in a talk with NPC %d the host did not see", sp) end
	local fits, who
	if target ~= nil then
		fits, who = target == sp or host.squad_of(sp) == target, "where it points"
	elseif giver ~= nil then
		-- round 5 (S1): a member of the giver's squad is the giver (DRX gives with the squad's id)
		fits, who = host.is_giver(giver, sp), "its giver (it points nowhere)"
	else
		fits, who = host.condlist_names(tsk, sp), "an NPC its target condlist names (no giver, no target)"
	end
	if not fits then
		return false, string_format("a step in a talk with NPC %d, who is not %s; giver %s, target %s", sp, who, tostring(giver),
			tostring(target))
	end
	local talk = host.talk_of(from, sp)
	local used = talk and host.stage_used[from] and host.stage_used[from][id]
	if used and used[talk.key] == talk.n then
		return false, string_format("one step per talk: the talk with NPC %d moved this task a stage already", sp), talk
	end
	return true, nil, talk
end

-- Round 4 (S1 of the round 3 review): the Lua turn-in (ops.complete) checks money and items; may player `from` also turn task
-- `id` in, in the talk his request names (t.sp)? Check task_complete_talk, "log" first. A talk with the giver alone cannot be
-- asked for: the honest turn-ins are a dialog's with the giver (axr_task_manager.set_finished_task_complete, DRX's
-- drx_sl_set_finished_task_complete, z_gavrilenko_tasks_fix a second later, dialogs_yantar's psi helmet at Sakharov), with the
-- NPC the task points to (tasks_delivery complete_simulation_task: the parcel's receiver), or with an NPC of a task without a
-- giver (dialogs_lostzone's story tasks, tasks_defense barrier_defense_*_complete). So: the host saw a talk a moment ago
-- (_spoke_to) with the giver (round 5, S1: or a member of the giver's squad), with the NPC the task points to now (or a member of
-- its squad), or, for a task without a giver, with any NPC. Server: S5 (A-S5T), his map server names the NPC of his talk (the part
-- "talk"): judged the same; an engine that does not name him says only "in some dialog" (_talk_vague): that is enough. A map
-- server's turn-in is its level's logic: not judged.
function host.complete_talk(tm, id, t, from)
	if (tonumber(host.req_from) or 0) >= 0x100 then return true end
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	local sp = type(t) == "table" and tonumber(t.sp) or nil
	local ok, why = false, "no talk named"
	-- round 7 (the review of round 6): a turn-in outside any dialog (bind_heli.heli_die of a client's mirror of the helicopter, a
	-- client's condlist with xr_effects.set_task_completed) names no talk; it holds when the host's own check of the task says it is
	-- done (the host's own logic would complete it the same: only who turned it in differs)
	if not (sp and sp > 0) and host.still_running(tm, id) == nil then ok, why = true, nil end
	if sp and sp > 0 and sp < 65535 and sp == math_floor(sp) then
		local okg, giver = pcall(function() return tonumber(tsk.task_giver_id) end)
		if not (okg and giver and giver > 0 and giver < 65535) then giver = nil end
		if _spoke_to(from, sp) ~= true then
			why = string_format("the host did not see a talk with NPC %d", sp)
		elseif giver == nil or host.is_giver(giver, sp) or _talk_vague(from) or host.dialog_npc(id, sp) then
			-- round 6: or the NPC of the dialog that completes it (host.DIALOG_TURN_INS: Nimble for the owl's PDA, an escort's
			-- companion), who is neither its giver nor where it points
			ok = true
		else
			local target = host.target_now(id, tsk)
			ok = target ~= nil and (target == sp or host.squad_of(sp) == target)
			why = string_format("in a talk with NPC %d, who is neither its giver (%d) nor where it points (%s)", sp, giver,
				tostring(target))
		end
	end
	return host.trust("task_complete_talk", ok, "player %s (#%s) turned task %s in: %s", host.nick(from), tostring(from), id,
		tostring(why))
end

-- Round 5 (S1 of the round 4 review): is NPC `sp` task giver `giver` (an NPC's id or a squad's)? DRX gives with the squad's id
-- (dialogs.drx_sl_give_sl_task: giver_id = se_obj.group_id) and its stock turn-in takes any member of that squad
-- (axr_task_manager.get_first_finished_task): the NPC himself, or a member of the squad the giver is.
function host.is_giver(giver, sp)
	return giver ~= nil and sp ~= nil and (giver == sp or host.squad_of(sp) == giver)
end

-- Round 5 (blocker 2 of the round 4 review): the Lua turn-in (ops.complete) of a task whose objective is not about items asks the
-- host's own state of the task, as the engine path does (host.still_running). Check task_complete_state, "log" first. Item tasks
-- are judged by the money and item checks before it (a DRX money task, a delivery, a fetch task with its item: host.items_judged).
-- The honest Lua turn-ins of the others (traced in the stock and the G.A.M.M.A. scripts):
--   - the turn-in dialogs (axr_task_manager set_finished_task_complete through get_first_finished_task, DRX's
--     drx_sl_set_finished_task_complete / _cf_task_complete, z_gavrilenko_tasks_fix one second after the dialog opens) turn in a
--     task only at its stage_complete (the task ini, 254 without one); the client's stub has the host's stage;
--   - a status functor or a condlist ended it on the host (last_check_task, forced_status: host.still_running);
--   - a dialog completes one named task directly, its own precondition being the objective (host.DIALOG_TURN_INS).
-- Co-op: the host's task objects. Server: the world server's, whose status functors run over the far view. A map server's turn-in
-- is its level's logic: not judged.
-- Round 6 (blockers 1 and 6 of the round 5 review): a stage the client stepped to stage_complete is no objective (host.done_here for
-- a bounty), and a task of host.DIALOG_TURN_INS asks its own dialog's condition (host.dialog_turn_in), not any stage. `t`: the
-- request (the NPC of his talk, t.sp).
function host.complete_state(tm, id, from, t)
	if (tonumber(host.req_from) or 0) >= 0x100 then return true end
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	if not is_task(tsk) or host.items_judged(tsk, id) then return true end
	local ok, why = host.still_running(tm, id) == nil, nil
	local spec = host.DIALOG_TURN_INS[id]
	if not ok and type(spec) == "table" then
		ok, why = host.dialog_turn_in(id, tsk, from, type(t) == "table" and t.sp or nil, spec)
	elseif not ok then
		local need = host.stage_complete(id)
		local okst, stage = pcall(function() return tonumber(tsk.stage) end)
		stage = okst and stage or nil
		ok = stage ~= nil and stage == need
		why = string_format("its stage is %s, a turn-in asks for its stage_complete %s, and the host's own check says it is still "
			.. "running", tostring(stage), tostring(need))
		local okf, sf = pcall(function() return tsk.status_functor end)
		if ok and okf and sf == "bounty_task" then ok, why = host.done_here(tm, id, tsk) end
	end
	return host.trust("task_complete_state", ok, "player %s (#%s) turned task %s in: %s", host.nick(from), tostring(from), id,
		tostring(why))
end

-- Round 6 (blocker 1 of the round 5 review): does the host's own state of task `id` (object tsk) say its objective is reached?
-- -> ok, why not. A bounty (status functor bounty_task, stage_complete 1, the client's step 0 -> 1 at its living, maybe neutral
-- target): its target (axr_task_manager.bounties_by_id) is dead in this process's ALife. Co-op: the host's objects. Server: the
-- world server's records, which a map server's death report updates (coop_srv_quests_far on_death): a death it has not reported yet
-- reads as alive (the world server's own functor moves the stage a moment later). Any other task: the host's own check found it
-- done (host.still_running). The only honest stage write of a client (aysd, Ashot and Yar) never reaches stage_complete (254).
function host.done_here(tm, id, tsk)
	local okf, sf = pcall(function() return tsk.status_functor end)
	if okf and sf == "bounty_task" then
		local b = bounties()
		local target = b and tonumber(b[id])
		if not target then return false, "a bounty with no target the host knows" end
		local f = rawget(_G, "alife_object")
		local oks, se = pcall(function() return type(f) == "function" and f(target) or nil end)
		if not (oks and se) then return false, string_format("its target %d is no object here (the host's check fails it)", target) end
		local okl, alive = pcall(function() return se:alive() end)
		if okl and alive == false then return true, nil end
		return false, string_format("its target %d is alive here", target)
	end
	if host.still_running(tm, id) == nil then return true, nil end
	return false, "a step to its stage_complete, and the host's own check says it is still running"
end

-- Round 5: is task `id` (object tsk) one the money and item checks of ops.complete judge? A DRX money task, a delivery (its
-- parcel), a fetch task that has its item.
function host.items_judged(tsk, id)
	local okf, sf = pcall(function() return tsk.status_functor end)
	sf = okf and sf or nil
	if sf == MONEY_FUNCTOR or sf == "delivery_task" then return true end
	local sec, foreign = host.fact_of(id .. "_fetch")
	return sf == "actor_has_fetch_item" and (foreign or type(sec) == "string")
end

-- Round 5: the stage a turn-in asks of task `id`: its ini's stage_complete, 254 without one (axr_task_manager CFG_CACHE).
function host.stage_complete(id)
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	local ok, n = pcall(function() return mod.task_ini:r_float_ex(id, "stage_complete") end)
	return ok and tonumber(n) or 254
end

-- Round 5: the tasks a dialog completes directly with set_task_completed, its own precondition being the objective. Stock:
-- dialogs_escape (the owl's and the Clear Sky trader's escorts), dialogs_marsh, dialogs_darkvalley, dialogs_jupiter (the ecologists'
-- escorts), tasks_top_10; G.A.M.M.A. (merged corpus): dialogs_lostzone (the story tasks), dialogs_yantar (the psi helmet),
-- tasks_defense (the barrier), tasks_the_living_fire. tasks_delivery's is a delivery (an item task); tasks_mystery_of_the_swamps
-- completes from its status functor on the host.
-- Round 6 (blocker 6 of the round 5 review): what each dialog asks, as the host can see it (host.dialog_turn_in; the dialogs and
-- the task files read in the stock, the merged corpus and the stand's configs):
--   npc / squad  the talk is with that dialog's own NPC (story ids; a squad: any member), not the giver;
--   items        the group holds them (the task's on_complete takes them); recent: or held them in the last 15 s (the dialog
--                hands the item over in the same action that completes the task, and the release may reach the host first);
--   info         the world has that info portion (a phrase's has_info, the task's own condlist);
--   stage        the task's stage is at least that (its status functor's);
--   near         the turning-in player's character is within 50 m of that smart (the escort's destination: the dialog's
--                check_nearest_smart_dist_le 40, the warfare escort's smart when one is set), and no escort anomaly is pending;
--   loot         the companion squad's members (online here) looted at least that many (dialogs_darkvalley).
-- Server: the partner of his talk as his map server names it (S5, the part "talk"; an older engine: not reported, _talk_vague), the
-- rest is the world server's view (far bodies, its records).
host.DIALOG_TURN_INS = (function() -- (a function: the chunk has no room for more locals)
	local DLG_ISG = { npc = { "jup_depo_isg_leader" }, squad = { "jup_depo_isg_leader_squad" } }
	local DLG_OWL = { npc = { "esc_2_12_stalker_nimble" }, items = { "mar_base_owl_stalker_trader_task_1_pda" }, recent = true }
	local DLG_ECO1 = { squad = { "ecolog_companion_task_1" }, near = "mar_smart_terrain_base", escort = true }
	local DLG_ECO2 = { squad = { "ecolog_companion_task_2" }, near = "jup_b41", escort = true }
	local DLG_BANDIT = { squad = { "bandit_companion_task_1" }, loot = 9, escort = true }
	return {
	-- dialogs_lostzone_ll.xml living_legend_strelok_answers (has_info lttz_ll_crucible_task_done), at Strelok
	lttz_ll_answers = { npc = { "lost_stalker_strelok" }, info = "lttz_ll_crucible_task_done" },
	-- Hollow Boundaries: at the ISG leader (the tasks' target), each on_complete takes its items
	lttz_hb_task_1_2_recruit = { npc = DLG_ISG.npc, squad = DLG_ISG.squad, items = { "hb_isg_dushman_intel" } },
	lttz_hb_task_2_1_guarded_secrets = { stage = 2, items = { "jupiter_documents" } }, -- its dialog's NPC: not found (partly)
	lttz_hb_task_2_2_breakthrough = { npc = DLG_ISG.npc, squad = DLG_ISG.squad, items = { "main_story_6_jup_ug_documents" } },
	lttz_hb_task_3_8_handle_docs = { npc = DLG_ISG.npc, squad = DLG_ISG.squad, items = { "main_story_1_quest_case",
		"main_story_2_lab_x18_documents", "main_story_3_lab_x16_documents", "main_story_4_lab_x10_documents",
		"main_story_5_lab_x8_documents" } },
	lttz_hb_task_4_1_crossfire = { npc = DLG_ISG.npc, squad = DLG_ISG.squad, items = { "strelok_pendrive" } },
	-- dialogs_yantar.xml yan_stalker_sakharov_good_psi_helmet / _bad_psi_helmet: at Sakharov. Round 7 (P-PSI of the round 6 review):
	-- at its stage 2 (actor_has_good_psi_helmet_task_completed: the wait is over), or right after its give by the same player (the
	-- paid good helmet: G.A.M.M.A.'s phrase 122 runs take_money_good_psi_helmet, which gives it, and give_player_good_psi_helmet,
	-- which completes it, in one action)
	yan_stalker_sakharov_psi_helmet_upgrade = { npc = { "yan_stalker_sakharov" }, stage = 2, fresh = 15000 },
	-- tasks_defense: the turn-in is relayed to the host (coop_quests_missions); the task's own condlist_0 gives the info when
	-- all_attackers_dead holds. Round 7 (P-INFO of the round 6 review): the engine applies an info a client gives (coop_story
	-- InfoPortion), so the host also asks its own record of the attackers (tasks_defense all_attackers_dead)
	barrier_defense_monolith = { info = "barrier_defense_monolith_finished", attackers = true },
	barrier_defense_zombie = { info = "barrier_defense_zombie_finished", attackers = true },
	-- dialogs_new_tasks_addon.xml yan_stalker_sakharov_the_living_fire_5 (has_info the_living_fire_prometheus_killed_gg)
	bar_informator_mlr_task_the_living_fire = { npc = { "yan_stalker_sakharov" }, info = "the_living_fire_prometheus_killed_gg" },
	-- dialogs_bar.xml top_10_task_finish_dialog: tasks_top_10.almost_done_task_top_10 (stage 10)
	snitch_top_10_task = { stage = 10 },
	-- dialogs_escape.xml esc_2_12_stalker_nimble_about_quest: the owl's PDA to Nimble
	mar_base_owl_stalker_trader_task_1 = DLG_OWL, sim_default_csky_trader_task_1 = DLG_OWL,
	-- dialogs_marsh.xml ecolog_companion_task_1_dialog, dialogs_jupiter.xml ecolog_companion_task_2_dialog: the ecologist escorted
	mar_base_owl_stalker_trader_task_3 = DLG_ECO1, sim_default_csky_trader_task_3 = DLG_ECO1,
	sim_default_ecolog_trader_task_1 = DLG_ECO2, yan_stalker_sakharov_task_2 = DLG_ECO2, jup_b6_scientist_tech_task_1 = DLG_ECO2,
	-- dialogs_darkvalley.xml: the bandit escort's loot
	sim_default_bandit_trader_task_4 = DLG_BANDIT, val_smart_terrain_7_4_bandit_trader_stalker_task_3 = DLG_BANDIT,
}
end)()

-- Round 6: the object id of story id `sid` here, nil: none.
function host.story_id(sid)
	local f = rawget(_G, "get_story_object_id")
	local ok, id = pcall(function() return type(f) == "function" and f(sid) or nil end)
	return ok and tonumber(id) or nil
end

-- Round 6: is NPC `sp` (host numbering) the NPC of the dialog that completes task `id` (spec of host.DIALOG_TURN_INS), or a member
-- of its squad? false when the spec names none.
function host.dialog_npc(id, sp, spec)
	spec = spec or host.DIALOG_TURN_INS[id]
	sp = tonumber(sp)
	if type(spec) ~= "table" or not sp then return false end
	for _, sid in ipairs(spec.npc or {}) do
		if host.story_id(sid) == sp then return true end
	end
	local squad = (spec.squad and spec.squad[1]) and host.squad_of(sp) or nil
	for _, sid in ipairs(spec.squad or {}) do
		local sq = host.story_id(sid)
		if sq and squad == sq then return true end
	end
	return false
end

-- Round 6: the character of player `peer` as this process sees it (Co-op: the host's object; Server: his far body), nil: none.
function host.body_of(peer)
	local c = character_of(peer)
	return c and (level.object_by_id(c) or far_of(peer, c)) or nil
end

-- Round 6 (blocker 6 of the round 5 review): may player `from` turn in task `id` (object tsk), which its own dialog completes
-- directly, in his talk with NPC `sp`? spec: host.DIALOG_TURN_INS[id]. -> ok, why not. What cannot be read here is no refusal.
function host.dialog_turn_in(id, tsk, from, sp, spec)
	sp = tonumber(sp)
	if (spec.npc or spec.squad) and not _talk_vague(from) then
		if not (sp and sp > 0 and sp < 65535 and sp == math_floor(sp) and _spoke_to(from, sp) == true) then
			return false, "its dialog's NPC: the host saw no talk"
		end
		if not host.dialog_npc(id, sp, spec) then
			return false, string_format("a talk with NPC %d, who is not the NPC of the dialog that completes it", sp)
		end
	end
	if spec.stage then
		local okst, stage = pcall(function() return tonumber(tsk.stage) end)
		-- round 7: fresh = a dialog that gives the task and completes it in one action (his give a moment ago)
		local g = host.given_at[id]
		local fresh = spec.fresh and type(g) == "table" and g.peer == from and now() - g.at <= spec.fresh
		if okst and stage and stage < spec.stage and not fresh then
			return false, string_format("its stage is %d, its dialog asks for %d", stage, spec.stage)
		end
	end
	if spec.info then
		local f = rawget(_G, "has_alife_info")
		local ok, yes = pcall(f, spec.info)
		if ok and yes == false then return false, string_format("the world has no info %s", spec.info) end
	end
	if spec.attackers then
		-- round 7 (P-INFO): the host's own record of the attackers it spawned (MDATA of tasks_defense); not readable here: no verdict
		local xc = rawget(_G, "xr_conditions")
		local f = type(xc) == "table" and xc.all_attackers_dead
		local ok, dead = false, nil
		if type(f) == "function" then ok, dead = pcall(f, nil, nil, { id }) end
		if ok and dead == false then return false, "its attackers are not all dead here (tasks_defense all_attackers_dead)" end
	end
	if spec.escort then
		local why = host.escort_gone(spec)
		if why then return false, why end
	end
	for _, sec in ipairs(spec.items or {}) do
		if party_count(sec) < 1 and not (spec.recent and now() - (host.held_at[id .. "|" .. sec] or -1e9) <= 15000) then
			return false, string_format("nobody of the group holds %s", sec)
		end
	end
	if spec.near then
		-- round 7 (P-ESC of the round 6 review): the escort's end and its pending anomaly as the host's own logic wrote them
		-- (host.esc_value), never a client's coop_tvd write; the warfare smart only in warfare (only setup_companion_task writes it,
		-- under _G.WARFARE); a smart not known here is no end (a made-up name failed the distance and passed)
		local warfare = rawget(_G, "WARFARE") and true or false
		local smart = warfare and host.esc_value("warfare_escort_task_smart") or spec.near
		local sb = rawget(_G, "SIMBOARD")
		local smarts = type(sb) == "table" and type(sb.smarts_by_names) == "table" and sb.smarts_by_names or nil
		local s = smarts and smarts[smart] or nil
		if smarts and s == nil then return false, string_format("its end %s is no smart known here", tostring(smart)) end
		local body = host.body_of(from)
		local okp, d = pcall(function() return body:position():distance_to(s.position) end)
		if okp and type(d) == "number" and d > 50 then
			return false, string_format("his character is %.0f m from %s, the escort's end", d, tostring(smart))
		end
		-- xr_conditions.has_task_target_anomaly, over the host's record
		local pending
		if warfare then
			pending = host.esc_value("task_target_anomaly_analyzed") == "not_analyzed"
		else
			pending = host.esc_value("task_target_anomaly") ~= nil
		end
		if pending then return false, "an anomaly of the escort is still to be analyzed" end
	end
	if spec.loot then
		local n, seen = 0, false
		local f = rawget(_G, "get_story_squad")
		pcall(function()
			local squad = f(spec.squad[1])
			for k in squad:squad_members() do
				local st = db.storage[k.id]
				if st and st.object then
					seen = true
					n = n + (tonumber(load_var(st.object, "s_loot_count")) or 0)
				end
			end
		end)
		if seen and n < spec.loot then
			return false, string_format("the companions looted %d of %d", n, spec.loot)
		end
	end
	return true, nil
end

-- Round 7 (P-ESC of the round 6 review): the keys the escorts' end reads (dialogs_marsh / dialogs_jupiter / dialogs_darkvalley:
-- warfare_escort_task_smart; xr_conditions.has_task_target_anomaly: task_target_anomaly, in warfare task_target_anomaly_analyzed).
-- They carry shared prefixes ("warfare_escort_", "task_target_anomaly"): a client's coop_tvd writes them into the host's pstor, and
-- no check judged them. Their honest writers are the host's own logic (axr_companions.setup_companion_task,
-- xr_effects.setup_task_target_anomaly / reset_task_target_anomaly / reset_warfare_escort_task: on_init, on_complete, the companion's
-- logic, beh_companion) and, in a server, that logic on a map server (its coop_tvd, a peer >= 0x100). The host keeps the value those
-- wrote last (host.var_own, host_on_var); the values a load brought are taken as its own before the first client write lands.
host.ESC_KEYS = { warfare_escort_task_smart = true, task_target_anomaly = true, task_target_anomaly_analyzed = true }

function host.esc_init()
	if host.esc_ready or not db.actor then return end
	host.esc_ready = true
	for k in pairs(host.ESC_KEYS) do
		if host.esc_own[k] == nil then host.esc_own[k] = { v = load_var(db.actor, k) } end
	end
end

-- Round 7: escort key `k` as the host's own logic wrote it last (nil: nothing).
function host.esc_value(k)
	host.esc_init()
	local r = host.esc_own[k]
	return r and r.v
end

-- Round 7 (P-ESC): an escort (spec.escort) is turned in with its companions: their squad (its story id) has a living member in
-- this process's ALife (Co-op: the host's; Server: the world server's records, which a map server's death report updates). Server:
-- the talk with a member is not reported there, so this is the only check of the companions; where they stand is not (the world
-- server's record of an NPC on a map server's level is no position to judge by). -> why not, nil: ok or not readable here.
function host.escort_gone(spec)
	local f = rawget(_G, "get_story_squad")
	local sid = spec.squad and spec.squad[1]
	if type(f) ~= "function" or not sid then return nil end
	local oks, squad = pcall(f, sid)
	if not oks then return nil end
	if squad == nil then return string_format("the escort's companions (%s) are gone here", sid) end
	local seen, alive = 0, 0
	pcall(function()
		for k in squad:squad_members() do
			seen = seen + 1
			local se = alife_object(k.id)
			local okl, al = pcall(function() return se:alive() end)
			if se and (not okl or al ~= false) then alive = alive + 1 end
		end
	end)
	if seen > 0 and alive == 0 then return string_format("the escort's companions (%s) are dead here", sid) end
	return nil
end

-- Round 6: the scan notes when the group held an item a running dialog turn-in asks for (spec.recent), for the 15 s after.
function host.watch_held()
	local tm = tmgr()
	local info = tm and tm.task_info
	if type(info) ~= "table" then return end
	for id, spec in pairs(host.DIALOG_TURN_INS) do
		if spec.recent and info[id] ~= nil then
			for _, sec in ipairs(spec.items or {}) do
				if party_count(sec) > 0 then host.held_at[id .. "|" .. sec] = now() end
			end
		end
	end
end

-- Round 4: the squad of NPC `sp` (its ALife record's group_id), nil: none known.
function host.squad_of(sp)
	local f = rawget(_G, "alife_object")
	local oks, se = pcall(function() return type(f) == "function" and f(sp) or nil end)
	local okq, squad = pcall(function() return oks and se and se.group_id or nil end)
	return okq and tonumber(squad) or nil
end

-- Round 4: does the target condlist of task object tsk (its ini line "target", what the stock target_condlist reads) name NPC
-- `sp` or his squad in any branch? Its sections are story ids (get_story_object_id).
function host.condlist_names(tsk, sp)
	local okt, text = pcall(function() return tsk.target end)
	local f = rawget(_G, "get_story_object_id")
	if not (okt and type(text) == "string" and type(f) == "function") then return false end
	local squad = host.squad_of(sp)
	text = text:gsub("%b{}", " "):gsub("%%[^%%]*%%", " ")
	for name in text:gmatch("[^,%s]+") do
		local ok, oid = pcall(f, name)
		oid = ok and tonumber(oid) or nil
		if oid and (oid == sp or oid == squad) then return true end
	end
	return false
end

-- Round 4: the talks the host saw, to tell one talk of a player from the next. Co-op: the talk lock he holds (coop.talk_lock_of),
-- a new lock is a new talk. Server: his map server's word "in some dialog" (_spoke_to), a new dialog is a new talk (key "?").
-- host.talks[peer] = { held = what he holds now (false: nothing), n = the last number, of = key -> number of his last talk }.
-- Numbers are kept only for the keys a step used (host.talk_of); a talk the looks never saw gets one at the step that names
-- it. Looked at by the scan (host.talk_watch) and at each step. nil: no talk facts here (an engine without the talk locks).
function host.talk_look(from)
	local facts, far = host.talk_facts(from)
	local cur = facts and facts.partner
	if cur ~= nil then
		-- S5 (A-S5T): the NPC his map server names, as the co-op's talk lock; a new NPC is a new talk
		host.far_with(from, cur, 0)
	elseif far then
		local live = facts == nil or facts.talking ~= false
		host.far_said(from, live)
		cur = live and "?" or false
	else
		local f = api and api.talk_lock_of
		if type(f) ~= "function" then return nil end
		local ok, npc = pcall(f, from)
		cur = ok and tonumber(npc) or false
	end
	local t = host.talks[from]
	local starts = host.talk_starts[from] or 0
	if not t then
		t = { held = false, n = 0, of = {}, starts = starts }
		host.talks[from] = t
	end
	-- round 5 (S5 of the round 4 review): a lock the host granted him since the last look is a new talk, also with the NPC he
	-- held then (a dialog closed and opened again between two looks of the scan)
	local fresh = starts ~= t.starts
	t.starts = starts
	if cur and (cur ~= t.held or fresh) and t.of[cur] ~= nil then
		t.n = t.n + 1
		t.of[cur] = t.n
	end
	t.held = cur
	return t
end

-- Round 5 (S5 of the round 4 review): the talks the host grants. The engine asks coop_npc_meet.talk_verdict before it grants a
-- client's talk lock (coop_dialog.cpp host_try_lock, B8; it exposes no start time of a lock): an answer that is not false grants
-- the lock now. A lock he asks for again while he holds it is no new talk (a client that only repeats the request); a dialog
-- closed and opened again with the same NPC between two looks of the scan is. Counted in host.talk_starts, read by
-- host.talk_look. Installed by the scan (host.talk_watch): coop_npc_meet is loaded at the game's start (its on_game_start).
function host.watch_talks()
	local m = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_meet")
	if not (type(m) == "table" and type(m.talk_verdict) == "function") or rawget(m, "_coop_talk_starts") then return end
	local verdict = m.talk_verdict
	rawset(m, "_coop_talk_starts", true)
	m.talk_verdict = function(npc, who, ...)
		local yes, why = verdict(npc, who, ...)
		if yes ~= false then pcall(host.talk_started, npc, who) end
		return yes, why
	end
end

-- Round 5: the host grants a talk lock of NPC `npc` to the player whose character is `who` (host objects).
function host.talk_started(npc, who)
	local peer = peer_for_character(who:id())
	if type(peer) ~= "number" or peer == 0 then return end
	local f = api and api.talk_lock_of
	if type(f) == "function" and tonumber(f(peer)) == npc:id() then return end -- he holds it already: no new talk
	host.talk_starts[peer] = (host.talk_starts[peer] or 0) + 1
end

-- Review A-REV-E-2 finding 5: the process that leads player `peer`'s map granted him a new talk lock of NPC `npc` (host numbering;
-- coop_srv_tasks hears it from his map server's bridge). The talk a step used with that NPC is over: the next step with him is a step
-- of a new talk. The map server's body reports (LevelBodyFacts.partner, about one a second) miss a dialog closed and opened again
-- between two of them; this word does not. A talk no step used yet needs nothing: the step that names it numbers it (host.talk_of).
function far_talk_new(peer, npc)
	if not (type(peer) == "number" and peer >= 1 and peer <= 0xffff and peer == math_floor(peer)) then return end
	if not (type(npc) == "number" and npc >= 1 and npc <= 65534 and npc == math_floor(npc)) then return end
	local t = host.talks[peer]
	if not t then return end
	for _, key in ipairs({ npc, "?" }) do -- "?": an engine that says only "in some dialog" (_talk_vague)
		if t.of[key] ~= nil then
			t.n = t.n + 1
			t.of[key] = t.n
		end
	end
end

-- Round 4: the talk of player `from` with NPC `sp` that a step names now: { key, n }, nil: no talk facts here.
function host.talk_of(from, sp)
	local t = host.talk_look(from)
	if not t then return nil end
	local key = _talk_vague(from) and "?" or sp
	if t.of[key] == nil then
		t.n = t.n + 1
		t.of[key] = t.n
	end
	return { key = key, n = t.of[key] }
end

-- Round 4: step of task `id` by player `from` used talk { key, n }.
function host.stage_note(id, from, talk)
	local mine = host.stage_used[from]
	if not mine then
		mine = {}
		host.stage_used[from] = mine
	end
	local used = mine[id] or {}
	mine[id] = used
	used[talk.key] = talk.n
end

-- Round 4: the scan's look at the talks of the players who stepped a stage (host.talk_look); a player who left is forgotten with
-- his steps (his peer slot may come back as another player), a task that is gone with its steps.
function host.talk_watch()
	host.watch_talks() -- round 5 (S5): the talks the host grants
	host.far_watch() -- round 6 (S2): when the players of a map server's level were last in a dialog
	host.watch_held() -- round 6 (blocker 6): when the group last held what a dialog turn-in hands over
	if next(host.talks) == nil and next(host.stage_used) == nil and next(host.talk_starts) == nil then return end
	local here = {}
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do here[p.id] = true end
	for peer in pairs(host.talk_starts) do
		if not here[peer] then host.talk_starts[peer] = nil end
	end
	local tm = tmgr()
	for peer, mine in pairs(host.stage_used) do
		for id in pairs(mine) do
			if not (tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id] ~= nil) then mine[id] = nil end
		end
		if not here[peer] or next(mine) == nil then host.stage_used[peer] = nil end
	end
	for peer in pairs(host.talks) do
		if here[peer] and host.stage_used[peer] then host.talk_look(peer) else host.talks[peer] = nil end
	end
end

-- Round 3 (R2-S2): where task `id` points now (an object id: an NPC, a squad, a place), nil: nowhere.
function host.target_now(id, tsk)
	local tf = rawget(_G, "task_functor")
	local okf, name = pcall(function() return tsk.target_functor end)
	local f = okf and type(tf) == "table" and type(name) == "string" and tf[name]
	if type(f) == "function" then
		local ok, t = pcall(function() return f(id, "target", tsk.target, tsk) end)
		if ok then return tonumber(t) end
	end
	local okc, cur = pcall(function() return tsk.current_target end)
	return okc and tonumber(cur) or nil
end

-- A client's active task (C8): check_level below brings the guide marker of his task.
function ops.active(tm, id, t, from)
	host.active[from] = not t.off and id or nil
	return "pending"
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host: checks of a client's word (TZ 6.4 #1, owner 2026-11-18), verdicts through coop_trust. In "log" (build 57) a failed
-- check is logged and the request goes on exactly as before. Functions of `host`, not locals: the chunk is at 200 locals.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- coop_trust.pass(name, ok, fmt, ...); no coop_trust: through.
function host.trust(name, ok, fmt, ...)
	local okm, t = pcall(function() return coop_trust end)
	if not (okm and type(t) == "table" and type(t.pass) == "function") then return true end
	local good, res = pcall(t.pass, name, ok, fmt, ...)
	return not good or res ~= false
end

-- coop_trust's setting of check `name` ("log" | "refuse" | "off"); no coop_trust: "log".
function host.trust_mode(name)
	local okm, t = pcall(function() return coop_trust end)
	if not (okm and type(t) == "table" and type(t.mode_of) == "function") then return "log" end
	local good, mode = pcall(t.mode_of, name)
	return good and (mode == "refuse" or mode == "off") and mode or "log"
end

-- Round 7 (P-SEC of the round 6 review): an object id a client's request names: a whole number 1..65534 (an engine object id; 65535
-- is the engine's "none"), else nil. Infinities, NaN, fractions and negative numbers never reach level.object_by_id or alife_object.
function host.obj_id(x)
	x = tonumber(x)
	if x and x >= 1 and x <= 65534 and x == math_floor(x) then return x end
	return nil
end

function host.nick(peer)
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if p.id == peer then return tostring(p.nick or "?") end
	end
	return peer == 0 and "host" or "?"
end

-- Round 4 (blocker 3 of the round 3 review): this process's own save_var of key `k` of its actor's pstor (every machine: only
-- the deciding one asks). coop_quests_trust keeps the values that are its own: the checks read a quest fact only with one of
-- them. A client's coop_tvd write is no save_var here (host_on_var writes the pstor itself).
function host.var_own(k, v)
	if host.making and type(k) == "string" then host.making[k] = { v = v } end -- round 6: host.give_own's own generation
	if host.ESC_KEYS[k] then host.esc_own[k] = { v = v } end -- round 7: the escort's end (host.esc_value)
	if host.var_quiet then return end
	local qt = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_trust")
	if type(qt) ~= "table" or type(qt.note_own) ~= "function" then return end
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	pcall(qt.note_own, k, v, ps and ps[k], host.give_vars == true, host.var_foreign == true)
end

-- Round 5: do two task vars hold the same value? Compared as the payload codec writes them (numbers to their last bit, a flat
-- table by its sorted pairs).
function host.same_var(a, b)
	return pack({ x = a }, true) == pack({ x = b }, true)
end

-- Round 6: a task fact a client's coop_tvd wrote into the host's pstor before the give (DRX's dialog writes its drx_sl_ keys there
-- at once; a running task is judged by task_var_write, one not given yet is not) is his word as much as the give's vars: added to
-- `vars` where the give does not carry the key and the host has no value of its own there (coop_quests_trust.recorded).
function host.his_vars(id, vars)
	local qt = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_trust")
	if type(qt) ~= "table" or type(qt.record_of) ~= "function" or type(qt.is_fact) ~= "function" then return end
	for k, v in pairs(task_vars(id)) do
		if vars[k] == nil then
			local ok, mine = pcall(qt.record_of, k) -- round 7: the record itself, whatever check task_var_write's mode
			local okf, fact = pcall(qt.is_fact, k, v)
			if ok and mine == nil and okf and fact == true then vars[k] = v end
		end
	end
end

-- Round 5 (blocker 1 of the round 4 review): the vars of player `from`'s give of task `id` (vars: his pstor's, his dialog prepared
-- them) count as the host's own facts (coop_quests_trust note_own) only where they are what the host offered him. The host keeps
-- its offers per player, task and NPC (coop_quests_offer offers_of: the host of a co-op, the world server of a server). Round 6:
--   - only the offers of his giver t.g count (S3 of the round 5 review: or an NPC of the giver's squad; a give with no giver: any).
--     The PDA board's row and a dialog both show the offer of the NPC that then gives the task;
--   - judged: every var an offer of his giver has, and the bounty target t.bt against the one the offer named (blocker 2); a fact
--     var none of them has (a fetch, its count, a target: coop_quests_trust is_fact) is a leftover of an older offer in his pstor
--     (put_vars never deletes one): out of the judgement, not written (S4);
--   - no offer of his giver: host.give_own.
-- Check task_give_offer: a judged var differs: "log" writes his vars as before, as facts; "refuse" writes the newest offer's
-- values instead (a var it has not: nothing), the host's own facts.
-- A map server's give is its level's logic: its vars are the host's. -> own (var -> true: what is written is a fact), put (var ->
-- value to write), the bounty target to keep (nil: none named, false: none), drop (var -> true: delete it, no fact of his there)
function host.give_offer(id, from, vars, t, bt)
	local own, put, drop = {}, {}, {}
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do own[k], put[k] = true, v end
	if (tonumber(host.req_from) or 0) >= 0x100 then return own, put, bt, drop end
	t = type(t) == "table" and t or {}
	local qo, qt = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_offer"), rawget(_G, "coop_quests_trust")
	local giver = tonumber(t.g)
	local oko, offers, meta = pcall(function() return qo.offers_of(from, id) end)
	local mine = {}
	for i, o in ipairs(oko and type(offers) == "table" and offers or {}) do
		local m = type(meta) == "table" and type(meta[i]) == "table" and meta[i] or {}
		if giver == nil or host.is_giver(giver, tonumber(m.npc)) then mine[#mine + 1] = { vars = o, bt = tonumber(m.bt) } end
	end
	if #mine == 0 then return host.give_own(id, from, vars, t, bt, own, put, drop) end
	local judged, seen = {}, {}
	for _, o in ipairs(mine) do
		for k in pairs(o.vars) do
			if not seen[k] and is_task_key(k, id) then
				seen[k] = true
				judged[#judged + 1] = k
			end
		end
	end
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		local okf, fact = pcall(function() return qt.is_fact(k, v) end)
		if not seen[k] and okf and fact == true then put[k], own[k], drop[k] = nil, nil, true end
	end
	local bt_judged = bt ~= nil
	for _, o in ipairs(mine) do if o.bt ~= nil then bt_judged = true end end
	if #judged == 0 and not bt_judged then return own, put, bt, drop end
	table_sort(judged)
	local ok, why = false, nil
	for i, o in ipairs(mine) do
		local bad = nil
		for _, k in ipairs(judged) do
			if not host.same_var(vars[k], o.vars[k]) then bad = bad or k end
		end
		if not bad and bt_judged and bt ~= o.bt then bad = "bt" end
		if not bad then
			ok = true
			break
		end
		if i == 1 and bad == "bt" then
			why = string_format("his bounty target is %s, the host's offer named %s", tostring(bt), tostring(o.bt))
		elseif i == 1 then
			why = string_format("his %s is %s, the host offered %s", bad, host.var_text(vars[bad]), host.var_text(o.vars[bad]))
		end
	end
	if not ok and host.own_fits(id, vars, bt, drop, judged, bt_judged, mine[1]) then
		ok = true
		host.gives_own = host.gives_own + 1
	end
	if host.trust("task_give_offer", ok, "player %s (#%s) took task %s from NPC %s: %s", host.nick(from), tostring(from), id,
		tostring(giver), tostring(why)) then
		return own, put, bt, drop
	end
	local o = mine[1]
	for _, k in ipairs(judged) do
		own[k], put[k], drop[k] = o.vars[k] ~= nil or nil, o.vars[k], o.vars[k] == nil or nil
	end
	return own, put, o.bt or false, drop
end

-- Round 7 (P-S3b of the round 6 review): his give differs from every offer of his giver t.g, yet his machine may have made the pick
-- itself: his dialog ran before the host's answer came, or after an empty list over the far view while the host kept an older offer
-- of that NPC. A pick the task's own generator can make (coop_quests_offer.own_pick) then holds, as on a give with no offer: a client
-- that never asks for an offer is judged so anyway, so an offer bounds nothing beyond it. Every key where his give differs from the
-- newest offer `o` (and the bounty target, where it differs) must be one the generator makes ("fetch" / "job"); the leftovers the
-- caller drops are left out. -> true: no line, counted as a give of no offer.
function host.own_fits(id, vars, bt, drop, judged, bt_judged, o)
	local qo = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_offer")
	if type(qo) ~= "table" or type(qo.own_pick) ~= "function" or type(o) ~= "table" then return false end
	local his = {}
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		if not drop[k] then his[k] = v end
	end
	local okp, ok, _, parts = pcall(qo.own_pick, id, his, bt)
	if not (okp and ok == true and type(parts) == "table") then return false end
	for _, k in ipairs(judged) do
		if not host.same_var(vars[k], o.vars[k]) and parts[k] ~= "fetch" and parts[k] ~= "job" then return false end
	end
	return not (bt_judged and bt ~= o.bt and parts.bt == nil)
end

-- Round 6 (blockers 2, 4 and 5 of the round 5 review): a give with no offer of its giver. His machine made the vars itself: DRX's
-- storyline, mechanic and change-faction dialogs (the host never offers them), an offer the host refused or that expired, an
-- empty list over the far view (Server). The stock picks at random, so the host judges whether the task's own generator can make
-- his pick (coop_quests_offer.own_pick: the fetch lists, a bounty's factions and its living target). Check task_give_offer:
--   - a pick it can make: his vars as the host's facts, no line (counted: coop_status "gives of no offer");
--   - one it cannot make, or a generator not known here: "log" writes his vars as before, as facts, with a line; "refuse" has the
--     host make its own (coop_quests_offer.host_make: the task's fetch_func / on_job_descr with the NPC of his talk, checked
--     against the giver, else the giver) and writes those, the host's facts. The task's state carries them to his machine, which
--     uses them (its journal shows the host's pick, which may differ from what his dialog said). Nothing made (no NPC of the give
--     here, the generator failed): a pick it cannot make is not written; a generator not known here keeps his vars (no knowledge
--     is no refusal).
function host.give_own(id, from, vars, t, bt, own, put, drop)
	local qo = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_offer")
	if type(qo) ~= "table" or type(qo.own_pick) ~= "function" then return own, put, bt, drop end
	local okp, ok, why, judged, want = pcall(qo.own_pick, id, vars, bt)
	if not okp or type(judged) ~= "table" or next(judged) == nil then return own, put, bt, drop end
	-- round 7 (the review of round 6): a fact key the task's on_init writes itself ("init": a DRX money task's price his pstor keeps
	-- from the last run) is out of the judgement: written as before, as his word, never as the host's fact (its on_init writes the
	-- host's own right after the give)
	for k, part in pairs(judged) do
		if part == "init" then own[k] = nil end
	end
	if ok == true then
		host.gives_own = host.gives_own + 1
		return own, put, bt, drop
	end
	if host.trust("task_give_offer", false, "player %s (#%s) took task %s from NPC %s with no offer of the host: %s",
		host.nick(from), tostring(from), id, tostring(t.g), tostring(why)) then
		return own, put, bt, drop
	end
	want = type(want) == "table" and want or {}
	if want.no_bt then bt = false end
	for k, part in pairs(judged) do
		if part == "none" then put[k], own[k], drop[k] = nil, nil, true end -- a fact no generator of the task makes
	end
	if not (want.fetch or want.job) then return own, put, bt, drop end
	host.making = {} -- what the host's own generation writes (host.var_own)
	local okm, made = pcall(qo.host_make, id, host.give_npc(from, t), tonumber(t.g), want)
	local wrote = host.making
	host.making = nil
	-- only the part of the generation that his pick fails is the host's (a fetch, a bounty)
	if not (okm and type(made) == "table") then
		if ok == nil then return own, put, bt, drop end
		for k, part in pairs(judged) do
			if k ~= "bt" and want[part] then put[k], own[k], drop[k] = nil, nil, true end
		end
		-- P-STALE (F2 round 7 review): no bounty target when the host's own run is a bounty's ("job"): not his (`want.job and false
		-- or bt` was always bt), not the last run's (false clears it, ops.give)
		if want.job then return own, put, false, drop end
		return own, put, bt, drop
	end
	for k, part in pairs(judged) do
		if k ~= "bt" and want[part] then put[k], own[k], drop[k] = nil, nil, true end
	end
	for k, w in pairs(wrote) do
		if is_task_key(k, id) then own[k], put[k], drop[k] = w.v ~= nil or nil, w.v, w.v == nil or nil end
	end
	-- round 7 (the review of round 6): his dialog said another item or target; the host's own pick goes to his machine with the
	-- task's state, and its lines ("needs: X", the bounty's target) to him now, so his dialog and journal agree
	if type(qo.tell_made) == "function" then pcall(qo.tell_made, from, id, made) end
	if want.job then return own, put, made.bounty or false, drop end
	return own, put, bt, drop
end

-- Round 6: the NPC whose talk a give names (t.sp), when the host saw that talk and he is the giver t.g or a member of its squad
-- (or the task has no giver); nil otherwise (coop_quests_offer.host_make then takes the giver).
function host.give_npc(from, t)
	local sp, giver = tonumber(t.sp), tonumber(t.g)
	if not (sp and sp > 0 and sp < 65535 and sp == math_floor(sp)) or _spoke_to(from, sp) ~= true then return nil end
	if giver ~= nil and not host.is_giver(giver, sp) then return nil end
	return sp
end

-- Round 5: a task var for the log line ("a table" for a table).
function host.var_text(v)
	if type(v) == "table" then return "a table" end
	return v == nil and "nothing" or tostring(v)
end

-- Round 4 (blocker 3 of the round 3 review): may client `from` write shared key `k` through coop_tvd? The quest facts the host
-- holds are taken first (coop_quests_trust.facts_ready), so the write cannot become one of them. A fetch / target key of a
-- running task ("<id>", "<id>_fetch", "<id>_fetch_count", "<id>_target_id") written by a client is check task_var_write. Round 6
-- (blocker 3 of the round 5 review): by its taker too (his rewrite of his own DRX fetch or money task's price decided the turn-in).
-- No honest writer writes one of a running task: the stock writes them in the offer, before the give (tasks_fetch fetch_func,
-- tasks_delivery on_job_descr: the host's offer, else the stock local generation on the client, whose drx_sl_ keys come here
-- then; a running task is offered to nobody), on_init, on_complete and the status functors run on the host. "log": written as
-- before; the turn-in reads the host's own record of the key anyway (host.fact_of).
function host.var_write_ok(k, from)
	local qt = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_trust")
	if type(qt) == "table" and type(qt.facts_ready) == "function" then pcall(qt.facts_ready) end
	local tm = tmgr()
	local info = tm and tm.task_info
	if type(info) ~= "table" or type(k) ~= "string" then return true end
	local id = nil
	for _, suffix in ipairs({ "_fetch_count", "_fetch", "_target_id", "" }) do
		local cand = k
		if suffix ~= "" then cand = #k > #suffix and k:sub(-#suffix) == suffix and k:sub(1, -#suffix - 1) or nil end
		local tsk = cand and info[cand]
		local okr, over = pcall(function() return tsk.stage == 255 or tsk.status == "completed" or tsk.status == "fail" end)
		if is_task(tsk) and okr and not over then
			id = cand
			break
		end
	end
	if not id then return true end
	local mine, want = host.is_taker(id, from)
	return host.trust("task_var_write", false, "player %s (#%s) wrote %s of running task %s through a shared var (%s); taker %s",
		host.nick(from), tostring(from), k, id, mine and "his own task" or "another player's task", host.taker_text(id, want))
end

-- Round 6 (blocker 3 of the round 5 review): the value of task fact `key` a turn-in is judged by: the host's own record of it
-- (coop_quests_trust.recorded: what it wrote itself last), not what a client's coop_tvd write left in the live pstor since.
-- -> value (default when none), foreign: true when the live pstor holds a value the host has no record of as its own (a
-- client's word). No record at all (a key no check names, a save from before round 4): the live pstor, as before.
-- Round 7 (the review of round 6: this refused in every mode, "log" too, with no line): recorded answers only where check
-- task_var_write is "refuse". "log" / "off": the live pstor, exactly as build 56 (money_short, host.item_short, the readiness of a
-- fetch task); host.fact_line writes the line at the turn-in when the record differs.
function host.fact_of(key, default)
	local qt = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_trust")
	local live = load_var(db.actor, key)
	local ok, v, known = pcall(function() return qt.recorded(key) end)
	if not (ok and known) then
		if live == nil then return default, false end
		return live, false
	end
	if v == nil then return default, live ~= nil end
	return v, false
end

-- Round 7: a turn-in of task `id` by player `who` is judged by its facts (money_short, host.item_short: a DRX money task's price, a
-- fetch task's item and count, a delivery's parcel). Does the live pstor hold what the host recorded (coop_quests_trust.record_of)?
-- It differs after a client's coop_tvd write "log" let through (his own running task's fact too) and where the host has no record of
-- the value (no_fact: a give whose var it did not take, a fact key missing from its save's list). Check task_var_write: "log" writes
-- the line and the turn-in reads the live pstor as build 56 did; "refuse" writes it and the turn-in reads the host's record
-- (host.fact_of). A map server's turn-in is its level's logic: not judged.
function host.fact_line(tm, id, who)
	if (tonumber(host.req_from) or 0) >= 0x100 then return end
	local qt = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_trust")
	if type(qt) ~= "table" or type(qt.record_of) ~= "function" then return end
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	local okf, sf = pcall(function() return tsk.status_functor end)
	sf = okf and sf or nil
	local keys = nil
	if sf == MONEY_FUNCTOR then
		keys = { id .. "_fetch" }
	elseif sf == "actor_has_fetch_item" then
		keys = { id .. "_fetch", id .. "_fetch_count" }
	elseif sf == "delivery_task" then
		keys = { id }
	end
	for _, k in ipairs(keys or {}) do
		local live = load_var(db.actor, k)
		local ok, v, known = pcall(qt.record_of, k)
		if ok and known and not host.same_var(v, live) then
			host.trust("task_var_write", false, "player %s (#%s) turned task %s in: its %s is %s, the host recorded %s; judged by %s",
				host.nick(who), tostring(who), id, k, host.var_text(live), host.var_text(v),
				host.trust_mode("task_var_write") == "refuse" and "the host's record" or "the live value, as before")
			return
		end
	end
end

-- Did player `peer` take task `id`? The taker's character (host.taker_char: written at the give, kept in the host's save, a
-- reconnect keeps it) against the requester's. No verdict without knowledge, true: no record (a save from before it), a
-- record of the host's character on a seat that plays none (a world server's), a requester whose character is unknown.
-- Second value: the taker's character, for the log.
function host.is_taker(id, peer)
	local want = host.taker_char[id]
	if want == nil then return true, nil end
	if want == 0 then
		local plays = false
		for _, p in ipairs(players()) do if p.is_self then plays = true end end
		if not plays then return true, want end
	end
	local have = character_of(peer)
	if have == nil then return true, want end
	return have == want, want
end

-- The text of a taker for the log: "nick (#peer, character c)".
function host.taker_text(id, want)
	local tp = host.taker[id]
	return string_format("%s (#%s, character %s)", tp ~= nil and host.nick(tp) or "?", tostring(tp), tostring(want))
end

-- Round 2 (F5): did player `from` talk a moment ago to NPC `sp` (host numbering), the one his request names, and is that NPC the
-- task's giver? A task with no giver (a story task of dialogs_lostzone.give_task) takes the NPC of his dialog: the crossfire
-- of the Hidden Base is given by Hernandez and failed at Strelok. The talk is the host's word (_spoke_to: its talk locks; a
-- player on a map server's level, that server's).
function host.talked_for(id, from, sp)
	sp = tonumber(sp)
	if not sp or sp <= 0 or sp >= 65535 or sp ~= math_floor(sp) then return false end
	local tm = tmgr()
	local tsk = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
	local ok, giver = pcall(function() return is_task(tsk) and tonumber(tsk.task_giver_id) or nil end)
	giver = ok and giver or nil
	local has_giver = giver ~= nil and giver > 0 and giver < 65535
	if has_giver and not host.is_giver(giver, sp) then return false end -- round 5 (S1): or a member of the giver's squad
	-- Server (round 3, R2-S3): his map server says only "he is in some dialog", any dialog: for a task with a giver that cannot
	-- tell the giver's talk from another, so the exception holds only for a task without a giver
	if has_giver and _talk_vague(from) then return false end
	return _spoke_to(from, sp) == true
end

-- Round 2 (F5): an end of task `id` that the stock logic of a player's own machine sends for tasks he did not take: a faction
-- change cancels every DRX task there (xr_effects.drx_sl_cancel_questlines writes forced_status "fail" and cancelled_by_actor:
-- a fail and a cancel per task), and surge_manager's level change cancels faction_base_defense.
function host.auto_end(id)
	return type(id) == "string" and (id:sub(1, 7) == "drx_sl_" or id == "faction_base_defense")
end

-- Round 2 (F5): the refused player's news line "only <taker> can cancel this task" (the text is his machine's: the nick goes
-- only as an argument, never as the format).
function host.tell_only_taker(peer, id)
	if type(peer) ~= "number" or peer <= 0 or peer >= 0x100 then return end
	local tp = host.taker[id]
	local nick = tp ~= nil and host.nick(tp) or nil
	send(EV_REWARD, pack({ k = "only", n = nick ~= "?" and nick or nil, t = id }), peer)
end

-- Fail / cancel of a running task only by the player who took it. `from` is the transport's sender; one of a map server
-- (>= 0x100) is its level's logic (a timer, a target that died there), no player: ok. `t`: the request (Lua path), with the
-- NPC of his talk (sp).
function host.may_end(op, id, from, why, t)
	local ok, want = true, nil
	if from < 0x100 then ok, want = host.is_taker(id, from) end
	-- round 2 (F5): his choice in a dialog with the task's giver, a moment ago (dialogs.npc_cancel_task, a story fail phrase)
	if not ok and type(t) == "table" and host.talked_for(id, from, t.sp) then ok = true end
	if not ok and host.auto_end(id) then
		-- his own machine's stock logic (round 3, R2-B2): its own check "task_auto_end", counted without a line each (a faction
		-- change sends a fail and a cancel for every DRX task). "log": through, exactly as before round 1; "refuse": refused, the
		-- requester gets the host's state back; "off": through, not counted. Not a task_fail / task_cancel failure.
		local mode = host.trust_mode("task_auto_end")
		if mode == "off" then return true end
		stats.auto_end = stats.auto_end + 1
		if mode ~= "refuse" then return true end
		stats.auto_end_refused = stats.auto_end_refused + 1
		return false
	end
	local pass = host.trust("task_" .. op, ok, "player %s (#%s), task %s: %s by a player who did not take it; taker %s",
		host.nick(from), tostring(from), id, why or op, host.taker_text(id, want))
	if not pass then host.tell_only_taker(from, id) end
	return pass
end

-- Round 2 (F2): what the host's own check of task `id` says (the stock CRandomTask:task_complete reads the same fields): nil
-- when it found the task complete (last_check_task) or a turn-in on the host forced it; else why it is still running.
function host.still_running(tm, id)
	local tsk = tm.task_info[id]
	local ok, done = pcall(function() return tsk.last_check_task == "complete" or tsk.forced_status == "complete" end)
	if not ok or done then return nil end
	return "the host's own check of the task says it is still running"
end

-- Why player `who` cannot turn in task `id` now (the checks of ops.complete: money, items), or nil.
function host.turn_in_short(tm, id, who)
	if money_short(tm, id, who) then
		local price, foreign = host.fact_of(id .. "_fetch", 0)
		return string_format("not enough money: has %s, the task asks %s", tostring(ledger_money(who)),
			foreign and "a price that is a client's word" or tostring(price))
	end
	return host.item_short(tm, id)
end

-- Called by the engine (coop_story.cpp host_on_task_state, lua_task_state_ok) on the host for a client's TaskReqState, before
-- it notes the finisher or changes the task, whether the request is "explicit" or not. st: 2 completed, 0 failed. `from` is the
-- transport's sender, bridge: it is a map server. timed_out: the host's own clock says the task's time ran out (the engine's
-- fail of a task with a time limit). explicit: a script's set_task_state (else the client's own task check). False: refuse.
-- Round 2 (F2): a turn-in also needs the host's own check of the task to say it is done (host.still_running), explicit or not:
-- no honest flow completes a group task through the engine (a client's task functors answer false for them). A map server's
-- turn-in is its level's logic, whose facts the world server has not: not judged by the world server's own check.
function host_state_verdict(id, st, from, bridge, timed_out, explicit)
	if not world_active() or type(id) ~= "string" or type(from) ~= "number" then return true end
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not (tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id] ~= nil) then return true end -- no Lua task: nothing of ops.complete to ask
	if st == 2 then
		local who = player_of_request(from, id)
		if bridge ~= true then host.fact_line(tm, id, who) end -- round 7: as ops.complete
		local short = host.turn_in_short(tm, id, who)
		if short == nil and bridge ~= true then short = host.still_running(tm, id) end
		return host.trust("task_complete", short == nil, "player %s (#%s), task %s: turned in through the engine (%s), %s",
			host.nick(who), tostring(who), id, explicit == true and "a script's set_task_state" or "his task check", tostring(short))
	end
	if bridge == true or timed_out == true then return host.trust("task_fail", true) end
	return host.may_end("fail", id, from, "failed through the engine")
end

local function host_on_request(payload, from)
	if not world_active() or type(from) ~= "number" or from == 0 then return end
	stats.req_in = stats.req_in + 1
	local t = unpack_payload(payload)
	-- round 7 (P-SEC of the round 6 review): every object id his request names (the giver, the NPC of his talk, a bounty target) is a
	-- whole number 1..65534 or none, before any use (level.object_by_id, alife_object, give_task, host_make)
	t.g, t.sp, t.bt = host.obj_id(t.g), host.obj_id(t.sp), host.obj_id(t.bt)
	local id, op = t.i, t.op
	local fn = type(op) == "string" and ops[op]
	if type(id) ~= "string" or id == "" or not fn or not task_known(id) then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		log("! bad task request from #%s: %s %s", tostring(from), tostring(op), tostring(id))
		if type(id) == "string" and id ~= "" and #id <= 128 then host_send_state(id, from) end
		return
	end
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm then return end
	-- a player out of the task's audience can neither take, turn in, cancel nor stage it; for him it is not there. A map server's
	-- logic is no player: not gated (what it causes is cut at the rewards). A finished task keeps its record (the engine keeps
	-- it in the journal): a give of an id that is not running is a new task, judged anew by its give (as the engine's give).
	if from < 0x100 and not host.aud_sees(id, from) and not (op == "give" and tm.task_info[id] == nil) then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		log("#%s: %s '%s' refused: not his task", tostring(from), tostring(op), id)
		send(EV_STATE, pack(op == "give" and { i = id, d = true, r = 1 } or { i = id, d = true }), from)
		stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
		return
	end
	-- TZ 6.4 #1: a running group task is failed or cancelled only by the player who took it
	if (op == "fail" or op == "cancel") and tm.task_info[id] ~= nil and engine_task_running(id)
		and not host.may_end(op, id, from, nil, t) then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		host_send_state(id, from) -- his view back
		return
	end
	local who = player_of_request(from, id)
	host.exec_peer = who
	host.req_from = from -- the transport's sender (ops.stage: a map server's is not judged)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	local ok, res
	if qc and qc.with_level_of then
		ok, res = pcall(qc.with_level_of, who, fn, tm, id, t, who) -- his dialog, his NPC, his level
	else
		ok, res = pcall(fn, tm, id, t, who)
	end
	host.exec_peer = nil
	host.req_from = nil
	if not ok then report("request " .. op .. " " .. id, res) end
	if not ok or not res then
		stats.refused = stats.refused + 1
		if op == "give" and tm.task_info[id] == nil then
			-- A give this host could not do (its on_init died, the task said no) and no such task here: "not given" by name. The
			-- requester tells its player and frees the dialog that asked; a plain removal would drop his stub in silence.
			send(EV_STATE, pack({ i = id, d = true, r = 1 }), from)
			stats.state_out = stats.state_out + 1
		else
			host_send_state(id, from) -- the requester is behind: put its view back
		end
		return
	end
	log("#%s: %s '%s'", tostring(from), op, id)
	if res ~= "pending" then host_scan(false) end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host: rewards to the player who turned the task in (R-7.6)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function rcpt_client()
	return ctx ~= nil and ctx.rcpt ~= 0 and ctx.rcpt or nil
end

local function is_my_actor(obj)
	if obj == nil or not db.actor then return false end -- compared by id below: game_object has no == in luabind
	local ok, id = pcall(function()
		local f = obj.id
		if type(f) == "function" then return obj:id() end
		return f
	end)
	return ok and id == db.actor:id()
end

local function send_reward(peer, t)
	if t.t == nil and ctx then t.t = ctx.task end
	if send(EV_REWARD, pack(t), peer) then stats.rewards_routed = stats.rewards_routed + 1 end
end

-- The key of a player's waiting effects is his character, never a reusable peer slot.
local function effect_key(peer)
	return character_of(peer)
end

-- Host: an effect on a player's own character, run by his machine. It waits for his answer and goes out again on his next
-- sync: a level change or a reconnect right after the turn-in would lose it (client_on_reward needs an actor), and money
-- may already have been taken for it. The host's save keeps what waits (save_effects).
local function send_effect(peer, t)
	local key = effect_key(peer)
	if key == nil then report("effect", "recipient character is unknown"); return end
	-- split levels: the world records a player's own faction change itself (coop_faction.on_forward; nothing on a map server)
	local cf = t.k == "fx" and _G.coop_faction
	if type(cf) == "table" and type(cf.on_forward) == "function" then
		local ok, err = pcall(cf.on_forward, key, t, peer)
		if not ok then report("faction record", err) end
	end
	host.fx_seq = host.fx_seq + 1
	t.q = host.fx_seq
	if t.t == nil and ctx then t.t = ctx.task end
	local delivery = host.task_delivery()
	local event, target
	if delivery then event, target = delivery.effect_route(t, key) end
	local s = pack(t)
	local wait = host.fx_wait[key]
	if not wait then
		wait = {}
		host.fx_wait[key] = wait
	end
	wait[#wait + 1] = { q = t.q, s = s }
	if event then send(event, s, target); return end
	local online = peer_for_character(key)
	if online and online ~= 0 and send(EV_REWARD, s, online) then stats.rewards_routed = stats.rewards_routed + 1 end
end

local function host_on_effect_ack(payload, from)
	if not world_active() or type(from) ~= "number" or from == 0 then return end
	local q = tonumber(payload)
	local wait = host.fx_wait[effect_key(from)]
	if not (q and wait) then return end
	for i, e in ipairs(wait) do
		if e.q == q then
			table.remove(wait, i)
			return
		end
	end
end

local function host_resend_effects(peer)
	local wait = host.fx_wait[effect_key(peer)]
	if not wait then return end
	for _, e in ipairs(wait) do send(EV_REWARD, e.s, peer) end
end

-- Host: effect `fname` on the own character of the player the effects being run now belong to (FORWARD_EFFECTS), params p: it goes
-- to his machine (send_effect, k = "fx"), which runs it there. -> true: his (sent, or skipped: the task was not paid, or it is
-- nobody's, character 0 where seat 0 plays none); false: run it here. Module functions below, not locals: the chunk is at Lua's
-- limit (test_engine_header); the server's part (coop_srv_tasks, from coop_mode.when_srv) uses them too.
function forward_fx(fname, p)
	local peer = rcpt_client()
	if ctx and ctx.character == 0 then
		local away, seat = host.char0_elsewhere()
		if away then
			if seat == nil then return true end -- nobody's: not run on this process's ghost either
			peer = seat
		end
	end
	if peer and ctx.unpaid then
		log("'%s': %s skipped, the task was not paid", tostring(ctx.task), fname)
		return true
	end
	-- a world without split levels changes faction as a group: the host runs it once for all (coop_faction)
	local cf = _G.coop_faction
	local together = type(cf) == "table" and type(cf.group_mode) == "function" and cf.group_mode() == true
	if peer and type(p) == "table" and not together then
		local t = { k = "fx", f = fname }
		for i = 1, 4 do
			if p[i] ~= nil then t["p" .. i] = tostring(p[i]) end
		end
		send_effect(peer, t)
		return true
	end
	return false
end

-- S5 (A-S5T): a server's part adds an effect a player's machine runs for the world (its name in FORWARD_EFFECTS: his machine takes it
-- from the host, the world server takes it from a map server). Whoever wraps it calls forward_fx. Nothing adds one in the co-op.
function forward_allow(fname)
	if type(fname) ~= "string" or fname == "" or #fname > 80 then return false end
	FORWARD_EFFECTS[fname] = true
	return true
end

function forward_allowed(fname) return type(fname) == "string" and FORWARD_EFFECTS[fname] == true end

-- Host: personal effect `t` (k = "stat" | "fx") for the player the effects being run now belong to (with_character): it waits for
-- his machine's answer as a reward's does (send_effect). -> false outside such a scope.
function send_personal(t)
	if not (ctx and type(t) == "table") then return false end
	send_effect(ctx.rcpt, t)
	return true
end

-- The effects of players this process sent and nobody answered yet: character -> { { q, s }, ... } (a map server sends its own up
-- again until the world server answers, coop_srv_tasks). The table itself: a load replaces it.
function fx_pending() return host.fx_wait end

-- The map servers' effects the host ran already: "<bridge>:<epoch>:<number>" -> true (kept in the save, save_effects).
function map_seen() return host.map_seen end

function decode_payload(s) return unpack_payload(s) end

-- Host: money for (or from, n < 0) a client's character. The money is the host ledger's (F2 T6): coop.money_grant
-- changes the character's money (never below 0) and the engine sends the client its new balance. A client's own
-- Lua never adds it: the engine would count that as the client's income, limited by the Script allowance, and a
-- reward above it would be lost. The client only gets the news line (event coop_trw, k = mn).
local function grant_money(peer, n)
	local whole = n >= 0 and math_floor(n) or -math_floor(-n)
	if whole ~= whole or whole == 0 or whole == math.huge or whole == -math.huge then return false end
	local grant = api and api.money_grant
	if type(grant) ~= "function" then
		report("grant_money", "coop.money_grant is missing")
		return false
	end
	local called, ok, why = pcall(grant, peer, whole)
	if not (called and ok) then
		log("money %d for #%s refused: %s", whole, tostring(peer), tostring(called and why or ok))
		return false
	end
	send_reward(peer, { k = "mn", n = whole })
	return true
end

function flush_fines()
	if not world_active() then return end
	for id, owed in pairs(host.fines) do
		local peer = peer_for_character(id)
		local balance = peer ~= nil and api.money_of and api.money_of(peer)
		if type(balance) == "number" then
			local amount = math.min(owed, math.max(0, balance))
			if amount == 0 or grant_money(peer, -amount) then host.fines[id] = nil end
		end
	end
end

-- Offline guide fines wait for that character; another player reusing his peer pays nothing.
function fine_character(id, amount)
	if not world_active() or type(id) ~= "number" or id < 0 or id >= 65535 or id % 1 ~= 0
		or type(amount) ~= "number" or amount ~= amount or amount <= 0 or amount == math.huge then return false end
	host.fines[id] = (host.fines[id] or 0) + math_floor(amount)
	flush_fines()
	return true
end

-- Host: the "money received" line on a player's machine for money the host changed outside a task reward (achievement
-- money, coop_quests_pda); the money itself is the ledger's.
function money_line(peer, n)
	if not world_active() then return false end
	n = tonumber(n)
	if not (n and peer ~= nil and tonumber(peer) ~= 0) then return false end
	send_reward(tonumber(peer), { k = "mn", n = n })
	return true
end

local function online_peers()
	-- peer 0 is the host player's character. A world server whose seat plays no character has only its ghost there: no share for it
	-- (the quest audit, 2026-11-13: with coop_share_rewards 1 the ghost took a part of every reward).
	local list = (coop_mode.decides_world() and not coop_mode.seat_plays(0)) and {} or { 0 }
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if not p.is_self and p.avatar_id and (level.object_by_id(p.avatar_id) or far_of(p.id, p.avatar_id)) then list[#list + 1] = p.id end
	end
	if #list == 0 then list[1] = ctx and ctx.rcpt or 0 end -- nobody in the world to share with: the one who earned it
	return list
end

-- Host, in a reward scope: pays n to the player who turned the task in, or splits it over the online players
-- (coop_share_rewards 1). The remainder goes to the player it is for when he shares, else to the first sharer: a world
-- server's seat 0 and a player off the level do not share, and the parts must add up to n. give(peer, amount) pays one share,
-- peer 0 = the host.
local function split_money(n, give)
	if ctx.group then
		local rg = reward_group()
		for _, e in ipairs(rg.money_plan(n, ctx.group, ctx.rcpt, ctx.full)) do
			if e.m.in_world then give(e.m.peer, e.n) else rg.pay_absent(e.m, e.n) end
		end
		return
	end
	local list = { ctx.rcpt }
	if ctx.share then
		list = {}
		for _, peer in ipairs(online_peers()) do -- a task with an audience: only those who see it
			if host.aud_sees(ctx.task, peer) then list[#list + 1] = peer end
		end
		if #list == 0 then list[1] = ctx.rcpt end
	end
	local part = math_floor(n / #list)
	local rest = n - part * #list
	local rest_to = list[1]
	for _, peer in ipairs(list) do
		if peer == ctx.rcpt then rest_to = peer end
	end
	for _, peer in ipairs(list) do
		local amount = part + (peer == rest_to and rest or 0)
		if amount > 0 then give(peer, amount) end
	end
end

-- Stock payouts that do not go through dialogs.relocate_money but call db.actor:give_money themselves
-- (tasks_multifetch.remove_items_and_pay from multifetch_remove, tasks_defense.barrier_defense_*_complete) would put the
-- money on the HOST's actor whoever turned the task in (F2 T6 review). Their file cannot change, so the wrapper
-- (redirect_payout) measures what the call adds to the host's money, takes it back and pays it as every other task
-- money: to the player who turned the task in through the host ledger, or split with coop_share_rewards 1. The host
-- keeps it only when it turned the task in itself. While the call runs, the stock "money received" line for the host's
-- actor is swallowed (payout_scope): the player who gets the money sees his own line.
local payout_scope = false
local news_money = nil -- news_manager.relocate_money as it was before patch_rewards

local function redirect_payout(orig)
	return function(...)
		if not (ctx and (ctx.rcpt ~= 0 or ctx.share) and world_active() and db.actor) then return orig(...) end
		local before = db.actor:money()
		local prev = payout_scope
		payout_scope = true
		local res = { pcall(orig, ...) }
		payout_scope = prev
		local gained = db.actor:money() - before
		if gained > 0 and ctx then
			db.actor:give_money(-gained)
			split_money(gained, function(peer, amount)
				if peer == 0 then
					db.actor:give_money(amount)
					if news_money then news_money(db.actor, "in", amount) end
				else
					grant_money(peer, amount)
				end
			end)
		end
		if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
		return unpack(res, 2)
	end
end

local FETCH_EFFECTS = { "fetch_reward_and_remove", "remove_fetch_item", "remove_artefact_item" }

-- Host: one unit of a group reward (coop_share_rewards 2, 3). The stock code that asked gets the item of the player who
-- turned the task in, if he got one.
local function give_to_group(create, section, t)
	local rg = reward_group()
	local res, copies = nil, {}
	for _, m in ipairs(rg.item_targets(ctx.group, ctx.full)) do
		local owner = rg.holder(m)
		local se = owner and create(section, owner, t)
		if se then
			local g = ctx.given[m.id]
			if not g then
				g = { m = m, items = {} }
				ctx.given[m.id] = g
			end
			g.items[section] = (g.items[section] or 0) + 1
			ctx.counted[section] = true
			copies[#copies + 1] = se
			if res == nil or m.peer == ctx.rcpt then res = se end
		end
	end
	local state = coop_item_entity_state
	if res and state then state.roll_group(section, copies, res, t, ctx.stock_item) end
	return res
end

-- Host, when (a part of) a group reward was handed out: one line per player and section, however many units the stock
-- code made. A player who is away gets a note instead.
local news_item = nil -- news_manager.relocate_item as it was before patch_rewards

local function group_lines(c)
	if not c.group then return end
	local rg = reward_group()
	for _, g in pairs(c.given) do
		for section, n in pairs(g.items) do
			if not g.m.in_world then
				rg.note_item(g.m.id, section, n)
			elseif g.m.peer == 0 then
				if news_item then news_item(db.actor, "in", section, n) end
			else
				send_reward(g.m.peer, { k = "news", ty = "in", s = section, n = n, t = c.task })
			end
		end
	end
	c.given = {}
	if c.noted then return end
	c.noted = true
	for _, m in ipairs(c.group) do
		if not m.in_world then rg.note(m.id, "c", 1) end
	end
end

local function host_task_callback(orig, tsk, state)
	local okid, id = pcall(function() return tsk:get_id() end)
	if not (world_active() and okid and type(id) == "string") or not (state == task.completed or state == task.fail) then
		return orig(tsk, state)
	end
	local rcpt = recipient(id)
	local swapped = not host.aud_sees(id, rcpt) -- a recipient out of the task's audience: its taker instead
	if swapped then rcpt = host.aud_taker_peer(id) end
	local owner = rcpt -- statistics, rank and reputation: his, also when he has left (they wait for him)
	-- messages: the player who asked for this result (nil: a script, a timer), and whether it was a cancel
	local by = host.finisher[id]
	local tm = tmgr()
	local rtask = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
	local cancelled = is_task(rtask) and rtask.cancelled_by_actor == true
	host.finisher[id] = nil
	local mode = state == task.completed and reward_mode() or 0
	local share = mode ~= 0
	local everyone = mode == EVERYONE_SHARED or mode == EVERYONE_FULL
	-- W5: also for the host's own task (rcpt 0): without the reward scope the story wrapper
	-- (coop_quests_story) took its on_complete rewards for a story condlist and paid every client too
	local prev = ctx
	ctx = { task = id, rcpt = rcpt, share = share, by = by, cancelled = cancelled, owner = owner }
	ctx.aud = host.aud_rec(id)
	ctx.character = (swapped or by == nil) and host.taker_char[id] or character_of(rcpt)
	if not cancelled then
		if state == task.fail then
			ctx.personal = host.failure_participants[id]
		elseif rep_share_rule() == "everyone" then
			-- each character once: the taker, who was in game at the accept, who is in game now
			local ids, seen = {}, {}
			local function put(list)
				for _, c in ipairs(list or {}) do
					if type(c) == "number" and not seen[c] then ids[#ids + 1], seen[c] = c, true end
				end
			end
			put({ host.taker_char[id] })
			put(host.rep_party[id] or host.participants[id])
			put(participant_ids())
			ctx.personal = #ids > 0 and ids or nil
		end
		if ctx.personal == nil and host.taker_char[id] ~= nil then ctx.personal = { host.taker_char[id] } end
		ctx.personal = host.aud_cut(id, ctx.personal) -- a task with an audience: only those who see it
	end
	if everyone then
		ctx.group, ctx.full = host.aud_group(id, reward_group().list()), mode == EVERYONE_FULL
		ctx.given, ctx.counted = {}, {}
	end
	local this = ctx
	-- The stock end of a task (on_complete, on_fail, on_cancel and what they call) reads the world around "the actor": the giver's
	-- game object (goodwill by the tasker), the quest item to take away, the actor's faction (the next DRX giver), the first target of
	-- the task it gives next. On a world server that world is a map server's level, and "at home" none of it was found (the quest
	-- audit, 2026-11-13). The end runs in the far view of the level of the player it is for - he stands at the giver when he turns
	-- the task in - and, with nobody to name (a timer, a script), on the level of what the task is about. Without split levels the
	-- far view is no view: the call is the stock's.
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	local ok, err
	if not (qc and qc.with_level_of and qc.with_target) then
		ok, err = pcall(orig, tsk, state)
	elseif rcpt ~= 0 then
		ok, err = pcall(qc.with_level_of, rcpt, orig, tsk, state)
	else
		local about = is_task(rtask) and (type(rtask.current_target) == "number" and rtask.current_target or rtask.task_giver_id) or nil
		ok, err = pcall(qc.with_target, about, 0, id, orig, tsk, state)
	end
	ctx = prev
	group_lines(this)
	host.given_by[id] = nil
	if not ok then report("task callback " .. id, err) end
	if rcpt ~= 0 then log("rewards of '%s' go to #%s%s", id, tostring(rcpt), share and " (money shared)" or "") end
end

-- Character 0 is seat 0's player (the host's; a world server's seat plays none). Where this process's own actor is no player (a
-- server's ghost: a map server, a world server), character 0 is not this actor. -> true and the peer whose it is: 0 when seat 0 plays
-- a character, nil when it plays none (nobody's). false: this actor is a player (the co-op host), or no mode facade here.
-- S5 (A-S5T): was "peer 0 on a map server", from the hybrid, where the host played; on a server it sent the effect up to a world
-- server whose seat plays nobody, which dropped it without an answer, and the map server sent it again every second for good.
function host.char0_elsewhere()
	local m = coop_mode
	if not (type(m) == "table" and type(m.actor_is_player) == "function" and m.actor_is_player() == false) then return false end
	return true, (type(m.seat_plays) == "function" and m.seat_plays(0) == true) and 0 or nil
end

-- The client whose character the rank and reputation being changed now belong to, or nil: the host's.
local function stat_peer()
	-- character 0 where this process's actor is no player: seat 0's player, or nobody's (host.char0_elsewhere)
	if ctx and ctx.character == 0 then
		local away, seat = host.char0_elsewhere()
		if away then return seat end
	end
	local p = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_players")
	if ctx == nil and p and p.in_identity and p.in_identity() then
		local peer = p.peer_of(db.actor)
		if peer ~= nil then return peer ~= 0 and peer or nil end
	end
	if ctx == nil then return nil end
	if ctx.owner ~= nil and ctx.owner ~= 0 then return ctx.owner end
	return rcpt_client()
end

-- Client peer the effects being run now are keyed to (items into its character, news to it), or nil.
function reward_peer()
	return ctx ~= nil and ctx.rcpt ~= 0 and ctx.rcpt or nil
end

function personal_character()
	return ctx and ctx.character
end

function active_of(peer)
	return host.active[peer]
end

-- True while a task's rewards / status effects are being handed out (they belong to one player).
function in_reward_scope()
	return ctx ~= nil
end

-- Host: runs fn with the effects keyed to the actor (items, news, money, goodwill) going to `peer`.
function with_recipient(peer, fn, ...)
	peer = tonumber(peer)
	if not active() or not (coop_mode.decides_world() or coop_mode.leads_here()) then return fn(...) end
	if not peer or peer < 0 or peer % 1 ~= 0 then
		report("recipient", "missing or invalid player; personal effects were not applied")
		return
	end
	-- A player can be loading or disconnected while a timer fires. Keep his address:
	-- send_effect persists statistics until he acknowledges them. Never substitute the host.
	-- An explicit nested scope (including peer 0) must temporarily replace the outer recipient.
	local id, previous = character_of(peer), ctx
	ctx = { task = previous and previous.task or "", rcpt = peer, owner = peer, character = id, share = false, status = true }
	local res = { pcall(fn, ...) }
	ctx = previous
	if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
	return unpack(res, 2)
end

function with_character(id, fn, ...)
	if type(id) ~= "number" or id < 0 then return end
	local peer, previous = peer_for_character(id), ctx
	ctx = { task = previous and previous.task or "", rcpt = peer or -1, owner = peer or -1,
		character = id, share = false, status = true }
	local p = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_players")
	local result
	if id == 0 and p and p.in_identity and p.in_identity() then
		result = { pcall(p.with_identity, p.own_actor(), fn, ...) }
	else result = { pcall(fn, ...) } end
	ctx = previous
	if not result[1] then error(result[2], 0) end
	return unpack(result, 2)
end

function each_personal(fn, ...)
	if not (ctx and ctx.personal and #ctx.personal > 0) then return false end
	for _, id in ipairs(ctx.personal) do with_character(id, fn, ...) end
	return true
end

-- Execute world logic once, distributing only its personal reputation/statistic/goodwill effects.
function with_participants(ids, peer, fn, ...)
	if not active() or not (coop_mode.decides_world() or coop_mode.leads_here()) then return fn(...) end
	local previous = ctx
	ctx = { task = previous and previous.task or "", rcpt = peer or 0, owner = peer or 0,
		character = character_of(peer or 0), personal = ids, share = false, status = true }
	local result = { pcall(fn, ...) }
	ctx = previous
	if not result[1] then error(result[2], 0) end
	return unpack(result, 2)
end

-- Host: a task's status / target functors run with the actor's effects going to the player who took it
-- (a measuring device handed out on the first check lands in that player's character).
function with_task_owner(id, fn, ...)
	if ctx ~= nil or not world_active() or type(id) ~= "string" then return fn(...) end
	local t = host.taker[id]
	if t == nil then return fn(...) end
	ctx = { task = id, rcpt = t, owner = t, character = host.taker_char[id] or character_of(t), share = false, status = true,
		personal = host.aud_cut(id, host.participants[id]) }
	-- a functor can make a companion by writing the stock table itself (tasks_agent_rescue): what it added is the taker's
	local comp = rawget(_G, "coop_npc_companions")
	local before = comp and comp.squads_now and comp.squads_now()
	local res = { pcall(fn, ...) }
	ctx = nil
	if before then comp.claim_since(before, t) end
	if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
	return unpack(res, 2)
end

-- Stock effects read the actor of the machine they run on: statistics, rank and reputation of a task (the counters of
-- task_manager.task_callback, increase_rank and the like in on_complete, tasks_guide) would all land on the host's actor.
local function patch_statistics()
	local gs = rawget(_G, "game_statistics") or game_statistics
	if type(gs) ~= "table" then
		log("! game_statistics not found: a task's rank and reputation stay on the host's actor")
		return
	end
	-- owner 2026-11-13: what is no player's here would land on the ghost actor of a map server or of a world server whose seat plays
	-- no character (coop_quests_core.actor_is_nobody): dropped. An ordinary host's actor is its player: unchanged.
	local count = gs.increment_statistic
	if type(count) == "function" then
		gs.increment_statistic = function(name, custom_rank, custom_rept)
			if TASK_STATS[name] and each_personal(gs.increment_statistic, name, custom_rank, custom_rept) then return end
			local peer = stat_peer()
			if not peer and not coop_mode.actor_is_player() then return end
			if not peer then return count(name, custom_rank, custom_rept) end
			send_effect(peer, { k = "stat", f = name, r = tonumber(custom_rank), p = tonumber(custom_rept) })
		end
	end
	for fname, what in pairs({ increment_rank = "rank", increment_reputation = "rept" }) do
		local orig = gs[fname]
		if type(orig) == "function" then
			gs[fname] = function(value)
				if what == "rept" and each_personal(gs[fname], value) then return end
				local peer = stat_peer()
				if not peer and not coop_mode.actor_is_player() then return end
				if not peer then return orig(value) end
				send_effect(peer, { k = "stat", f = what, n = tonumber(value) or 0 })
			end
		end
	end
end

-- The "stash coordinates" line of a task's reward is the player's who turned it in (the spot is everybody's). The line
-- is shown inside set_random_stash; a mod's override may add a text, the client computes that one in its own language.
local function patch_stash_line()
	local tm = rawget(_G, "treasure_manager") or treasure_manager
	if not (type(tm) == "table" and type(tm.set_random_stash) == "function") then
		log("! treasure_manager.set_random_stash not found: stash lines of task rewards stay on the host")
		return
	end
	local orig = tm.set_random_stash
	tm.set_random_stash = function(no_spot, hint, bonus, id, dbg)
		local peer = rcpt_client()
		local nm = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
		local stock = nm and nm.send_treasure
		if not (peer and type(stock) == "function") then return orig(no_spot, hint, bonus, id, dbg) end
		local told = false
		nm.send_treasure = function(param, text)
			if param == 0 or param == nil then told = true else return stock(param, text) end
		end
		local res = { pcall(orig, no_spot, hint, bonus, id, dbg) }
		nm.send_treasure = stock
		if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
		local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
		if told and type(qc) == "table" then qc.send("treasure", { p = 0, b = tonumber(res[2]) or tonumber(id) }, peer) end
		return unpack(res, 2)
	end
end

local function patch_rewards()
	-- a restrictor's condlist gives a task: the effect knows the zone (nearest_taker)
	local xfx = rawget(_G, "xr_effects") or xr_effects
	if xfx and type(xfx.reward_item) == "function" then
		local reward = xfx.reward_item
		xfx.reward_item = function(actor, npc, p, ...)
			local group = ctx and ctx.group and ctx
			if not group then return reward(actor, npc, p, ...) end
			local previous = group.stock_item
			group.stock_item = p and p[1]
			local result = { pcall(reward, actor, npc, p, ...) }
			group.stock_item = previous
			if not result[1] then error(result[2], 0) end
			return unpack(result, 2)
		end
	end
	if xfx and type(xfx.give_task) == "function" then
		local give = xfx.give_task
		xfx.give_task = function(actor, obj, p)
			local prev = host.give_near
			host.give_near = obj
			local res = { pcall(give, actor, obj, p) }
			host.give_near = prev
			if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
			return unpack(res, 2)
		end
	end

	-- money
	local dlg = rawget(_G, "dialogs") or dialogs
	if dlg and type(dlg.relocate_money) == "function" then
		local orig = dlg.relocate_money
		dlg.relocate_money = function(victim, num, typ)
			local n = tonumber(num)
			if not (ctx and typ == "in" and n and n > 0) then return orig(victim, num, typ) end
			split_money(n, function(peer, amount)
				if peer == 0 then
					orig(victim, amount, "in")
				else
					grant_money(peer, amount)
				end
			end)
		end
	else
		log("! dialogs.relocate_money not found: task money is not routed")
	end

	-- items into the turning-in player's character (host-authoritative spawn)
	local create = rawget(_G, "alife_create_item")
	if type(create) == "function" then
		raw_create = create
		_G.alife_create_item = function(section, obj, t)
			if ctx and ctx.group and not ctx.returns and is_my_actor(obj) and reward_group().shareable(section) then
				return give_to_group(create, section, t)
			end
			local peer = rcpt_client()
			if peer and is_my_actor(obj) then
				local o = recipient_body(peer)
				if o then return create(section, o, t) end
				report("item reward", "recipient character unavailable: " .. tostring(character_of(peer)))
				return -- never create a client's item in the host's inventory
			end
			return create(section, obj, t)
		end
	else
		log("! alife_create_item not found: task items are not routed")
	end

	-- xr_effects.give_actor (the PDA of a task, in its on_init) makes the item with alife_create(section, ..., AC_ID): past the
	-- redirect above, into the host's own inventory, which on a world server is its ghost's (the quest audit, 2026-11-13). For a
	-- task of another player the item is made the routed way; the host's own task is the stock's.
	local xe = rawget(_G, "xr_effects") or xr_effects
	if xe and type(xe.give_actor) == "function" then
		local stock_give = xe.give_actor
		xe.give_actor = function(actor, npc, p)
			if not (rcpt_client() and type(p) == "table") then return stock_give(actor, npc, p) end
			local news = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
			for _, section in pairs(p) do
				alife_create_item(section, db.actor)
				if news and news.relocate_item then news.relocate_item(db.actor, "in", section) end
			end
		end
	end

	-- xr_effects.inc_goodwill_by_tasker_comm takes the giver's faction from the task's var (task_giver_comm: only the delivery
	-- tasks write it) or from the NPC the actor talks to. A task a client turns in ends in the host's task callback, where nobody
	-- talks: 15 tasks gave no goodwill (the quest audit, 2026-11-13). The faction of the task's giver, from his record, stands
	-- in the var for this one call; a faction the task wrote itself and the host's own talk are the stock's.
	local stock_comm = xe and xe.inc_goodwill_by_tasker_comm
	if type(stock_comm) == "function" then
		xe.inc_goodwill_by_tasker_comm = function(actor, npc, p)
			local id = type(p) == "table" and p[1]
			local tm = type(id) == "string" and world_active() and tmgr() or nil
			local tsk = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
			if not (tsk and db.actor) or db.actor:is_talking() then return stock_comm(actor, npc, p) end
			local had = load_var(db.actor, id)
			if type(had) == "table" and had.task_giver_comm then return stock_comm(actor, npc, p) end
			local se = tsk.task_giver_id and rawget(_G, "alife_object") and alife_object(tsk.task_giver_id)
			local ok, comm = pcall(function() return se and se:community() end)
			if not (ok and type(comm) == "string" and comm ~= "") then return stock_comm(actor, npc, p) end
			local with = {}
			if type(had) == "table" then
				for k, v in pairs(had) do with[k] = v end
			end
			with.task_giver_comm = comm
			host.var_quiet = true -- round 4: a stand-in for one call, the var back as it was: its facts unchanged
			save_var(db.actor, id, with)
			host.var_quiet = nil
			local res = { pcall(stock_comm, actor, npc, p) }
			host.var_quiet = true
			save_var(db.actor, id, had)
			host.var_quiet = nil
			if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
			return unpack(res, 2)
		end
	end

	-- item news to the player who gets / gives the items
	local nm = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
	if nm and type(nm.relocate_item) == "function" then
		local orig = nm.relocate_item
		news_item = orig
		nm.relocate_item = function(actor, typ, item, amount)
			if ctx and ctx.group and ctx.counted[item] and typ == "in" and is_my_actor(actor) then return true end -- group_lines
			local peer = rcpt_client()
			if peer and is_my_actor(actor) then
				send_reward(peer, { k = "news", ty = tostring(typ), s = tostring(item), n = tonumber(amount) or 1 })
				return true
			end
			return orig(actor, typ, item, amount)
		end
	end

	if nm and type(nm.relocate_money) == "function" then
		news_money = nm.relocate_money
		nm.relocate_money = function(actor, typ, amount)
			if payout_scope and is_my_actor(actor) then return true end -- the player who gets the money sees the line
			return news_money(actor, typ, amount)
		end
	end

	-- goodwill rewards / penalties keyed to the player's own character
	local xe = rawget(_G, "xr_effects") or xr_effects
	if xe then
		for _, fname in ipairs({ "inc_faction_goodwill_to_actor", "dec_faction_goodwill_to_actor" }) do
			local orig = xe[fname]
			if type(orig) == "function" then
				xe[fname] = function(actor, npc, p)
					if is_my_actor(actor) and each_personal(xe[fname], actor, npc, p) then return end
					local peer = rcpt_client()
					if peer and type(p) == "table" and is_my_actor(actor) then
						local o = recipient_body(peer)
						if o then
							local r = orig(o, npc, { p[1], p[2] }) -- no message on the host
							if p[3] and p[1] then
								send_reward(peer, { k = "gw", c = tostring(p[1]),
									g = fname == "inc_faction_goodwill_to_actor" and (tonumber(p[2]) or 0) > 0 })
							end
							return r
						end
						report("goodwill", "recipient character unavailable: " .. tostring(character_of(peer)))
						return
					end
					return orig(actor, npc, p)
				end
			end
		end
		-- payment for a money task: taken from the player who turned it in
		local pay = xe.drx_sl_money_task_payment
		if type(pay) == "function" then
			xe.drx_sl_money_task_payment = function(actor, npc, p)
				local peer = rcpt_client()
				if peer and type(p) == "table" and p[1] ~= nil then
					local money = tonumber(load_var(db.actor, p[1], 0)) or 0
					local have = money > 0 and ledger_money(peer) or nil
					if have and have < money then
						-- spent since the turn-in: the ledger would stop at 0 and the faction change would be free
						ctx.unpaid = true
						log("'%s': #%s has %d RU, the task takes %d: not paid", tostring(ctx.task), tostring(peer), have, money)
						return
					end
					if money > 0 then grant_money(peer, -money) end
					return
				end
				return pay(actor, npc, p)
			end
		end
		-- Stock fetch effects take the player's goods and hand back what is left of them: the artefact out of its container,
		-- the empty container, the leftover uses. That is no reward: the group gets no copies of it.
		local fetch_module = _G.tasks_fetch -- it adds these effects to xr_effects when it loads: loads it now
		for _, fname in ipairs(FETCH_EFFECTS) do
			local orig = fetch_module ~= false and xe[fname]
			if type(orig) == "function" then
				xe[fname] = function(...)
					if not (ctx and ctx.group) then return orig(...) end
					local c, prev = ctx, ctx.returns
					c.returns = true
					local res = { pcall(orig, ...) }
					c.returns = prev
					if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
					return unpack(res, 2)
				end
			end
		end
		-- tasks_multifetch pays on_complete with db.actor:give_money (the host's actor): to the one who turned it in
		if type(xe.multifetch_remove) == "function" then xe.multifetch_remove = redirect_payout(xe.multifetch_remove) end
		-- effects on the player's own character run on that player's machine (forward_fx)
		for fname in pairs(FORWARD_EFFECTS) do
			local orig = xe[fname]
			if type(orig) == "function" then
				xe[fname] = function(actor, npc, p)
					if forward_fx(fname, p) then return end
					return orig(actor, npc, p)
				end
			end
		end
	end

	-- Freedom barrier defense pays 40 000 / 25 000 with db.actor:give_money from a dialog action (the speaker's
	-- machine). A client's own run is not touched (the engine ledger takes its change); when the host runs it for a
	-- player (with_recipient) the money goes to that player. The host's own talk pays the host.
	local td = rawget(_G, "tasks_defense") or tasks_defense
	if type(td) == "table" then
		for _, fname in ipairs({ "barrier_defense_monolith_complete", "barrier_defense_zombie_complete" }) do
			if type(td[fname]) == "function" then td[fname] = redirect_payout(td[fname]) end
		end
	end

	-- delayed rewards (fetch pays one second later) keep the context
	local cte = rawget(_G, "CreateTimeEvent")
	if type(cte) == "function" then
		_G.CreateTimeEvent = function(ev_id, act_id, timer, f, ...)
			if ctx and type(f) == "function" then
				local c, f0, returns = ctx, f, ctx.returns
				f = function(...)
					local prev = ctx
					ctx = c
					-- the group may have changed since the task was turned in; a return stays one a second later
					local prev_returns = c.returns
					c.returns = returns
					if c.group then c.group = host.aud_group(c.task, reward_group().list()) end
					local res = { pcall(f0, ...) }
					c.returns = prev_returns
					ctx = prev
					group_lines(c)
					if not res[1] then
						report("delayed task reward", res[2])
						return true
					end
					return unpack(res, 2)
				end
			end
			return cte(ev_id, act_id, timer, f, ...)
		end
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Host: quest items of any group member (R-7.5)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Holders to take items from: the player who turned the task in first, then the host, then the rest.
local function holders()
	local list, rest = {}, {}
	local rc = rcpt_client()
	local mine
	for _, h in ipairs(party()) do
		if h.self then
			mine = h
		elseif rc and h.peer == rc then
			list[#list + 1] = h
		else
			rest[#rest + 1] = h
		end
	end
	if mine then list[#list + 1] = mine end
	for _, h in ipairs(rest) do list[#list + 1] = h end
	return list
end

-- Releases up to `amt` items of `sec` held by h (each item counts 1, like xr_effects.remove_item).
local function release_from(h, sec, amt)
	local ids = {}
	pcall(function()
		h.obj:iterate_inventory(function(_, item)
			if #ids < amt and item:section() == sec then ids[#ids + 1] = item:id() end
		end, nil)
	end)
	for _, id in ipairs(ids) do alife_release_id(id) end
	if not h.self then stats.party_releases = stats.party_releases + #ids end
	return #ids
end

-- Moves up to `units` of `sec` from h to the host's actor (they arrive before a delayed stock reward runs).
local function move_from(h, sec, units)
	local moved = 0
	local multi = uses_of(sec)
	local items = {}
	pcall(function()
		h.obj:iterate_inventory(function(_, item)
			if moved < units and item:section() == sec then
				items[#items + 1] = item
				moved = moved + (multi and item:get_remaining_uses() or 1)
			end
		end, nil)
	end)
	for _, item in ipairs(items) do h.obj:transfer_item(item, db.actor) end
	stats.party_moves = stats.party_moves + #items
	return moved
end

local function container_of(h, sec)
	for _, cont in ipairs(CONTAINERS) do
		local c = h.obj:object(sec .. "_" .. cont)
		if c then return c, cont end
	end
	return nil
end

-- Spawn without the reward redirect (the item goes exactly where asked).
local function create_plain(sec, obj, reward)
	local f = raw_create or rawget(_G, "alife_create_item")
	local se = f(sec, obj)
	if se and reward and coop_item_entity_state then coop_item_entity_state.roll_reward(sec, se) end
	return se
end

local function count_items(obj, sec) -- items, not uses
	local n = 0
	pcall(function()
		obj:iterate_inventory(function(_, item)
			if item:section() == sec then n = n + 1 end
		end, nil)
	end)
	return n
end

local function party_remove(sec, amt)
	local left = amt
	for _, h in ipairs(holders()) do
		if left <= 0 then break end
		left = left - release_from(h, sec, left)
	end
	local removed = amt - left
	if removed > 0 then news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, "out", sec, removed) end
	if left > 0 then log("! group had %d x %s less than the task takes", left, sec) end
	return removed
end

-- Host: takes up to `amt` items of `sec` from the group (the player the effects are keyed to first,
-- then the host, then the others). Returns how many were taken.
function party_take(sec, amt)
	if not world_active() or type(sec) ~= "string" then return 0 end
	amt = tonumber(amt) or 1
	if amt <= 0 then return 0 end
	local ok, n = pcall(party_remove, sec, amt)
	if not ok then
		report("party_take " .. sec, n)
		return 0
	end
	return n or 0
end

-- Host: a db.actor:iterate_inventory for ONE call (coop_quests_core.with_actor) that walks every player's character: the
-- turning-in player's first, then the host's, then the rest. Stock tasks_multifetch counts, pays for and takes items through
-- db.actor:iterate_inventory and releases them by id, so the group's items count and go like the host's own.
-- real = the plain method of db.actor. f(item_owner, item) returning true stops the walk, as in the engine.
function party_inventory_walker(real)
	return function(me, f, x)
		local stop = false
		local function g(owner, item)
			local r = f(owner, item)
			if r == true then stop = true end
			return r
		end
		for _, h in ipairs(holders()) do
			if h.self then real(me, g, x) else h.obj:iterate_inventory(g, x) end
			if stop then return end
		end
	end
end

-- Host: money and items for one player (0 = the host's own actor). Items are spawned by the host into
-- that player's character; the player sees the news on its own machine. `effect`: the stock effect that made the reward;
-- a copy is rolled only when that effect rolls (coop_item_entity_state.effect_rolls), a caller naming none keeps the roll.
function give_to_peer(peer, money, sections, effect)
	if not active() or not (coop_mode.decides_world() or coop_mode.leads_here()) then return end
	peer = tonumber(peer) or 0
	money = math_floor(tonumber(money) or 0)
	local mine = peer == 0 or peer == self_peer()
	if money ~= 0 then
		if mine then
			if money > 0 then dialogs.relocate_money(db.actor, money, "in") else db.actor:give_money(money) end
		else
			grant_money(peer, money)
		end
	end
	if type(sections) == "table" then
		local obj = mine and db.actor or avatar_obj(peer)
		for _, sec in ipairs(sections) do
			if type(sec) == "string" and sec ~= "" and obj then
				create_plain(sec, obj, effect == nil or (coop_item_entity_state ~= nil
					and coop_item_entity_state.effect_rolls(effect)))
				if mine then
					news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, "in", sec, 1)
				else
					send_reward(peer, { k = "news", ty = "in", s = sec, n = 1 })
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

-- Fetch reward (stock: one second later, from the host's inventory): bring the items to the host's actor,
-- the turning-in player's own items first.
local function gather_fetch(var)
	local sec = load_var(db.actor, var)
	if type(sec) ~= "string" then return end
	local need = tonumber(load_var(db.actor, var .. "_count")) or 1
	local left = need
	local rc = rcpt_client()
	local list = holders()
	if rc and list[1] and list[1].peer == rc then left = left - move_from(list[1], sec, left) end
	left = left - count_in(db.actor, sec)
	for _, h in ipairs(list) do
		if left <= 0 then break end
		if not h.self and h.peer ~= rc then left = left - move_from(h, sec, left) end
	end
	-- an artefact asked for may sit in a container another player carries
	if left > 0 and sec:find("af_", 1, true) then
		for _, h in ipairs(list) do
			if left <= 0 then break end
			if not h.self then
				local c, cont = container_of(h, sec)
				if c then
					alife_release_id(c:id())
					create_plain(sec, db.actor)
					create_plain(cont, h.obj) -- the empty container stays with its owner
					left = left - 1
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

local function patch_party_items()
	local xe = rawget(_G, "xr_effects") or xr_effects
	if not xe then return end

	local remove_item = xe.remove_item
	if type(remove_item) == "function" then
		xe.remove_item = function(actor, npc, p)
			if not (world_active() and has_clients() and type(p) == "table" and type(p[1]) == "string") then
				return remove_item(actor, npc, p)
			end
			local amt = tonumber(p[2]) or 1
			if not rcpt_client() and count_items(db.actor, p[1]) >= amt then return remove_item(actor, npc, p) end
			local ok, err = pcall(party_remove, p[1], amt)
			if not ok then
				report("remove_item " .. p[1], err)
				return remove_item(actor, npc, p)
			end
		end
	end

	local remove_fetch = xe.remove_fetch_item
	if type(remove_fetch) == "function" then
		xe.remove_fetch_item = function(actor, npc, p)
			if not (world_active() and has_clients() and type(p) == "table" and p[1]) then return remove_fetch(actor, npc, p) end
			local sec = load_var(db.actor, p[1])
			if type(sec) ~= "string" then return remove_fetch(actor, npc, p) end
			local amt = tonumber(p[2]) or tonumber(load_var(db.actor, p[1] .. "_count")) or 1
			if not rcpt_client() and count_items(db.actor, sec) >= amt then return remove_fetch(actor, npc, p) end
			local ok, err = pcall(party_remove, sec, amt)
			if not ok then
				report("remove_fetch_item " .. sec, err)
				return remove_fetch(actor, npc, p)
			end
		end
	end

	local remove_art = xe.remove_artefact_item
	if type(remove_art) == "function" then
		-- true when one artefact (or its container) was taken from somebody in the group
		local function party_remove_art(sec)
			for _, h in ipairs(holders()) do
				if release_from(h, sec, 1) > 0 then
					news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, "out", sec, 1)
					return true
				end
				local c, cont = container_of(h, sec)
				if c then
					alife_release_id(c:id())
					create_plain(cont, h.obj) -- the empty container stays with its owner
					news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, "out", sec, 1)
					return true
				end
			end
			return false
		end
		xe.remove_artefact_item = function(actor, npc, p)
			if not (world_active() and has_clients() and type(p) == "table" and p[1]) then return remove_art(actor, npc, p) end
			local sec = load_var(db.actor, p[1])
			if type(sec) ~= "string" then return remove_art(actor, npc, p) end
			local mine = { obj = db.actor, self = true }
			if not rcpt_client() and (db.actor:object(sec) or container_of(mine, sec)) then return remove_art(actor, npc, p) end
			local ok, done = pcall(party_remove_art, sec)
			if not ok then report("remove_artefact_item " .. sec, done) end
			if ok and done then return end
			return remove_art(actor, npc, p)
		end
	end

	-- tasks_multifetch: its effects count and take through db.actor:iterate_inventory (the check is in coop_quests_party)
	for _, name in ipairs({ "multifetch_remove", "multifetch_task_trigger_extra_items_condlist" }) do
		local stock = xe[name]
		if type(stock) == "function" then
			xe[name] = function(...)
				local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
				local qp = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_party")
				if not (world_active() and has_clients() and db.actor and qc and type(qc.with_actor) == "function")
					or (qp and type(qp.checking_task) == "function" and qp.checking_task()) then
					return stock(...)
				end
				local fields = { iterate_inventory = party_inventory_walker(db.actor.iterate_inventory) }
				local res = { qc.with_actor(fields, stock, ...) }
				if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
				return unpack(res, 2)
			end
		end
	end

	local fetch_reward = xe.fetch_reward_and_remove
	if type(fetch_reward) == "function" then
		xe.fetch_reward_and_remove = function(actor, npc, p)
			if world_active() and has_clients() and type(p) == "table" and p[1] then
				local ok, err = pcall(gather_fetch, p[1])
				if not ok then report("fetch gather " .. tostring(p[1]), err) end
			end
			return fetch_reward(actor, npc, p)
		end
	end

	-- status functors: the task is ready to turn in when the group has the items
	local tsf = rawget(_G, "task_status_functor")
	if type(tsf) ~= "table" then
		log("! task_status_functor not found: quest items count only from the host's inventory")
		return
	end
	local function wrap_status(name, after)
		local orig = tsf[name]
		if type(orig) ~= "function" then return end
		tsf[name] = function(tsk, task_id)
			local r = orig(tsk, task_id)
			if r == nil and world_active() and has_clients() and tsk and tsk.stage ~= 1 then
				local ok, err = pcall(after, tsk, task_id)
				if not ok then report("status " .. name, err) end
			end
			return r
		end
	end
	wrap_status("actor_has_fetch_item", function(tsk, task_id)
		local n, need = host.fetch_units(task_id)
		if n and n >= need then
			tsk.stage = 1
			stats.stage_by_party = stats.stage_by_party + 1
		end
	end)
	wrap_status("actor_has_fetch_weapon_warfare", function(tsk, task_id)
		local sec = load_var(db.actor, task_id .. "_fetch")
		if type(sec) == "string" and party_count(sec, 0.6) > 0 then
			tsk.stage = 1
			stats.stage_by_party = stats.stage_by_party + 1
		end
	end)
	wrap_status("drx_sl_quest_item_task_status", function(tsk, task_id)
		local var = load_var(db.actor, task_id)
		if type(var) == "table" and var.stash_created and var.stash_type
			and party_count("drx_sl_quest_item_" .. tostring(var.stash_type)) > 0 then
			tsk.stage = 1
			stats.stage_by_party = stats.stage_by_party + 1
		end
	end)
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Client: mirrored task stubs
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
local cl = {
	recv = {}, -- id -> last state string from the host
	vars = {}, -- id -> { key = true } mirrored into our pstor
	synced = false,
	next_sync = 0,
	next_check = 0,
	full = nil, -- { gen, got, seen } the whole shared set while its parts arrive
	list = nil, -- { gen, got, listed, differ } the digest list while its parts arrive
	active = nil, -- the active task the host knows about
	want_active = nil, -- { id, at } a task this player asked for, to make active when it arrives
	fx_done = {}, -- q -> true: effects that ran here (a sync crossing the answer sends one again)
	lang_told = false,
	partner = nil, -- round 5: { id (host numbering), at } the NPC of this player's last talk (_talk_partner)
}

local client_request -- forward

local STUB_METHODS = {
	check_task = function() end,
	give_task = function() end,
	give_reward = function() end,
	reverse_task = function() end,
	deactivate_task = function() end,
	check_level = function() end,
	remove_guider_spot = function() end,
	save = function() end,
	load = function() end,
	load_state = function() return false end,
	get_title = function(self) return self.title or "" end,
	get_icon_name = function(self) return self.icon end,
	-- Saved like a real task, so a game saved from this world after the session (if ever) still knows it.
	save_state = function(self, m_data)
		if type(m_data) ~= "table" or type(m_data.task_objects) ~= "table" then return end
		m_data.task_objects[self.id] = {
			status = self.status, stage = self.stage, task_giver_id = self.task_giver_id,
		}
	end,
}

local function stub_data(t)
	if type(t) ~= "table" then return nil end
	local mt = getmetatable(t)
	return type(mt) == "table" and mt.__coop_data or nil
end

local function engine_task(id)
	local a = db and db.actor
	if not a then return nil end
	local ok, t = pcall(a.get_task, a, id, true)
	return ok and t or nil
end

local function task_is_story(id)
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	local ini = mod and mod.task_ini
	local ok, v = pcall(function() return ini:r_bool_ex(id, "storyline", false) end)
	return ok and v == true
end

-- What a real task object has and a stub can answer from the engine's copy (the GAMMA task monitor and HUD marks read them).
-- The engine's task type has no getter in Lua: the storyline flag comes from the task's config, as in CGeneralTask.
local STUB_FIELDS = {
	t = function(data) return engine_task(data.id) end,
	current_target = function(data)
		local t = engine_task(data.id)
		local ok, oid = pcall(function() return t and t:get_map_object_id() end)
		return ok and type(oid) == "number" and oid ~= 65535 and oid or nil
	end,
	storyline = function(data) return task_is_story(data.id) end,
}

-- A dialog script writing a stub field the host owns: the host does it.
local function on_stub_write(data, k, v)
	if not client_live() then return end
	if k == "stage" and type(v) == "number" then
		client_request("stage", data.id, { st = v })
	elseif k == "forced_status" and (v == "complete" or v == "fail") then
		client_request(v == "complete" and "complete" or "fail", data.id)
	elseif k == "cancelled_by_actor" and v == true then
		client_request("cancel", data.id)
	end
end

local function new_stub(id)
	local data = { id = id, coop_stub = true, stage = 0, status = "selected" }
	local mt = { __coop_data = data }
	mt.__index = function(_, k)
		local v = data[k]
		if v ~= nil then return v end
		local f = STUB_FIELDS[k]
		if f then return f(data) end
		return STUB_METHODS[k]
	end
	mt.__newindex = function(_, k, v)
		local old = data[k]
		data[k] = v
		if old ~= v then
			local ok, err = pcall(on_stub_write, data, k, v)
			if not ok then report("stub write", err) end
		end
	end
	return setmetatable({}, mt), data
end

local function clear_vars(id, keep)
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	local old = cl.vars[id]
	cl.vars[id] = nil
	if ps and old then
		for k in pairs(old) do
			local held = keep and keep[k] ~= nil
			for _, keys in pairs(cl.vars) do held = held or keys[k] == true end -- "a_b_x" is also a var of task "a_b"
			if not held then ps[k] = nil end
		end
	end
end

local function apply_vars(id, vars)
	clear_vars(id, vars)
	local ps = actor_pstor(true)
	if not ps then return end
	local keys = {}
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		if is_task_key(k, id) then
			ps[k] = v
			keys[k] = true
		end
	end
	cl.vars[id] = keys
end

-- The items of a multifetch task, for the stock inventory marks (fetch_item_icon reads alife_storage_manager's state,
-- on a client the join save's). tasks_multifetch keeps them in a local table; they come from the task's config, the same
-- on every machine.
local function multifetch_items(ini, id, kind)
	local out = {}
	local i = 1
	while ini:line_exist(id, kind .. "_item_" .. i) do
		out[i] = { sec = ini:r_string_ex(id, kind .. "_item_" .. i) }
		i = i + 1
	end
	return out
end

local function mirror_multifetch(id, on)
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	local ini = mod and mod.task_ini
	local asm = rawget(_G, "alife_storage_manager") or alife_storage_manager
	if not (ini and asm and asm.get_state) then return end
	local st = asm.get_state()
	if type(st) ~= "table" then return end
	if not on then
		if type(st.multifetch_data) == "table" then st.multifetch_data[id] = nil end
		return
	end
	if ini:r_string_ex(id, "status_functor") ~= "multifetch_status_functor" then return end
	st.multifetch_data = st.multifetch_data or {}
	st.multifetch_data[id] = { required_items = multifetch_items(ini, id, "required"),
		optional_items = multifetch_items(ini, id, "optional") }
end

local function forget_task(tm, id)
	tm.task_info[id] = nil
	cl.recv[id] = nil
	clear_vars(id)
	local ok, err = pcall(mirror_multifetch, id, false)
	if not ok then report("multifetch " .. id, err) end
end

-- The infos of the dialog phrase that asked for a task. The engine runs a phrase's actions first and gives its <give_info> after
-- them, in the same frame (CDialogScriptHelper::Action): an info the actor gets in the frame of a give asked from a talk is the
-- phrase's, and it is kept with the provisional stub.
function _client_on_info(npc, info)
	local a = cl.asking
	if not a or a.at ~= now() or type(info) ~= "string" then return end
	for _, data in ipairs(a.stubs) do
		local list = data.phrase_infos
		if list and #list < 8 then list[#list + 1] = info end
	end
end

-- The host could not give the task this player asked for ("The Last Dawn", 2026-11-13: the give died in the task's on_init, the stub
-- vanished in silence). The player is told. The infos of the phrase that asked are taken back: a dialog closed by its own info
-- (dont_has_info) would never offer the task again, to anybody. The engine carries the removal to the host and the others.
function _client_not_given(id, data)
	log("! the host could not give task '%s'", id)
	for _, info in ipairs(data.phrase_infos or {}) do
		if db.actor and db.actor:has_info(info) then
			db.actor:disable_info_portion(info)
			log("info '%s' of the phrase that asked for '%s' is taken back", info, id)
		end
	end
	local am = rawget(_G, "actor_menu")
	if type(am) == "table" and type(am.set_msg) == "function" then
		am.set_msg(1, game.translate_string("st_coop_news_task_not_given"), 8)
	end
end

-- Client: the NPC this player talks to now, in host numbering, or nil. Round 5 (S4 of the round 4 review): else the NPC of his
-- last talk, while the host's window lasts (_spoke_to: 15 s from its end). z_gavrilenko_tasks_fix turns a task in 1 s after the
-- dialog opens, which may be closed by then. Noted at each look and when the dialog window opens and closes (on_game_start).
function _talk_partner()
	local sid = nil
	if db.actor and db.actor:is_talking() and type(rawget(_G, "get_speaker")) == "function" then
		local ok, npc = pcall(get_speaker)
		sid = ok and npc and npc.id and npc:id() or nil
	end
	if type(sid) == "number" and sid ~= 0 then
		cl.partner = { id = to_host_id(sid), at = now() }
		return cl.partner.id
	end
	local p = cl.partner
	if p and now() - p.at <= 15000 then return p.id end
	return nil
end

-- Client (TZ 6.4 #1 round 2, F5): the host refused this player's fail / cancel of a task another player took. The news line
-- names who can. The format is this machine's text; the nick from the network goes in only as an argument.
function _client_only_taker(t)
	local nick = type(t.n) == "string" and t.n:gsub("%c", ""):sub(1, 64) or ""
	local id = nick ~= "" and "st_coop_task_only_taker" or "st_coop_task_only_taker_anon"
	local text = game.translate_string(id)
	if nick ~= "" then
		local ok, line = pcall(string_format, text, nick)
		text = ok and line or text
	end
	local caption = game.translate_string("st_coop_task_only_taker_caption")
	log("! the host refused our end of task '%s': only %s may end it", tostring(t.t), nick ~= "" and nick or "its taker")
	local ok = pcall(function() db.actor:give_game_news(caption, text, "ui_iconsTotal_storyline", 0, 6000) end)
	if not ok then
		local am = rawget(_G, "actor_menu")
		if type(am) == "table" and type(am.set_msg) == "function" then am.set_msg(1, text, 6) end
	end
end

local function client_apply_state(s)
	local rec = unpack_payload(s)
	local id = rec.i
	if type(id) ~= "string" or id == "" or is_local(id) then return end
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm or type(tm.task_info) ~= "table" then return end
	stats.state_in = stats.state_in + 1
	if rec.d then
		local asked = stub_data(tm.task_info[id])
		local not_given = rec.r ~= nil and asked ~= nil and asked.pending_at ~= nil
		forget_task(tm, id)
		if not_given then
			local ok, err = pcall(_client_not_given, id, asked)
			if not ok then report("not given " .. id, err) end
		end
		return
	end
	cl.recv[id] = s
	local stub = tm.task_info[id]
	local data = stub_data(stub)
	if not data then
		stub, data = new_stub(id) -- also replaces a task object this machine loaded with the join save
		local ok, err = pcall(mirror_multifetch, id, true)
		if not ok then report("multifetch " .. id, err) end
	end
	local status = rec.s or "selected"
	local opt = data.optimistic
	if opt and status ~= "completed" and status ~= "fail" and now() - opt.at < PENDING_MS then
		status = data.status -- our turn-in is on its way: do not offer it again meanwhile
	else
		data.optimistic = nil
	end
	data.stage = rec.st or 0 -- a record built after an error has no stage, dialogs compare it
	data.status = status
	data.task_giver_id = rec.g and to_local_id(rec.g) or nil
	data.pending_at = nil
	tm.task_info[id] = stub
	if not rec.nv then apply_vars(id, type(rec.v) == "string" and unpack_payload(rec.v) or {}) end
	local b = bounties()
	if b and type(rec.bt) == "number" then b[id] = to_local_id(rec.bt) end
end

-- A part of the whole set (_f = number of the set, part _p of _n) or the keys that changed. "-key" = removed, "+key" = in the
-- set but too long to send. Only a whole set says what the host does not have: the last part drops the other keys.
local function client_apply_shared(payload)
	local vars = unpack_payload(payload)
	local ps = actor_pstor(true)
	if not ps then return end
	local gen = tonumber(vars._f)
	local full = cl.full
	if gen and not (full and full.gen == gen) then
		full = { gen = gen, got = 0, seen = {} }
		cl.full = full
	end
	if gen then full.got = full.got + 1 end
	for k, v in pairs(vars) do
		local mark = k:sub(1, 1)
		local key = (mark == "-" or mark == "+") and k:sub(2) or k
		if is_shared_key(key) then
			if mark == "-" then
				ps[key] = nil
			elseif mark ~= "+" then
				ps[key] = v
			end
			if gen and mark ~= "-" then full.seen[key] = true end
		end
	end
	if gen and vars._p == vars._n and full.got == vars._n then
		cl.full = nil
		local drop = {}
		for k in pairs(ps) do
			if is_shared_key(k) and not full.seen[k] then drop[#drop + 1] = k end
		end
		for _, k in ipairs(drop) do ps[k] = nil end
	end
end

-- save_var on this client's actor for a shared key: the host keeps the group's value.
local function client_route_var(k, v)
	local ps = actor_pstor(false)
	local old = ps and ps[k]
	local t = { k = k }
	if v == nil then
		t.op = "del"
	elseif type(v) == "number" and (old == nil or type(old) == "number") and k:sub(1, #COUNTER_PREFIX) == COUNTER_PREFIX then
		t.op, t.d = "add", v - (old or 0)
		if t.d == 0 then return end
	elseif var_value_ok(v) then
		t.op, t.v = "set", v
	else
		return
	end
	send(EV_VAR, pack(t, true), 0)
end

local function client_request_sync()
	cl.next_sync = now() + SYNC_RETRY_MS
	send(EV_SYNC, "", 0)
end

local function client_on_list(payload)
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm or type(tm.task_info) ~= "table" then return end
	local gen, part, parts, items = tostring(payload):match("^(%d+)/(%d+)/(%d+)|(.*)$")
	gen, part, parts = tonumber(gen), tonumber(part), tonumber(parts)
	if not (gen and part and parts) then return end
	local list = cl.list
	if not (list and list.gen == gen) then
		list = { gen = gen, got = 0, listed = {}, differ = false }
		cl.list = list
	end
	list.got = list.got + 1
	for item in items:gmatch("[^,]+") do
		local k, d = item:match("^([^:]*):(.*)$")
		if k then
			k = unesc(k)
			list.listed[k] = true
			local mine = cl.recv[k]
			if not mine or digest(mine) ~= d then list.differ = true end
		end
	end
	if part ~= parts or list.got ~= parts then return end -- a part went missing: this list says nothing
	cl.list = nil
	stats.lists = stats.lists + 1
	local listed, differ = list.listed, list.differ
	local drop = {}
	for id, tsk in pairs(tm.task_info) do
		if not listed[id] and not is_local(id) then
			local data = stub_data(tsk)
			if not (data and data.pending_at and now() - data.pending_at < PENDING_MS) then drop[#drop + 1] = id end
		end
	end
	for _, id in ipairs(drop) do forget_task(tm, id) end
	cl.synced = true
	if differ and now() >= cl.next_sync then client_request_sync() end
end

client_request = function(op, id, extra)
	if type(id) ~= "string" then return false end
	local t = extra or {}
	t.op, t.i = op, id
	-- TZ 6.4 #1 round 2 (F5): a fail / cancel names the NPC this player talks to (the host lets a choice in a dialog with the
	-- task's giver through, after its own look at the talk); round 3 (R2-S2): a stage write too (a step is a dialog's); round 4
	-- (S1): a turn-in too (check task_complete_talk)
	if (op == "fail" or op == "cancel" or op == "stage" or op == "complete") and t.sp == nil then t.sp = _talk_partner() end
	local ok = send(EV_REQ, pack(t), 0)
	if ok then stats.req_out = stats.req_out + 1 end
	return ok
end

local function client_give(tm, id, giver)
	local gid = tonumber(giver)
	local extra = { g = gid and to_host_id(gid) or nil }
	local v = pack(task_vars(id), true)
	if #v > 9000 then
		log("! task vars of '%s' too long (%d characters), the host keeps its own", id, #v)
		v = ""
	end
	if v ~= "" then extra.v = v end
	local b = bounties()
	if b and type(b[id]) == "number" then extra.bt = to_host_id(b[id]) end
	if db.actor and db.actor:is_talking() and type(rawget(_G, "get_speaker")) == "function" then
		local ok, npc = pcall(get_speaker) -- whom this player talks to: the host's on_init of the task may ask for him
		local sid = ok and npc and npc.id and npc:id() or nil
		if type(sid) == "number" and sid ~= 0 then extra.sp = to_host_id(sid) end
	end
	if not client_request("give", id, extra) then return false end
	local stub, data = new_stub(id)
	data.task_giver_id = gid
	data.pending_at = now()
	if db.actor and db.actor:is_talking() then -- asked by a phrase: its infos go with the stub (client_on_info)
		data.phrase_infos = {}
		local a = cl.asking
		if not (a and a.at == now()) then
			a = { at = now(), stubs = {} }
			cl.asking = a
		end
		a.stubs[#a.stubs + 1] = data
	end
	tm.task_info[id] = stub
	cl.want_active = { id = id, at = now() }
	log("asked the host for task '%s'", id)
	return true
end

local function client_finish(tm, id, op)
	if not client_request(op, id) then return false end
	local data = stub_data(tm.task_info[id])
	if data and data.status ~= "completed" and data.status ~= "fail" then
		data.optimistic = { at = now(), status = data.status }
		data.status = op == "complete" and "completed" or "fail"
	end
	log("%s '%s' sent to the host", op, id)
	return true
end

-- The task this actor has as its active one (task_info holds every running task), id and engine task.
local function active_task(tm)
	local actor = db and db.actor
	if not actor then return nil end
	for id in pairs(tm.task_info) do
		local et = engine_task(id)
		if et then
			local ok, on = pcall(actor.is_active_task, actor, et)
			if ok and on == true then return id, et end
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- A task this player took becomes his active one when the engine's copy arrives (a copy for somebody else's task leaves
-- it alone: coop_story apply_record). The host hears about the active task: the guide marker of a target on another level
-- is added by the host's task objects.
local function client_active_tick(tm, t)
	local want = cl.want_active
	if want then
		local et = engine_task(want.id)
		if et then
			pcall(db.actor.set_active_task, db.actor, et)
			cl.want_active = nil
		elseif t - want.at >= PENDING_MS then
			cl.want_active = nil
		end
	end
	local id = active_task(tm)
	if id ~= cl.active then
		if id then
			client_request("active", id)
		elseif cl.active then
			client_request("active", cl.active, { off = true })
		end
		cl.active = id
	end
end

local function client_tick()
	local t = now()
	if not cl.synced and t >= cl.next_sync then client_request_sync() end
	if t < cl.next_check then return end
	cl.next_check = t + 1000
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not tm or type(tm.task_info) ~= "table" then return end
	local ok, err = pcall(client_active_tick, tm, t)
	if not ok then report("active task", err) end
	local stale = false
	for _, tsk in pairs(tm.task_info) do
		local data = stub_data(tsk)
		if data then
			if data.pending_at and t - data.pending_at >= PENDING_MS then
				data.pending_at = nil
				stale = true
			end
			local opt = data.optimistic
			if opt and t - opt.at >= PENDING_MS then
				data.status = opt.status
				data.optimistic = nil
				stale = true
			end
		end
	end
	if stale and t >= cl.next_sync then client_request_sync() end
end

-- Host events for this player
local function apply_stat(t)
	local gs = rawget(_G, "game_statistics") or game_statistics
	if type(gs) ~= "table" then return end
	if t.f == "rank" then
		gs.increment_rank(tonumber(t.n) or 0)
	elseif t.f == "rept" then
		gs.increment_reputation(tonumber(t.n) or 0)
	elseif type(t.f) == "string" then
		gs.increment_statistic(t.f, tonumber(t.r), tonumber(t.p))
	end
end

local function client_on_reward(payload, from)
	if from ~= 0 or not mirrors_tasks() then return end
	if not db.actor then
		cl.synced = false -- an effect in this event is sent again on the next sync
		return
	end
	local t = unpack_payload(payload)
	local q = type(t.q) == "number" and t.q or nil
	if q and cl.fx_done[q] then
		send(EV_ACK, tostring(q), 0)
		return
	end
	stats.rewards_in = stats.rewards_in + 1
	if t.k == "mn" and type(t.n) == "number" then
		-- the money itself is the host's (coop.money_grant, shown with the engine's balance): only the news line here
		local n = t.n >= 0 and math_floor(t.n) or -math_floor(-t.n)
		if n ~= 0 then news_manager.relocate_money(db.actor, n > 0 and "in" or "out", n > 0 and n or -n) end
	elseif t.k == "news" and type(t.s) == "string" then
		news_manager.relocate_item(db.actor, t.ty == "out" and "out" or "in", t.s, tonumber(t.n) or 1)
	elseif t.k == "only" then
		_client_only_taker(t)
	elseif t.k == "away" then
		-- what the group's rewards brought while this player was out of the game (coop_reward_group)
		local nw, rg = news_mod(), reward_group()
		if nw and nw.show_rewards and rg then
			nw.show_rewards(tonumber(t.c) or 0, tonumber(t.m) or 0, rg.parse_items(t.i), tonumber(t.x) or 0)
		end
	elseif t.k == "gw" and type(t.c) == "string" then
		local mlr = rawget(_G, "dialogs_mlr") or dialogs_mlr
		if mlr and mlr.show_goodwill_change_message then mlr.show_goodwill_change_message(t.c, nil, nil, t.g == true) end
	elseif t.k == "fx" and type(t.f) == "string" and FORWARD_EFFECTS[t.f] then
		local f = xr_effects and xr_effects[t.f]
		-- coop_faction tells the world's forwarded effect from this machine's own calls (split levels: only this one changes it)
		local cf = _G.coop_faction
		local run = type(cf) == "table" and type(cf.run_forwarded) == "function" and cf.run_forwarded
		if type(f) == "function" and run then run(f, db.actor, nil, { t.p1, t.p2, t.p3, t.p4 })
		elseif type(f) == "function" then f(db.actor, nil, { t.p1, t.p2, t.p3, t.p4 }) end
	elseif t.k == "stat" then
		apply_stat(t)
	elseif t.k == "lang" then
		-- texts of tasks are final strings of the host's language: said once, at the first sync
		if type(t.l) == "string" and not cl.lang_told and game.translate_string("general_new_task") ~= t.l then
			cl.lang_told = true
			local nw = news_mod()
			if nw and nw.show_language then nw.show_language() end
		end
	end
	if q then
		cl.fx_done[q] = true
		send(EV_ACK, tostring(q), 0)
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Messages of the shared journal (docs\MESSAGES.md)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The stock lines "New task" / "Task updated" / "Task completed" / "Task failed" / "Task reversed" are
-- news_manager.send_task. The host's scripts call it ("new" and "complete" from the actor's task callback the engine fires
-- for a state it sets itself, "fail" from task_manager.task_callback, "updated" / "reversed" from the task objects). On a
-- client the engine applies the host's copy of a task silently (a finished one without any callback) and fires the callback
-- for a new one once, so the client's own send_task is dropped for a group task and the host's call is sent to every
-- client instead, as event coop_tn: kind, task id, title, icon and the player who caused it. One line per event per
-- machine. The line the one who did it sees is the stock one; the others see "<nick> took a task" and so on
-- (coop_quests_news.show_task), the host included when a client did it.
local NEWS_KINDS = { new = true, updated = true, complete = true, fail = true, reversed = true }
local NEWS_NICK_KINDS = { new = true, complete = true, fail = true } -- updated / reversed: nobody did it
local NEWS_DEDUP_MS = { updated = 3000 }
local NEWS_DEDUP_DEFAULT_MS = 1500
local NEWS_LIMIT, NEWS_WINDOW_MS, NEWS_SEEN_MAX = 20, 10000, 200 -- lines a machine takes / sends in a window
local news_out_win = { at = 0, n = 0 }
local news_in_win = { at = 0, n = 0 }
local orig_send_task = nil -- news_manager.send_task as it was before the wrapper


local function nick_of(peer)
	for _, p in ipairs(players()) do
		if p.id == peer and type(p.nick) == "string" and p.nick ~= "" then return p.nick end
	end
	return "#" .. tostring(peer)
end

local function cut(s, n)
	s = type(s) == "string" and s or ""
	if #s > n then s = s:sub(1, n) end
	return s
end

local function window_ok(win)
	local t = now()
	if t - win.at >= NEWS_WINDOW_MS or t < win.at then win.at, win.n = t, 0 end
	if win.n >= NEWS_LIMIT then return false end
	win.n = win.n + 1
	return true
end

local function task_id_of(tsk)
	local ok, id = pcall(function() return tsk:get_id() end)
	if ok and type(id) == "string" and id ~= "" then return id end
	return nil
end

local function task_text(tsk)
	local title, icon
	pcall(function() title = tsk:get_title() end)
	pcall(function() icon = tsk:get_icon_name() end)
	return type(title) == "string" and title or "", (type(icon) == "string" and icon ~= "") and icon or nil
end

-- Host: the player whose action caused this event (a peer, 0 = the host), or nil: nobody (a script, a timer).
-- Second value: a "fail" the player asked for (cancel).
local function event_actor(kind, id)
	if kind == "new" then return host.given_by[id], false end
	if kind == "complete" then
		local by = ctx and ctx.task == id and ctx.by or nil
		if by == nil then by = host.finisher[id] end
		if by == nil then by = host.given_by[id] end -- a script completed it: the one who took it
		return by, false
	end
	if kind == "fail" then
		if ctx and ctx.task == id then return ctx.by, ctx.cancelled == true end
		local tm = tmgr()
		local rtask = tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id]
		return host.finisher[id], is_task(rtask) and rtask.cancelled_by_actor == true
	end
	return nil, false
end

-- Host: the event to every client (deduped, limited). False if it was not sent.
local function news_out(kind, id, title, icon, by, cancelled, story)
	local key = kind .. " " .. id
	local t = now()
	local last = host.news_seen[key]
	if last and t >= last and t - last < (NEWS_DEDUP_MS[kind] or NEWS_DEDUP_DEFAULT_MS) then return false end
	if not window_ok(news_out_win) then
		stats.news_limited = stats.news_limited + 1
		return false
	end
	if host.news_count >= NEWS_SEEN_MAX then host.news_seen, host.news_count = {}, 0 end
	if host.news_seen[key] == nil then host.news_count = host.news_count + 1 end
	host.news_seen[key] = t
	local rec = { k = kind, i = id, ti = cut(title, 160), ic = icon and cut(icon, 100) or nil }
	if by ~= nil then
		rec.by = by
		rec.n = cut(nick_of(by), 32)
	end
	if cancelled then rec.c = true end
	if story then rec.sl = true end
	host.send_task(EV_NEWS, pack(rec), id) -- a task with an audience: only to it
	stats.news_out = stats.news_out + 1
	return true
end

-- Host, a send_task call: the event to the clients; true if the host's own line was shown here (the nick variant for
-- a client's action), false to let the stock line follow.
local function host_news(kind, tsk)
	local id = task_id_of(tsk)
	if not id or is_local(id) then return false end
	local by, cancelled = event_actor(kind, id)
	local title, icon = task_text(tsk)
	news_out(kind, id, title, icon, by, cancelled, kind == "new" and task_is_story(id))
	if not host.aud_sees(id, 0) then return true end -- the host player is out of the task's audience: no line here
	if by ~= nil and by ~= 0 and NEWS_NICK_KINDS[kind] then
		local n = news_mod()
		if n and n.show_task then return n.show_task(kind, title, icon, nick_of(by), cancelled) == true end
	end
	return false
end

function news_actor(kind, id)
	if not world_active() or type(id) ~= "string" then return nil, false end
	return event_actor(kind, id)
end

local function wrap_send_task(orig)
	return function(actor, kind, tsk, ...)
		if NEWS_KINDS[kind] then
			if mirrors_tasks() then
				local id = task_id_of(tsk)
				if id and not is_local(id) then
					stats.news_swallowed = stats.news_swallowed + 1
					return true -- the host's event carries the group's line
				end
			elseif world_active() and has_clients() then
				local ok, shown = pcall(host_news, kind, tsk)
				if not ok then
					report("task news", shown)
				elseif shown then
					return true
				end
			elseif world_active() and not host.aud_sees(task_id_of(tsk), 0) then
				return true -- alone in the game and out of the task's audience: no line
			end
		end
		return orig(actor, kind, tsk, ...)
	end
end

-- Client: the stock line for a task the host announced (the stock function gets a stand-in for the engine task).
local function show_stock(kind, id, title, icon)
	local send_task = orig_send_task
	if not send_task then
		local nm = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
		send_task = nm and nm.send_task
	end
	if type(send_task) ~= "function" then return end
	local stand_in = { id = id }
	function stand_in.get_id() return id end
	function stand_in.get_title() return title end
	function stand_in.get_icon_name() return icon end
	local ok, err = pcall(send_task, db.actor, kind, stand_in)
	if not ok then
		-- a mod's override of the stock function failed (e.g. in a dialog): the line is still shown
		report("task line " .. kind .. " " .. id, err)
		local n = news_mod()
		if n and n.show_plain then n.show_plain(kind, title, icon) end
	end
end

local function client_on_news(payload, from)
	if from ~= 0 or not client_live() or not db.actor then return end
	local t = unpack_payload(payload)
	local kind, id = t.k, t.i
	if not NEWS_KINDS[kind] or type(id) ~= "string" or id == "" or #id > 128 or is_local(id) then return end
	if not window_ok(news_in_win) then
		stats.news_limited = stats.news_limited + 1
		return
	end
	stats.news_in = stats.news_in + 1
	local title = cut(t.ti, 160)
	local icon = (type(t.ic) == "string" and t.ic ~= "") and cut(t.ic, 100) or nil
	local by = tonumber(t.by)
	local n = news_mod()
	-- the storyline fade: the host's task object shows it in its constructor, a client has only stubs
	if t.sl == true and kind == "new" and n and n.show_story then n.show_story(title) end
	if by ~= nil and by ~= self_peer() and NEWS_NICK_KINDS[kind] then
		local nick = type(t.n) == "string" and t.n ~= "" and t.n or nick_of(by)
		if n and n.show_task and n.show_task(kind, title, icon, nick, t.c == true) then return end
	end
	show_stock(kind, id, title, icon)
end

local function patch_task_news()
	local nm = rawget(_G, "news_manager") or news_manager
	if not (nm and type(nm.send_task) == "function") then
		log("! news_manager.send_task not found: the group gets no task lines")
		return
	end
	orig_send_task = nm.send_task
	nm.send_task = wrap_send_task(orig_send_task)
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- task_manager patches (installed once, host.patched; every wrapper checks the role when called)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
host.patched = false

-- Host: the player a task given by a script belongs to: the one nearest to its giver, or to the zone of the effect that gave
-- it. A task nothing locates stays the host's. (A field of `host`, not a local: the chunk is at Lua's limit.)
function host.nearest_taker(giver)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if not (type(qc) == "table" and qc.nearest_character) then return 0 end
	local pos, gv
	local function place_of(o)
		local ok, p = pcall(function() return o:position() end)
		local ok2, v = pcall(function() return o:game_vertex_id() end)
		return ok and p or nil, ok2 and type(v) == "number" and v or nil
	end
	local near = host.give_near
	if near then pos, gv = place_of(near) end
	if not pos and type(giver) == "number" then
		local o = level.object_by_id(giver)
		if o then
			pos, gv = place_of(o)
		else
			local se = rawget(_G, "alife_object") and alife_object(giver)
			pos, gv = se and se.position or nil, se and se.m_game_vertex_id or nil
		end
	end
	-- A seat that plays no character: its ghost takes no task. With nobody to measure to (a script gave it with no giver:
	-- operacia_monolith's PDA in the group's inventory), or nobody on that level, a player of the world takes it, the one
	-- who has been in it longest (the lowest peer): rewards written on the ghost were nobody's.
	local function anybody()
		if coop_mode.actor_is_player() or not qc.bodies then return 0 end
		local first
		for _, c in ipairs(qc.bodies()) do
			if type(c.peer) == "number" and c.peer ~= 0 and (not first or c.peer < first) then first = c.peer end
		end
		return first or 0
	end
	if not pos then return anybody() end
	-- Split levels: only a player of that level is next to it; the world server's own characters are not all there is, and the
	-- coordinates of two levels do not compare (the quest audit, 2026-11-13: a task given by logic was written on the ghost).
	local _, peer
	if qc.nearest_body then
		_, peer = qc.nearest_body({ position = pos, m_game_vertex_id = gv })
	else
		_, peer = qc.nearest_character(pos)
	end
	if not peer or peer == 0 then return anybody() end
	return peer
end

local function patch_method(name, make)
	local tm = tmgr()
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	local cls = mod and mod.CRandomTask
	if cls then
		local ok, f = pcall(function() return cls[name] end)
		if ok and type(f) == "function" then
			local w = make(f)
			local set_ok = pcall(function() cls[name] = w end)
			local read_ok, back = pcall(function() return cls[name] end)
			if set_ok and read_ok and back == w then return true end
		end
	end
	if tm then -- the class is not reachable: patch the manager object itself
		local ok, f = pcall(function() return tm[name] end)
		if ok and type(f) == "function" then
			local w = make(f)
			if pcall(function() tm[name] = w end) then return true end
		end
	end
	log("! task_manager:%s could not be patched", name)
	return false
end

local function patch_task_manager()
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_manager") or task_manager
	if not mod then
		log("! task_manager not found: tasks are not shared in Lua")
		return
	end

	patch_method("give_task", function(orig)
		return function(self, id, giver, ...)
			if is_local(id) then return orig(self, id, giver, ...) end
			if mirrors_tasks() then
				if not client_live() then return end -- loading the host's world: the host has it already
				local ok, res = pcall(client_give, self, id, giver)
				if ok and res then return end
				report("give " .. tostring(id), ok and "send failed" or res)
				return
			end
			if world_active() and type(id) == "string" then
				-- split levels: may this player take it (coop_conditions_stock.may_take)? A give for a player - his Lua request (ops.give
				-- asked already) or the engine's TaskReqGive (coop_story.cpp host_on_task_give: lua_note "taker", then this) - is
				-- asked before anything of it is made; a script's give for nobody is not the storyline's to refuse.
				if (host.exec_peer or host.taker_note[id]) and host.take_asked ~= id then
					local sl = rawget(_G, "coop_conditions_stock")
					local okm, may = true, true
					if type(sl) == "table" and type(sl.may_take) == "function" then
						okm, may = pcall(sl.may_take, id, host.exec_peer or host.taker_note[id])
					end
					if okm and may == false then
						log("#%s may not take '%s': another faction's main story or a second change-faction task",
							tostring(host.exec_peer or host.taker_note[id]), id)
						host.taker_note[id] = nil
						return
					end
				end
				-- news: a player's action gave it (a request, the host's own dialog, the reward of a player's task)
				local who = host.exec_peer or host.taker_note[id]
				if who == nil and ctx and ctx.rcpt ~= nil and ctx.rcpt ~= 0 then who = ctx.rcpt end
				if who == nil and host_talking() then who = 0 end
				host.given_by[id] = who
				-- a follow-up task given by a reward belongs to the player who earned it
				host.taker[id] = host.exec_peer or host.taker_note[id] or (ctx and ctx.rcpt) or 0
				if who == nil and ctx == nil and has_clients() then host.taker[id] = host.nearest_taker(giver) end
				host.taker_note[id] = nil
				host.finisher[id] = nil
				host.taker_char[id] = character_of(host.taker[id])
				host.participants[id] = reward_mode() >= EVERYONE_SHARED and participant_ids() or nil
				host.failure_participants[id] = participant_ids()
				host.rep_party[id] = participant_ids()
				-- split levels: who sees the task, decided now, before the stock give, so its first message already goes by it
				local aud = task_audience()
				if aud and aud.on_give then
					local ok, err = pcall(aud.on_give, id, giver, host.taker_char[id])
					if not ok then report("task audience " .. id, err) end
				end
				-- the engine makes every new task the active one: a task another player took leaves the host's alone
				local keep = nil
				if host.taker[id] ~= 0 then keep = select(2, active_task(self)) end
				local prev_ctx = ctx
				if ctx == nil then
					-- W5: on_init (start items, PDAs) is the taker's, not a story reward for the whole group
					local t = host.taker[id]
					ctx = { task = id, rcpt = t, character = host.taker_char[id], share = false }
				end
				local res = { pcall(orig, self, id, giver, ...) }
				ctx = prev_ctx
				if keep then pcall(db.actor.set_active_task, db.actor, keep) end
				if not res[1] then error(res[2], 0) end
				return unpack(res, 2)
			end
			return orig(self, id, giver, ...)
		end
	end)

	for name, op in pairs({ set_task_completed = "complete", set_task_failed = "fail", set_task_cancelled = "cancel" }) do
		patch_method(name, function(orig)
			return function(self, id, ...)
				if is_local(id) then return orig(self, id, ...) end
				if mirrors_tasks() then
					if client_live() then
						local ok, err = pcall(client_finish, self, id, op)
						if not ok then report(name .. " " .. tostring(id), err) end
					end
					return
				end
				if world_active() and type(id) == "string" and host.finisher[id] == nil then
					-- a client's request, or the host turning it in in a dialog; a script completing it on
					-- its own leaves the reward to the player who took the task
					if host.exec_peer then
						host.finisher[id] = host.exec_peer
					elseif host_talking() then
						host.finisher[id] = 0
					end
				end
				return orig(self, id, ...)
			end
		end)
	end

	-- A client never evaluates the group's tasks: the host's scripts do, its state is mirrored here.
	-- Personal tasks are checked where they are.
	patch_method("update", function(orig)
		return function(self, ...)
			if mirrors_tasks() then
				if next(local_tasks) and type(self.task_info) == "table" then
					for id, tsk in pairs(self.task_info) do
						if is_local(id) and not stub_data(tsk) and type(tsk.check_task) == "function" then
							local ok, err = pcall(tsk.check_task, tsk, self)
							if not ok then report("local task " .. id, err) end
						end
					end
				end
				return
			end
			return orig(self, ...)
		end
	end)
	for _, name in ipairs({ "task_complete", "task_fail" }) do
		patch_method(name, function(orig)
			return function(self, id, ...)
				if mirrors_tasks() and not is_local(id) then return false end
				return orig(self, id, ...)
			end
		end)
		local f = mod[name]
		if type(f) == "function" then
			mod[name] = function(id, ...)
				if mirrors_tasks() and not is_local(id) then return false end
				return f(id, ...)
			end
		end
	end

	local cb = mod.task_callback
	if type(cb) == "function" then
		mod.task_callback = function(tsk, state)
			if mirrors_tasks() then
				local ok, id = pcall(function() return tsk:get_id() end)
				if ok and is_local(id) then return cb(tsk, state) end
				return -- results come from the host (silently, see coop_story)
			end
			if world_active() then return host_task_callback(cb, tsk, state) end
			return cb(tsk, state)
		end
	end
end

-- Guide markers (a target on another level): the host's task objects add them for the host's active task only. The same
-- check runs for each client's active task, and the marker of a target somebody still needs stays when the host's own target
-- is on this level. The markers are the group's, a client sees those of the others too. A player on a map server's level has
-- his on the exits of his level: the check looks from there (far view); the stock spot goes to him through coop_story.
-- (Both modes: in the co-op the clients' active tasks get their markers here too. S5 (A-S5T): fields of `host`, not locals.)
function host.target_elsewhere(target)
	local ok, yes = pcall(function()
		local se = alife_object(target)
		if not se then return false end
		return alife():level_name(game_graph():vertex(se.m_game_vertex_id):level_id()) ~= level.name()
	end)
	return ok and yes == true
end

function host.guide_wanted()
	local tm = tmgr()
	if not (tm and type(tm.task_info) == "table") then return false end
	for _, id in pairs(host.active) do
		local rt = tm.task_info[id]
		if is_task(rt) and rt.current_target ~= nil and host.target_elsewhere(rt.current_target) then return true end
	end
	return false
end

function host.guides()
	local tm = tmgr()
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if not (next(host.active) and tm and type(tm.task_info) == "table" and type(qc) == "table" and qc.with_actor) then return end
	local fields = { is_active_task = function() return true end }
	for peer, id in pairs(host.active) do
		local rt = tm.task_info[id]
		local body = avatar_obj(peer)
		if not peer_in_session(peer) then
			host.active[peer] = nil -- left the game
		elseif body and is_task(rt) and rt.check_level and rt.current_target ~= nil then
			local ok, err = true, nil
			if body.far then
				ok, err = qc.with_level_of(peer, qc.with_actor, fields, rt.check_level, rt, rt.current_target)
			elseif host.target_elsewhere(rt.current_target) then
				ok, err = qc.with_actor(fields, rt.check_level, rt, rt.current_target)
			end
			if not ok then report("guide of #" .. tostring(peer), err) end
		end
	end
end

function host.patch_guides()
	local mod = rawget(_G, "task_objects") or task_objects
	local cls = mod and mod.CGeneralTask
	local orig = cls and cls.remove_guider_spot
	if type(orig) ~= "function" then return end
	local guide_wanted = host.guide_wanted
	cls.remove_guider_spot = function(self, ...)
		if world_active() and guide_wanted() then return end
		return orig(self, ...)
	end
end

local function patch_shared_vars()
	local orig = rawget(_G, "save_var")
	if type(orig) ~= "function" then
		log("! save_var not found: shared task vars written on a client stay local")
		return
	end
	_G.save_var = function(obj, k, v)
		if client_live() and is_shared_key(k) and is_my_actor(obj) then
			local ok, err = pcall(client_route_var, k, v)
			if not ok then report("shared var " .. tostring(k), err) end
		end
		if is_my_actor(obj) then host.var_own(k, v) end -- round 4: the values this process writes itself
		return orig(obj, k, v)
	end
end

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Update, events, start
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- S5 (A-S5T): the server's parts of these that were here - a world hurt by a give that died (heal_lost_gives), a map server's
-- effects sent up again until the world server answers, the world server's coop_rep_map / coop_rep_map_ack - are coop_srv_tasks'.
host.next_tick = 0

local function actor_on_update()
	if not api then return end
	local t = now()
	if t < host.next_tick then return end
	host.next_tick = t + 250
	if world_active() and next(host.fines) ~= nil then flush_fines() end
	if world_active() then
		if not has_clients() then
			-- nobody to send to: host_scan does not run, the audiences of tasks that ended go here
			local aud = task_audience()
			local tm = aud and aud.prune and tmgr()
			if tm and type(tm.task_info) == "table" then aud.prune(tm.task_info) end
			return
		end
		if t >= host.next_scan then
			host.next_scan = t + SCAN_MS
			host_scan(false)
			host.guides()
			host.talk_watch()
		end
		if t >= host.next_list then
			host.next_list = t + LIST_MS
			host_list(-1)
		end
	elseif client_live() then
		client_tick()
	end
end

-- level.add_call runs every frame of the level. Stock actor_binder:update returns while the actor is dead, before
-- task_manager:update and before the actor_on_update callback: the host's revive delay, longer for a wipe, would stop the
-- group's tasks, their mirror and every client's turn-in (the stub falls back to open after PENDING_MS). A live actor's
-- binder does all of this itself.
function host.actor_dead()
	local a = db and db.actor
	if not a then return false end
	local ok, alive = pcall(a.alive, a)
	return ok and alive == false
end

local function dead_tick()
	if not (api and active() and host.actor_dead()) then return false end
	local t = now()
	if world_active() and t >= host.next_dead_update then
		host.next_dead_update = t + DEAD_UPDATE_MS
		local tm = tmgr()
		if tm then
			local ok, err = pcall(tm.update, tm)
			if not ok then report("task update while dead", err) end
		end
	end
	local ok, err = pcall(actor_on_update) -- the host runs a unique call without a guard
	if not ok then report("tick while dead", err) end
	return false
end

local function actor_on_reinit()
	if type(AddUniqueCall) == "function" then AddUniqueCall(dead_tick) end
end

local function guarded(what, f)
	return function(...)
		local ok, err = pcall(f, ...)
		if not ok then report(what, err) end
	end
end

local function register_events()
	local cm = rawget(_G, "coop_main") or coop_main
	if not (cm and cm.add_event_handler) then
		log("! coop_main.add_event_handler not found: task events are not handled")
		return
	end
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_REQ, guarded("task request", host_on_request))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_SYNC, guarded("task sync", function(_, from)
		if world_active() and type(from) == "number" and from ~= 0 then
			-- split levels: a character the tasks of now have not judged yet (a late joiner) is judged once, here
			local aud = task_audience()
			local gained = from < 0x100 and aud and aud.judge_new and aud.judge_new(character_of(from)) == true
			host_full_sync(from)
			if gained and type(api.story_resend_tasks) == "function" then pcall(api.story_resend_tasks, from) end
			local rg = reward_group()
			local id = rg and rg.id_of(from)
			if id then host.char_of[from] = id end
			local e = id and rg.take(id)
			if e then send_reward(from, { k = "away", m = e.m, c = e.c, x = e.x, i = rg.items_text(e.i) }) end
			host_resend_effects(from)
			send_reward(from, { k = "lang", l = game.translate_string("general_new_task") })
		end
	end))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_STATE, guarded("task state", function(payload, from)
		if from == 0 and mirrors_tasks() then client_apply_state(payload) end
	end))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_LIST, guarded("task list", function(payload, from)
		if from == 0 and mirrors_tasks() then client_on_list(payload) end
	end))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_REWARD, guarded("task reward", client_on_reward))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_NEWS, guarded("task news", client_on_news))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_VAR, guarded("shared var", host_on_var))
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_ACK, guarded("effect answer", host_on_effect_ack))
	-- (a map server's personal effects, coop_rep_map / coop_rep_map_ack: coop_srv_tasks, S5)
	cm.add_event_handler(EV_VARS, guarded("shared vars", function(payload, from)
		if from == 0 and mirrors_tasks() then client_apply_shared(payload) end
	end))
end

-- Host: effects nobody answered yet, in the save: a restart of the host must not lose what was already paid for.
function save_effects(m_data)
	if mirrors_tasks() then m_data.coop_task_fx_done = cl.fx_done; return end
	local wait
	for key, list in pairs(host.fx_wait) do
		if #list > 0 then
			wait = wait or {}
			wait[key] = list
		end
	end
	m_data.coop_task_fx = { seq = host.fx_seq, wait = wait, characters = host.char_of,
		takers = host.taker, taker_char = host.taker_char, participants = host.participants, rep_party = host.rep_party,
		failure_participants = host.failure_participants, map_seen = host.map_seen, fines = host.fines }
end

function load_effects(m_data)
	if mirrors_tasks() then cl.fx_done = m_data.coop_task_fx_done or {}; return end
	local saved = m_data.coop_task_fx
	host.fx_seq = saved and saved.seq or 0
	host.fx_wait = saved and saved.wait or {}
	host.char_of = saved and saved.characters or {}
	host.taker = saved and saved.takers or {}
	host.taker_char = saved and saved.taker_char or {}
	host.participants = saved and saved.participants or {}
	host.rep_party = saved and saved.rep_party or {}
	host.failure_participants = saved and saved.failure_participants or {}
	host.map_seen = saved and saved.map_seen or {}
	host.fines = saved and saved.fines or {}
	host.esc_own, host.esc_ready = {}, false -- round 7: the escort keys of this save are taken as the host's at the first look
	m_data.coop_task_fx = nil
end

function print_status()
	local role = not api and "no engine API" or world_active() and "host" or mirrors_tasks() and "client" or "off"
	local n_stub, n_real = 0, 0
	local tm = tmgr()
	if tm and type(tm.task_info) == "table" then
		for _, tsk in pairs(tm.task_info) do
			if stub_data(tsk) then n_stub = n_stub + 1 else n_real = n_real + 1 end
		end
	end
	log("role %s, tasks: %d script, %d mirrored | requests out %d in %d refused %d | states out %d in %d, lists %d, syncs %d",
		role, n_real, n_stub, stats.req_out, stats.req_in, stats.refused, stats.state_out, stats.state_in, stats.lists, stats.syncs)
	log("rewards routed %d received %d, share %s | group items: moved %d released %d, stages %d | errors %d",
		stats.rewards_routed, stats.rewards_in, tostring(reward_mode()), stats.party_moves, stats.party_releases,
		stats.stage_by_party, stats.errors)
	log("task lines: sent %d, received %d, own engine lines dropped %d, limited %d", stats.news_out, stats.news_in,
		stats.news_swallowed, stats.news_limited)
	log("task_auto_end [%s]: %d, refused %d (ends of tasks a player did not take that his own stock logic sent: DRX tasks at a "
		.. "faction change, the base defense at a level change; no line each)", host.trust_mode("task_auto_end"), stats.auto_end,
		stats.auto_end_refused)
	if world_active() then
		for id, peer in pairs(host.taker) do
			if peer ~= 0 and tm and tm.task_info and tm.task_info[id] then log("  '%s' taken by #%s", id, tostring(peer)) end
		end
	end
	-- the rest of the quests group (offers, group items, story, PDA)
	local qc = rawget(_G, "coop_quests_core")
	if type(qc) == "table" and type(qc.print_status) == "function" then
		local ok, err = pcall(qc.print_status)
		if not ok then report("quests status", err) end
	end
end

function on_game_start()
	if not api then return end
	local md = _G.coop_economy_mdata
	if md and md.register_player_key then md.register_player_key("coop_task_fx_done", function() return cl.fx_done end) end
	if not host.patched then
		host.patched = true
		local steps = {
			{ "task_manager", patch_task_manager },
			{ "task news", patch_task_news },
			{ "rewards", patch_rewards },
			{ "statistics", patch_statistics },
			{ "stash lines", patch_stash_line },
			{ "guide markers", host.patch_guides },
			{ "group items", patch_party_items },
			{ "shared vars", patch_shared_vars },
			{ "events", register_events },
		}
		for _, s in ipairs(steps) do
			local ok, err = pcall(s[2])
			if not ok then report("install " .. s[1], err) end
		end
		if api.party_has == nil then
			pcall(function()
				api.party_has = party_has
				api.party_count = party_count
			end)
		end
	end
	RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_update", actor_on_update)
	RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_reinit", actor_on_reinit)
	RegisterScriptCallback("save_state", save_effects)
	RegisterScriptCallback("load_state", load_effects)
	RegisterScriptCallback("actor_on_info_callback", _client_on_info)
	-- round 5 (S4 of the round 4 review): the NPC of this player's talk, for a request a moment after it ended (_talk_partner)
	RegisterScriptCallback("GUI_on_show", function(name)
		if name == "Dialog" and client_live() then pcall(_talk_partner) end
	end)
	RegisterScriptCallback("GUI_on_hide", function(name)
		if name == "Dialog" and cl.partner then cl.partner.at = now() end
	end)
	-- Parity audit D10: this machine dropped events (a long stall): one of them may be a task's, ask for the whole list
	RegisterScriptCallback("coop_events_lost", function()
		if client_live() then client_request_sync() end
	end)
	-- The host's move: this player stayed in his world, the world server's Lua is new: who he is, what task he has on is told again
	RegisterScriptCallback("coop_world_back", function()
		if client_live() then
			cl.active = nil
			client_request_sync()
		end
	end)
end
